\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 First Thing: Grief and anger in Israel after death of six hostages\b0\par\par\uc2 Vivian Ho \par \uc2 1,499 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 September 2024\par 12:42 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 General strike follows tens of thousands taking to the streets in protest against the government\u8217\'20\'19s handling of the war in Gaza. Plus: fears of overtourism in NorwayDon\u8217\'20\'19t already get First Thing in your inbox? Sign up here\par \par \uc2 Good morning.\par \par \uc2 Over the weekend, Israel {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/sep/01/family-confirms-death-of-hostage-hersh-goldberg-polin-after-idf-finds-bodies-in-gaza"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 confirmed the deaths of six more hostages}}}\uc2  taken in the 7 October attack by \uc2 Hamas\uc2 , with the Israeli military saying they were killed by their captors shortly before their bodies were found in a tunnel complex under Gaza.\par \par \uc2 The findings about how the six died did little to deflect widespread fury towards \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  and his rightwing coalition for failing to agree a US-backed hostages-for-peace deal with \uc2 Hamas\uc2 . Tens of thousands of Israelis {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/sep/01/protests-israel-strike-eruption-outrage-gaza-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 took to the streets on Sunday night}}}\uc2 , chanting, \u8220\'20\'1CBibi [Netanyahu\u8217\'20\'19s nickname], you\u8217\'20\'19re killing the hostages.\u8221\'20\'1D On Monday, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/sep/02/israel-gaza-war-national-strike-hostages-ceasefire-netanyahu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first nationwide general strike }}}\uc2  in Israel since the 7 October attacks began, bringing large parts of the economy to a halt. As they did the night before, protesters have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/sep/02/israel-gaza-war-live-israel-faces-nationwide-general-strike-amid-public-anger-over-hostage-deaths-and-failed-ceasefire-talks?page=with:block-66d558538f0871b94295d424#block-66d558538f0871b94295d424"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 begun blocking streets}}}\uc2  in their call for a ceasefire deal to bring home the remaining hostages.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Who is on strike in Israel? Municipalities including Tel Aviv, Givatayim, Herzliya, Ra\u8217\'20\'19anana, Kfar Saba and Hod Hasharon are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/sep/02/israel-gaza-war-live-israel-faces-nationwide-general-strike-amid-public-anger-over-hostage-deaths-and-failed-ceasefire-talks?page=with:block-66d53ead8f08eed33c642353#block-66d53ead8f08eed33c642353"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  taking part, }}}\uc2  while others including Netanya and Sderot are holding solidarity strikes of several hours. All big banks are reportedly taking part, while hospitals are running at weekend capacity. Pre-schools are striking while some schools closed late morning. Ben Gurion airport closed between 8am and 10am, while in Tel Aviv the light rail came to a halt as did Haifa\u8217\'20\'19s underground Carmelit railway. Major bus companies Egged, Dan and Metropolin are also taking part.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Do the families of the hostages support the strike and the protests? Yes. \u8220\'20\'1CWe call on the public to prepare to bring the country to a standstill,\u8221\'20\'1D said the Hostage and Missing Families Forum. \u8220\'20\'1CThese six individuals were taken alive, endured the horrors of captivity, and were then coldly murdered \u8230\'20\'26 A deal for the return of the hostages has been on the table for over two months. Were it not for the delays, sabotage and excuses those whose deaths we learned about this morning would likely still be alive.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/sep/01/who-six-israeli-hostages-bodies-found-gaza-hamas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Who were the six hostages}}}\uc2  ? Hersh Goldberg-Polin, 23; Eden Yerushalmi, 24; Carmel Gat, 40; Alexander Lobanov, 33; Almog Sarusi, 27 and Ori Danino, 25.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 How has Netanyahu responded to the\par \par \uc2 ir deaths? While \uc2 Hamas\uc2  has blamed Israel and the US because Israel had not agreed to a ceasefire deal, Netanyahu blamed the Islamist militant group for blocking an agreement. While it is too early to tell, the anger over the deaths could {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/sep/01/hostage-deaths-pressure-netanyahu-agree-gaza-ceasefire"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reinvigorate the protest movement }}}\uc2  in Israel calling for a ceasefire and hostage release deal, as well as calls for new elections aimed at toppling Netanyahu\u8217\'20\'19s rightwing government.\par \par \uc2 Far-right party in Germany poised for state election victory\par \par \uc2 The electorate in two closely watched elections in the former communist east made clear their dissatisfaction with Germany\u8217\'20\'19s mainstream political parties, putting {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/sep/01/german-far-right-party-afd-state-election-victory-thuringia"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the far-right Alternative f\u252\'00\'FCr Deutschland (AfD) party in the top spot}}}\uc2  in Thuringia, with 32.8% of the vote, and second place in Saxony, with 30.6%. The preliminary results have prompted the German chancellor, \uc2 Olaf Scholz\uc2 , to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/sep/02/germany-state-elections-afd-europe-latest-politics-news?page=with:block-66d5658d8f0871b94295d480#block-66d5658d8f0871b94295d480"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 urge mainstream parties to exclude \u8220\'20\'1Crightwing extremists\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur country cannot and must not get used to this. The AfD is damaging Germany. It is weakening the economy, dividing society and ruining our country\u8217\'20\'19s reputation,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 What was the AfD\u8217\'20\'19s response? While the 11-year-old AfD clinched its first mayoral and district government posts last year, it has never joined a state government. \uc2 Alice Weidel\uc2 , the AfD\u8217\'20\'19s co-leader, said: \u8220\'20\'1CIt is a historic success for us. It is the first time we have become the strongest force in a state election. It is a requiem for this coalition [in Berlin].\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In other news \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 North Korean table tennis players have reportedly been placed under \u8220\'20\'1Cideological scrutiny\u8221\'20\'1D and could face punishment for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/sep/02/north-korean-table-tennis-selfie-paris-olympics-south-korea-punishment"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 taking part in a selfie on the Olympic podium}}}\uc2  with South Korean players.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Russia\par \par \uc2 bombarded Ukraine\u8217\'20\'19s capital\par \par \uc2 , Kyiv, with missiles early on Monday, sparking fires and damaging homes and infrastructure while {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/sep/02/russia-ukraine-war-live-kyiv-vladimir-putin-volodymyr-zelenskiy-latest-news-updates?page=with:block-66d55a528f08eed33c6423c9#block-66d55a528f08eed33c6423c9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  injuring at least two people}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  shared posts from\par \par \uc2 Gold Star families\par \par \uc2 that prais\par \par \uc2 ed his visit to Arlington national cemetery, where two of his campaign aides {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/01/trump-gold-star-families-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 allegedly shoved a cemetery worker}}}\uc2  so they could film the former president laying a wreath.\par \par \uc2 Stat of the day: More than 10,000 US hotel workers go on strike\par \par \uc2 o\par \par \uc2 ver Labor Day weekend\par \par \uc2 On Sunday, more than 10,000 workers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/sep/01/hotel-workers-strike-labor-day-weekend"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 went on strike }}}\uc2  and walked off the job at 24 hotels in eight cities across the US, after contract talks with the establishments\u8217\'20\'19 owners collapsed. The \uc2 Unite Here\uc2  union, which represents workers in hotels, casinos and airports across the US and Canada, warned that the industrial action could escalate to other cities over holiday weekend that was expected to be the busiest on Labor Day records.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe hotel industry has rebounded from the pandemic, and room rates are at record highs,\u8221\'20\'1D Gwen Mills, the union\u8217\'20\'19s international president, said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CBut hotel workers can\u8217\'20\'19t afford to live in the cities that they welcome guests to. Too many hotel workers have to work two or sometimes three jobs in order to make ends meet.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe won\u8217\'20\'19t accept a \u8216\'20\'18new normal\u8217\'20\'19 where hotel companies profit by cutting their offerings to guests and abandoning their commitments to workers.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Don\u8217\'20\'19t miss this: The new focus of China\u8217\'20\'19s internet police\par \par \uc2 In recent months, followers of influential liberal bloggers have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/sep/02/how-chinas-internet-police-went-from-targeting-bloggers-to-their-followers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 been getting called in for questioning by the police in China}}}\uc2 , where the internet is tightly regulated. It has reached a point that Li Ying, who runs a popular Chinese-language X account, had to post an \u8220\'20\'1Curgent notice\u8221\'20\'1D that urged people to unfollow him because his followers in China were being called in to \u8220\'20\'1Cdrink tea\u8221\'20\'1D with the police, a euphemism for interrogations. Instead of targeting the bloggers themselves, it appears the Chinese authorities are now going after their private followers \u8211\'20\'13 sign of the growing severity of China\u8217\'20\'19s censorship regime.\par \par \uc2 \u8230\'20\'26 or this: The 20th anniversary of Def Jam: Fight for NY\par \par \uc2 Twenty years ago this month, EA Games released Def Jam: Fight for NY, a video game featuring some of the music industry\u8217\'20\'19s biggest rappers fighting it out on the streets of New York. To {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/games/article/2024/sep/02/def-jam-fight-for-ny-at-20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 commemorate the anniversary of its release}}}\uc2 , the creators look back on the making of a game that still dominates social media conversation, despite never being remade or rereleased.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think you could make this game today,\u8221\'20\'1D said Daryl Anselmo, a former EA employee and the game\u8217\'20\'19s art director. \u8220\'20\'1CThe climate is too hostile. But we only ever intended Def Jam: Fight for NY to be a fantasy, escapist experience. It was like the gangsta rap version of The Warriors. It was just a bit of fun; we trusted the audience knew it wasn\u8217\'20\'19t cool to throw someone out of a window in real life! We really tried to respect the culture of hip-hop.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Climate check: The right to roam in Norway\par \par \uc2 In Norway, friluftslivet (outdoor life) is seen as foundational to the mountainous country\u8217\'20\'19s culture. Allemannsretten \u8211\'20\'13 which gives Norwegians the legal right to camp, swim, ski and walk freely in nature, regardless of who the landowner is \u8211\'20\'13 is the basis of friluftslivet. However, environmentalists are now warning that opening up the country\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cright to roam\u8221\'20\'1D laws to mass tourism {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/sep/02/norway-outdoors-tourism-campaign-environmental-fears-right-to-roam"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 could lead to environmental destruction}}}\uc2 , especially as interest in the the Nordic has risen among tourists seeking cooler destinations amid high temperatures in Europe.\par \par \uc2 Last Thing: A whale of a tale\par \par \uc2 The beluga whale rumored to be a Russian spy has died. Nicknamed Hvaldimir, a combination of the Norwegian word for whale, hval, and the first name of the Russian president, \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , the beluga was found {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/sep/01/beluga-whale-hvaldimir-found-dead-norway"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 floating in the Risavika Bay in southern Norway}}}\uc2  on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 Hvaldimir was first spotted in April 2019 near the northern island of Ing\u248\'00\'F8ya, not far from Russian waters, wearing a harness and what appeared to be a mount for a small camera and a buckle marked with the words \u8220\'20\'1CEquipment St Petersburg\u8221\'20\'1D. His getup sparked allegations that he was a \u8220\'20\'1Cspy whale\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 the Russian navy has been known to have trained whales for military purposes, experts said. After rescuers removed his harness, the amiable beluga became a local celebrity, clearly enjoying interacting with people and at one point retrieving a woman\u8217\'20\'19s iPhone after she dropped it in the water.\par \par \uc2 Sign up\par \par \uc2 First Thing is delivered to thousands of inboxes every weekday. If you\u8217\'20\'19re not already signed up, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/info/2018/sep/17/guardian-us-morning-briefing-sign-up-to-stay-informed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 subscribe now}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Get in touch\par \par \uc2 If you have any questions or comments about any of our newsletters please email {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:newsletters@theguardian.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 newsletters@theguardian.com}}}\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240902ek92001pb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
