\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Nashville \uc2 Uber\uc2  and \uc2 Lyft\uc2  drivers warn of \u8216\'20\'18ruined vacations\u8217\'20\'19 as they vote to strike\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 562 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 August 2024\par 13:52 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Recently formed Tennessee Drivers Union to take action at city airport as wave of Labor Day tourists is expected\par \par \uc2 Hundreds of ride - share drivers for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/uber"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Uber}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/lyft"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lyft}}}\uc2  in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/nashville"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Nashville}}}\uc2 , Tennessee, have voted to begin a strike on Friday 30 August at Nashville international airport, warning of \u8220\'20\'1Cruined vacations\u8221\'20\'1D as the city prepares for a wave of tourists celebrating the Labor Day holiday weekend.\par \par \uc2 The recently formed Tennessee Drivers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-unions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Union}}}\uc2  is taking action to raise awareness of their demands for improvements to their pay and working conditions.\par \par \uc2 The strike at the airport will be followed by a caravan of ride-share drivers through Nashville\u8217\'20\'19s Lower Broadway entertainment district, a tourism hotspot. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/tennessee"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tennessee}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tn.gov/tourism/news/2024/7/23/tennessee-tourism-breaks-30b-in-visitor-spending-in-2023-creating-a-record-tax-benefit-for-tennesseans.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recorded}}}\uc2  a record $30.6bn in tourism spending in 2023.\par \par \uc2 The workers are pushing for improved compensation amid allegations that \uc2 Uber\uc2  and \uc2 Lyft\uc2  can take upwards of 60 to 80% of a ride fare. They are also calling for expanded access to bathrooms at the Nashville airport, limits on the use of scooters at night, a cap on the number of ride-share drivers permitted on the road and a ban on out-of-state drivers due to delays drivers can face in securing fares.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMost of the drivers in the Tennessee Drivers Union (TDU) work 12-hour days every day of the week doing rideshare. They depend on rideshare to be able to make a living, and \uc2 Uber\uc2  and \uc2 Lyft\uc2  provide their sole income,\u8221\'20\'1D the Tennessee Drivers Union said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CThe drivers refuse to continue to let huge companies like \uc2 Uber\uc2  and \uc2 Lyft\uc2  profit off of its labor. They want Nashville to hear their struggle. This strike will be the first of more ruined vacations for Nashville tourists. Unless and until their demands are met, Tennessee and its tourists can expect further disruptions.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A driver for \uc2 Uber\uc2  and \uc2 Lyft\uc2  in Nashville for six years who requested to remain anonymous for fear of retaliation said that he and other drivers organized together due to the poor conditions and treatment that he claims have been worsening since he began driving, with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.forbes.com/sites/lensherman/2023/01/16/ubers-new-math-increase-prices-and-squeeze-driver-pay/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fares increasing}}}\uc2  yet driver pay decreasing.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe drivers are doing everything. The gas comes out of the drivers\u8217\'20\'19 pay, the repairs of the car because it is a personal car, so if they\u8217\'20\'19re giving the driver just 45% of the fare, that leaves everybody struggling,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CIn one hour, I can drive from the airport to downtown or downtown to the airport and get $8 to $10, and then a different hour I can get $17. We need the pay to be consistent.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He noted drivers can face long delays in waiting for fares. He also claimed ride-share drivers are unfairly treated in being issued tickets without warnings and not being provided adequate bathrooms at the airport.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s why we came together,\u8221\'20\'1D the driver added. \u8220\'20\'1CWith the current economic situation, it is really difficult to meet family needs or what you need to survive. We\u8217\'20\'19re trying to fight for our rights. We also don\u8217\'20\'19t want passengers to be overcharged by \uc2 Uber\uc2 . When they take over 50 or 60% of the ride fare, they are counting on us getting tips from riders, but the way we are struggling we understand people are struggling, so not everyone tips.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240830ek8u001mh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
