\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 Unions in higher education are surging, new report reveals\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 352 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 August 2024\par 13:07 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 An estimated 38% of graduate student employees are now in unions as \u8216\'20\'18unionization becomes a tactic for change\u8217\'20\'19\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-unions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Unionization}}}\uc2  has been surging in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/education/higher-education"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 higher education}}}\uc2 , according to a new comprehensive report that reveals a 133% increase among graduate student employees in the US since 2012.\par \par \uc2 An estimated 38% of graduate student employees are now unionized, with more than 150,000 workers in 81 bargaining units as of January 2024.\par \par \uc2 The extraordinary increase was highlighted by the first comprehensive study on unionization in higher education since 2012, by the National Center for the Study of Collective Bargaining in Higher Education and the Professions at Hunter College.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe growth of non-tenure track faculty, postdocs, academic researchers, graduate and undergraduate students shows how unionization is becoming a tactic of choice for change,\u8221\'20\'1D said Adrianna Kezar, professor and director of the Pullias Center for Higher Education at the \uc2 University of Southern California\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Unionized faculty members in higher education also grew by 7.5%, with a total of 402,217 unionized faculty members at over 600 institutions across 30 states and Washington DC. California, New York and New Jersey have the highest number of unionized faculty members.\par \par \uc2 In 2020, the first postdoctoral scholar union was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.chemistryworld.com/news/the-first-ever-postdoc-union-at-a-private-us-university-has-been-formed/4012413.article"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 formed}}}\uc2  at a private university, \uc2 Columbia University\uc2 . According to the report, as of this year, there are 10 bargaining units of exclusively postdoctoral scholars , with a total of 11,471 employees and two academic research units with a total of 6,132 employees in the US.\par \par \uc2 In 2016, the first undergraduate student employee union in the US was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://uniontrack.com/blog/student-workers-forming-unions#:~:text=In%202016%2C%20the%20first%20undergraduate,by%20presidents%20with%20the%20NLRB."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 formed}}}\uc2  at \uc2 Grinnell College\uc2  in Iowa. There are currently 19 exclusive undergraduate student employee units, with 3,515 represented employees.\par \par \uc2 The report comes as union density in the US has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2024/03/12/majorities-of-adults-see-decline-of-union-membership-as-bad-for-the-us-and-working-people/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rapidly declined}}}\uc2  in recent decades, from 20.1% of US workers in 1983 to 10% in 2023. Labor advocates have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/publication/union-membership-data/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pointed}}}\uc2  to obstacles to union organizing efforts and outdated US labor laws as driving factors for the decline, which comes despite {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/Gallup/status/1828793176754409957"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 majority support}}}\uc2  among Americans for labor unions, according to polling.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240829ek8t001e1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
FF
