\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Is \u8216\'20\'18No tax on tips\u8217\'20\'19 a distraction from the fight to end sub-minimum wages?\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 1,549 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 August 2024\par 21:41 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Trump and Harris have vowed to ban taxes on tips. Critics say it\u8217\'20\'19s not a solution for service workers\u8217\'20\'19 unlivable wagesUS politics \u8211\'20\'13 live updates\par \par \uc2 Tipping has always been a controversial subject in the US. Imported from Europe and popularized by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.povertylaw.org/article/the-racist-history-behind-americas-tipping-culture/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 some accounts}}}\uc2  after the fall of slavery to reinforce racial wage disparities, the practice comes freighted with historic baggage.\par \par \uc2 Nor is it overly popular with consumers. Since the pandemic, 72% of US adults say tipping is expected in more places today than it was in 2019, according to a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/2023/11/09/how-americans-see-recent-developments-in-tipping/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pew survey}}}\uc2 . Four in 10 Americans oppose the suggested tips that have been popping up on payment screens everywhere from coffee shops and dry cleaners to self-service machines in airports.\par \par \uc2 That hasn\u8217\'20\'19t stopped {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/donaldtrump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Donald Trump}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  from putting tips at the center of their election battle. Earlier this month, in a bold move, the vice-president {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.npr.org/2024/08/11/nx-s1-5071144/no-tax-on-tips-campaigns-trump-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 endorsed}}}\uc2  a policy that the former president touted earlier this year to ban taxes on tips for service workers, as both candidates have been vying for working-class voters in the 2024 election, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/22/harris-no-tax-on-tips-nevada-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 especially}}}\uc2  in the swing state of Nevada.\par \par \uc2 At a glance, the idea of giving a break to tipped workers is attractive \u8211\'20\'13 in some states the minimum wage for tipped workers is just $2.13 an hour and an alarming 14.8% of those workers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/blog/seven-facts-about-tipped-workers-and-the-tipped-minimum-wage/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 live in poverty}}}\uc2 . But the idea throws up many issues. Why should a low-wage worker who gets tips be treated differently to one who doesn\u8217\'20\'19t? Will higher-paid workers be able to use the measure to cut their tax bills? Harris says not, Trump is less clear.\par \par \uc2 But for some critics the \u8220\'20\'1Cno tax on tips\u8221\'20\'1D proposal is most worrisome because the debate detracts from the fight to eliminate sub-minimum wages and support policies that would raise wages.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe policy of sub-minimum wage is a way of institutionalizing low wages,\u8221\'20\'1D said the Rev Dr William J Barber II, president of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.poorpeoplescampaign.org/about/our-demands/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Repairers of the Breach }}}\uc2  and the founding director of the Center for Public Theology and Public Policy at Yale Divinity School. \u8220\'20\'1CWhat happens is the people forced to work those jobs that we call essential end up being economically rejected and treated like they\u8217\'20\'19re expendable.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Barber explained that although both Harris and Trump have endorsed the policy of ending taxes on tips, there are stark differences between the candidates on economics and that poverty is a systemic issue that needs {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.poorpeoplescampaign.org/about/our-demands/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 broad policy solutions }}}\uc2  rather than just one concession such as eliminating taxes on tips.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C[Trump] can say it all he wants. He had four years to do it and he didn\u8217\'20\'19t do it. But what he did do was give greedy people a $2tn tip through tax cuts,\u8221\'20\'1D said Barber. \u8220\'20\'1CWhen Harris {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/KamalaHarris/videos/we-choose-freedom/457114333973063/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 launched}}}\uc2  her campaign she said: I want to see a world where no child lives in poverty.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Without having earnings floors in place... workers are vulnerable to exploitation and inequality in the labor market\par \par \uc2 Lena Simet, senior researcher at \uc2 Human Rights Watch\par \par \uc2 Harris is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/business/2024/08/20/kamala-harris-taxes-on-tips/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 now considering}}}\uc2  a $75,000 annual income cap on her tips policy and prohibiting tax on tips only for service and hospitality workers. Her plan would also exempt the payroll tax, which funds social security and Medicare, and tie the no-tax-on-tips policy to an increase to the sub-minimum wage for tipped workers.\par \par \uc2 Lena Simet, a senior researcher and advocate on poverty and inequality at \uc2 Human Rights Watch\uc2 , authored a 2022 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hrw.org/news/2022/10/27/ending-us-subminimum-tipped-wages-can-reduce-poverty-and-inequality"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  on the impacts that eliminating the sub-minimum wage would have on reducing poverty and inequality. It noted that although employers are supposed to compensate workers when tips don\u8217\'20\'19t make up the difference between the sub-minimum wage and minimum wage, they often ignore this mandate.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think there\u8217\'20\'19s often a misperception that workers in service industries, tipped workers, are receiving wages far above the minimum wage or living wages due to the tips that they receive. So there\u8217\'20\'19s this idea that they\u8217\'20\'19re doing quite well, while in reality, of course, there are some workers who see very generous tips, but it\u8217\'20\'19s not the majority of workers,\u8221\'20\'1D said Simet. \u8220\'20\'1CWithout having these earnings floors in place, the minimum wage floor and calling for an increase, workers are vulnerable to exploitation and inequality in the labor market which is harmful overall for the economy.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt doesn\u8217\'20\'19t mean that workers can no longer be tipped. It just means a tip comes on top of a wage floor that would guarantee them a minimum,\u8221\'20\'1D added Simet. \u8220\'20\'1CWe see many countries\u8217\'20\'19 alternatives for wage floors \u8211\'20\'13 where this reliance of workers on tips is really not practiced \u8211\'20\'13 and that it\u8217\'20\'19s, in fact, a win for workers. It\u8217\'20\'19s also a win for customers and for consumer protection purposes. The main point is really to make employers aware of their responsibilities of providing workers with decent wages, and not allow for these huge fluctuations where workers simply don\u8217\'20\'19t know how much they\u8217\'20\'19re going to make on a given day.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Culinary Union in Nevada, has endorsed the tip tax proposal in conjunction with raising the minimum wage. The union, which represents 60,000 workers in Las Vegas and Reno, Nevada, has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://m.culinaryunion226.org/news/press/statement-endorsement-of-kamala-harris-for-president-and-tim-walz-for-vice-president"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 endorsed}}}\uc2  Harris for president.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is outrageous that over a million workers in this country are not guaranteed a fair minimum wage in 2024. Employers across the nation need to take responsibility for paying a real minimum wage and Congress must ensure it,\u8221\'20\'1D said Ted Pappageorge, the union\u8217\'20\'19s secretary-treasurer. \u8220\'20\'1CSeven states - Alaska, California, Minnesota, Montana, Nevada, Oregon and Washington - have banned the sub-minimum wage for tipped workers, ensuring that these workers receive the same minimum wage as non-tipped employees.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Nevada is a key swing state for the presidential election, and \uc2 Jacky Rosen\uc2 , the state\u8217\'20\'19s Democratic senator, is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/08/15/us/politics/jacky-rosen-nevada-senate.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 seeking }}}\uc2  to re-win her seat this year. Both she and her Republican opponent have supported the no-tax-on-tips proposals. According to recent polls, Trump still has a two-point lead over Harris in Nevada, but that gap has dwindled from a nine-point lead over Biden in May.\par \par \uc2 Al Horsford, a Democratic state representative, and the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/Culinary226/status/1825550810924650556"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Culinary Union}}}\uc2  have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nevadacurrent.com/2024/08/12/horsford-if-you-like-no-tax-on-tips-you-should-love-banning-subminimum-wages-for-tipped-workers/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 supported }}}\uc2  ending the sub-minimum wage. Horsford told the Nevada Current he plans on filing legislation with colleagues on the issue. Bernie Sanders and 29 other US Democratic senators have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sanders.senate.gov/press-releases/news-sanders-scott-29-democratic-senators-introduce-legislation-to-raise-the-minimum-wage-to-17-by-2028-benefitting-nearly-28-million-workers-across-america/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sponsored}}}\uc2  legislation to phase out the sub-minimum wage, while Republicans have historically opposed similar efforts.\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://static1.squarespace.com/static/6374f6bf33b7675afa750d48/t/669eb5ca5ed20a4a6492a00e/1721677260484/OFW_ShortChanged.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  published by One Fair Wage in July 2024 noted \u8220\'20\'1Cending income taxes on tips will not make sub minimum wages livable\u8221\'20\'1D. The report {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://static1.squarespace.com/static/6374f6bf33b7675afa750d48/t/669eb5ca5ed20a4a6492a00e/1721677260484/OFW_ShortChanged.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cited}}}\uc2  the policy proposal\u8217\'20\'19s benefits are limited given 66% of tipped restaurant workers do not receive high enough income to pay federal income taxes currently on their wages.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy hope is that the sudden new intention and desire to pander to tipped workers results in everybody supporting what workers are actually demanding and winning, which is a full livable wage,\u8221\'20\'1D said Saru Jayaraman, president of One Fair Wage and director of the food labor research center at \uc2 University of California Berkeley\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CWhat workers really need and want is an actual livable wage with tips on top.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 One Fair Wage and others have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hrw.org/news/2022/10/27/ending-us-subminimum-tipped-wages-can-reduce-poverty-and-inequality"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 published research}}}\uc2  demonstrating that states and localities that have ended sub-minimum wage have workers who receive higher overall earnings, are less likely to face poverty and face less harassment on the job.\par \par \uc2 The proclivity of tipping in the US has origins {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/magazine/story/2019/07/17/william-barber-tipping-racist-past-227361/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stemming}}}\uc2  from slavery. After the American civil war, employers exploited tipping as a way to avoid paying former slaves the wages their white colleagues would have received. Industry has consistently fought to maintain the wage gap for tipped workers, and when the first federal minimum wage was mandated in 1938, tipped workers were excluded.\par \par \uc2 It took several decades, until 1966, for a sub-minimum wage for tipped workers to be federally enacted.\par \par \uc2 While the federal minimum wage of $7.25 an hour has remain unchanged since 2009, the sub-minimum wage for tipped workers has remained $2.13 an hour {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://static1.squarespace.com/static/6374f6bf33b7675afa750d48/t/669eb5ca5ed20a4a6492a00e/1721677260484/OFW_ShortChanged.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 since 1991}}}\uc2 , when Republican activist and then head of the \uc2 National Restaurant Association\uc2 , Herman Cain, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/magazine/story/2019/07/17/william-barber-tipping-racist-past-227361/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 offered}}}\uc2  legislators a compromise to avoid lobbying against a federal minimum wage increase as long as the tipped sub-minimum wage remained stagnant.\par \par \uc2 Industry groups have continued fighting against efforts to raise the minimum wage and ban sub-minimum wages for tipped workers, including an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/OneFairWageNY/videos/john-oliver-calls-out-saveourtips-astroturf-campaign/232617294115287/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 astroturfed }}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/OneFairWageNY/videos/john-oliver-calls-out-saveourtips-astroturf-campaign/232617294115287/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 save our tips\u8221\'20\'1D campaign}}}\uc2  launched during the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/trump-administration"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump administration}}}\uc2  to oppose efforts at state levels, arguing the policies would result in decreased pay for workers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19ve been making the same argument for 90 years, since 1938 when they passed the first federal minimum wage as part of the New Deal,\u8221\'20\'1D added Jayaraman. \u8220\'20\'1CA full minimum wage with tips on top has resulted in the seven states already enacting this doing much better on every measure. Those states have higher restaurant sales per capita, higher small business growth rates per capita, higher overall restaurant industry job growth rate, higher tipping averages, one half the rate of sexual harassment in the industry.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240827ek8r0018h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
