\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Bernie Sanders stresses healthcare and ending \u8216\'20\'18horrific\u8217\'20\'19 Gaza war in speech\b0\par\par\uc2 Joan E Greve in Chicago \par \uc2 699 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 August 2024\par 14:48 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Senator also pushed for raising minimum wage and reducing higher education cost in DNC address\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/bernie-sanders"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bernie Sanders}}}\uc2  detailed an extensive progressive agenda that Democrats must enact if {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  is elected president as he addressed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.google.com/search?q=democratic+national+convention+site%3Atheguardian.com&oq=democr&gs_lcrp=EgZjaHJvbWUqBggAEEUYOzIGCAAQRRg7MgYIARBFGDsyDQgCEAAYgwEYsQMYgAQyDQgDEAAYgwEYsQMYgAQyBggEEEUYOTIGCAUQRRg8MgYIBhBFGDwyBggHEEUYPNIBCDI3NDJqMGo3qAIAsAIA&sourceid=chrome&ie=UTF-8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the party\u8217\'20\'19s nominating convention}}}\uc2  in Chicago on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The Vermont senator mentioned Harris\u8217\'20\'19s name only a handful of times and instead focused his forceful speech on the need to expand healthcare access, reduce the cost of higher education and raise the minimum wage.\par \par \uc2 As he seeks re-election to a fourth Senate term this November, Sanders insisted that Democrats could come together to make meaningful change, as they did in the early days of the coronavirus pandemic with the passage of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/mar/10/covid-us-house-biden-coronavirus-relief-stimulus"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 American Rescue Plan}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI say all of this not to relive that difficult moment, but to make one simple point. When the political will is there, government can effectively deliver for the people of our country,\u8221\'20\'1D Sanders said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe need to summon that will again \u8211\'20\'13 because too many of our fellow Americans are struggling every day to just get by.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Sanders\u8217\'20\'19 speech sounded much like his typical remarks at a rally, as he invoked the language of his two unsuccessful presidential campaigns. He implored his fellow lawmakers to \u8220\'20\'1Cget big money out of our political process\u8221\'20\'1D, \u8220\'20\'1Cguarantee healthcare to all as a human right\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Ctake on big pharma\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 While applauding {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/joebiden"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden}}}\uc2  and his administration for having accomplished \u8220\'20\'1Cmore than any government since FDR\u8221\'20\'1D, Sanders made it clear that he considers the work unfinished.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMuch more remains to be done,\u8221\'20\'1D Sanders said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe must have the courage to stand up to wealth and power and deliver justice for people at home and abroad.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Sanders\u8217\'20\'19 focus on policy rather than the new Democratic nominee was notable given his staunch support of Biden in the weeks after the president\u8217\'20\'19s devastating debate performance last month. While more Democrats were calling on the president to step aside, Sanders penned a New York Times {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/07/13/opinion/joe-biden-president.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 op-ed}}}\uc2  arguing Biden was \u8220\'20\'1Cthe strongest candidate to defeat Mr Trump\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Despite those concerns, Sanders has commended Harris in recent weeks, as she has ridden a wave of enthusiasm to quickly consolidate Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 support. In an interview on Monday, Sanders described Harris as \u8220\'20\'1Ca very strong candidate\u8221\'20\'1D while urging Democrats against potential complacency in the election. In that interview, Sanders attacked Trump as the \u8220\'20\'1Cmost dangerous candidate\u8221\'20\'1D in US history, a warning that he has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/13/end-of-democracy-bernie-sanders-on-if-trump-wins-and-how-to-stop-him"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 repeated}}}\uc2  throughout this election season.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, Sanders contrasted his vision of economic populism with the policies included in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/project-2025"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Project 2025}}}\uc2 , a rightwing manifesto that has become a punching bag for Democrats.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLet\u8217\'20\'19s be clear: this is not a radical agenda,\u8221\'20\'1D Sanders said of his proposals. \u8220\'20\'1CGiving more tax breaks to billionaires. Putting forth budgets to cut social security, Medicare, and Medicaid. Letting polluters destroy our planet. That is what is radical.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Sanders received a warm welcome from the convention crowd, but the senator received the most robust applause toward the end of his speech, when he addressed the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/video/2024/aug/20/bernie-sanders-democratic-national-convention"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 war in Gaza}}}\uc2 . Sanders has become one of the most vocal critics of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/benjamin-netanyahu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu}}}\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s government in Congress, and he has chastised Biden over his response to the war.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAbroad, we must end this horrific war in Gaza, bring home the hostages, and demand an immediate ceasefire,\u8221\'20\'1D Sanders said, prompting loud cheers from the crowd.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/aug/19/pro-palestinian-protest-democratic-convention"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pro-Palestinian protesters}}}\uc2  have held a series of demonstrations across Chicago this week to bring more attention to Biden\u8217\'20\'19s handling of the war and demand a new approach from Harris. Progressives are hopeful that Harris will set a new tone on Israel, and she will have a chance to specify her views on the war when she addresses the convention on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 As progressives wait to hear more details on Harris\u8217\'20\'19 platform, Sanders made it clear on Monday that he was ready to work to get her to the White House.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COn November 5, let us elect \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  as our president,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CAnd let us go forward to create the nation we know we can become.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240821ek8l000b6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
