\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Harley-Davidson\uc2  drops DEI initiatives amid pressure from \u8216\'20\'18anti-woke\u8217\'20\'19 activists\b0\par\par\uc2 Edward Helmore \par \uc2 627 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 August 2024\par 19:42 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Milwaukee-based company no longer has minority-owned supplier goals and plans to exit socially motivated training\par \par \uc2 Motorcycle maker \uc2 Harley-Davidson\uc2  has become the latest manufacturer to drop {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2023/dec/16/diversity-dei-us-companies-backlash"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 diversity, equity and inclusion}}}\uc2  initiatives amid sustained pressure from anti-DEI activist Robby Starbuck.\par \par \uc2 In a statement Monday, the Milwaukee-based company said it has not operated a corporate DEI function since April, no longer has minority-owned supplier goals and plans to exit socially motivated training for employees.\par \par \uc2 Harley-Davidson\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s statement, posted on X, said that it sees \u8220\'20\'1Cevery leader\u8217\'20\'19s role to ensure we have an employee base that reflects our customers and the geographies in which we operate\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 and the company would limit training to legal requirements.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are saddened by the negativity on social media over the last few weeks, designed to divide the \uc2 Harley-Davidson\uc2  community,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/harleydavidson/status/1825564138032234994"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the statement said}}}\uc2 . \u8220\'20\'1CAs a company, we take this issue very seriously, and it is our responsibility to respond with clarity, action and facts.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The company said in the statement that it will also reorganize employee resource groups to focus on business development, mentoring and training. Having a \u8220\'20\'1Cbroad customer base is good for business\u8221\'20\'1D, it added.\par \par \uc2 Harley-Davidson\uc2  has been in the cross-hairs of anti-DEI activists who earlier this summer won similar concessions from retailer \uc2 Tractor Supply\uc2  and farming equipment maker \uc2 John Deere & Co.\uc2  The tractor maker said in a statement in July it would {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2024-07-16/deere-backs-down-from-diversity-initiatives-after-online-attacks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 no longer participate}}}\uc2  in \u8220\'20\'1Ccultural awareness parades\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The motorcycle maker said in an email to staff that it began a review of its \u8220\'20\'1Cstakeholder and outreach activities\u8221\'20\'1D earlier this year. \uc2 Harley-Davidson\uc2  had been under attack from anti-DEI activist Starbuck, who accused it of adopting \u8220\'20\'1Cthe woke agenda of the very far left\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 More broadly, the issue of DEI has become a political lightning rod that reflects US political divisions, with American businesses anticipating an even broader roll-back of such initiatives if \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  wins a second presidency in November.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s time to get rid of these policies and bring back a sense of neutrality and sanity in corporate America,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2024-08-19/harley-drops-diversity-initiatives-maligned-by-anti-dei-activist?sref=fqqmZ8gi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Starbuck said in an interview with Bloomberg}}}\uc2 , pointing to activism on social media by \uc2 Harley-Davidson\uc2  influencers for the company\u8217\'20\'19s move. He reportedly added: \u8220\'20\'1CWe kind of reached critical mass.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Harley-Davidson\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s shares are up 5% since Starbuck started his campaign in July, according to the outlet.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this year, a Washington Post-Ipsos poll found 61% of adults think DEI programs in the workplace are \u8220\'20\'1Ca good thing\u8221\'20\'1D. But another {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/648269/americans-business-stay-quiet-public-policy.aspx?utm_source=newsletter&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=newsletter_axiosam&stream=top"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 survey}}}\uc2  from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/quote/78145MF:US"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bentley University}}}\uc2  and Gallop found that fewer than four in 10 US adults (38%) believe businesses should take public stances, a decline of 10% since 2022.\par \par \uc2 Harley-Davidson\uc2  became a focus of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attention in 2018 after it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2018/jun/26/trump-threatens-harley-davidson-tariff-big-tax"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 responded to his administration\u8217\'20\'19s tariffs}}}\uc2  by moving some production overseas. The former president subsequently encouraged people to boycott the company.\par \par \uc2 The company has also grappled with falling demand from younger buyers for its old-school touring bikes \u8211\'20\'13 or \u8220\'20\'1Chogs\u8221\'20\'1D \u8211\'20\'13 according to one analyst who has said \u8220\'20\'1Can experience for them is not about hitting the open road\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Harley-Davidson\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decision to drop DEI training received pushback on Tuesday from Eric Bloem, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hrc.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Human Rights Campaign}}}\uc2  president, who criticized the company\u8217\'20\'19s decision as \u8220\'20\'1Cimpulsive\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWith nearly 30% of gen Z identifying as LGBTQ+ and the community wielding $1.4tn in spending power, retreating from these principles undermines both consumer trust and employee success,\u8221\'20\'1D {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.hrc.org/press-releases/hrc-statement-on-harley-davidsons-retreat-from-values-of-diversity-equity-and-inclusion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bloem said in a statement}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 There had been a national shift in favor of DEI initiatives after the 2020 murder of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/george-floyd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 George Floyd}}}\uc2 , who was Black, by a white police officer in Minneapolis.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240820ek8k002s3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
