\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 SkyWest Airlines\uc2  facing federal lawsuit over alleged \u8216\'20\'18fake company union\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 1,389 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 August 2024\par 14:23 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Largest regional airline in North America also sued by flight attendant union for alleged retaliatory firings\par \par \uc2 SkyWest Airlines\uc2 , the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.skywest.com/about-skywest-airlines/facts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 largest regional airline}}}\uc2  in North America, is facing legal action over an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.afacwa.org/afa_sues_skywest_illegal_termination_fake_company_union"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 alleged}}}\uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cfake\u8221\'20\'1D company union that the airline operates and the allegedly retaliatory firings of flight attendants who were engaged in union organizing efforts.\par \par \uc2 A lawsuit was filed by the \uc2 Association of Flight Attendants\uc2  (\uc2 AFA\uc2 -\uc2 CWA\uc2 ) in October 2023. The \uc2 US Department of Labor\uc2  also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.naacpldf.org/contact-us/legal-assistance/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed}}}\uc2  a lawsuit last month against the SkyWest Inflight Association over the \u8220\'20\'1Ccompany union\u8221\'20\'1D, alleging SkyWest Inflight Association (\uc2 SIA\uc2 ) did not perform its legal duties as a representative agency and barred two employees from running in an election for leadership positions due to their support for an independent union at the airline.\par \par \uc2 The legal battles come as the conservative presidential plan for Trump\u8217\'20\'19s second term, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.documentcloud.org/documents/24088042-project-2025s-mandate-for-leadership-the-conservative-promise"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Project 2025}}}\uc2 , has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.salon.com/2024/07/31/its-designed-to-eliminate-unions-project-2025-lays-out-the-plan-to-undermine-organized-labor/#:~:text=Former%20President%20Donald%20Trump's%20first,rules%20meant%20to%20keep%20unions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called}}}\uc2  for enacting labor law reforms to permit employers to create non-union employee involvement organizations that are run jointly by management. The National Labor Relations Act {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.salon.com/2024/07/31/its-designed-to-eliminate-unions-project-2025-lays-out-the-plan-to-undermine-organized-labor/#:~:text=Former%20President%20Donald%20Trump's%20first,rules%20meant%20to%20keep%20unions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 currently}}}\uc2  makes it an unfair labor practice for employers \u8220\'20\'1Cto dominate or interfere with the formation or administration of any labor organization or contribute financial or other support to it\u8221\'20\'1D.The Railway Labor Act, which governs airline employees, has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://assets.nationbuilder.com/afacwa/pages/3329/attachments/original/1697057943/2-23-cv-00723.pdf?1697057943"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 similar}}}\uc2  language.\par \par \uc2 SkyWest Airlines\uc2 , which operates through partnerships with \uc2 United Airlines\uc2 , \uc2 Delta Air Lines\uc2 , \uc2 American Airlines\uc2  and \uc2 Alaska Airlines\uc2 , is accused of financially supporting and controlling the \uc2 SIA\uc2  and a handbook for \uc2 SIA\uc2  representatives states the airline supports and funds the organization.\par \par \uc2 In an interview with the Guardian, a former president of the SkyWest Inflight Association from October 2020 to October 2021, said he believed the company funded and controlled the union and improperly administered elections. The \uc2 AFA\uc2  requested he go by his first name only, Romero, as he was required to sign a non-disclosure agreement.\par \par \uc2 Romero also alleged he experienced racial discrimination and was pushed to resign.\par \par \uc2 Romero explained he was elected president of \uc2 SIA\uc2  in the wake of the Black Lives Matter protests around the US in 2020 as corporations were making efforts to appear sympathetic to diversity, equity and inclusion issues.\par \par \uc2 He said when he first assumed the role, he was excited to enact needed changes but immediately noticed issues and the lack of separation between management and the group and that leadership roles in the group had been a stepping stone to management positions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe site is supposed to be the separation of the labor union organization and management, but there\u8217\'20\'19s just so many things that just crossover,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 He explained that he would submit expense reports to Skywest to directly pay the SkyWest Inflight Association staff and add to their work schedules to get paid for activities related to the \uc2 SIA\uc2 : \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s how we would get our money, that is how the organization is paid for by the company, the same company that is supposed to be separate,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 He also alleged all public statements and messages from \uc2 SIA\uc2  went through \uc2 SkyWest\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s communications department to review and approve them.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s such a conflict of interest even from the point of they were implementing things for union busting tactics, we would be brought into meetings and we were able to see what domiciles (airports where staff were based) had union activity going on,\u8221\'20\'1D he continued.\par \par \uc2 Romero said when he was first elected, board members would criticize him and alleged one claimed he had a criminal record because they found someone with a similar name, who they didn\u8217\'20\'19t know, had one. He alleged the vice-president had a close relationship with management and consistently undermined him to discuss policies and changes.\par \par \uc2 He also claimed the \uc2 SIA\uc2  elections were never properly administered, such as mail notices not being sent out to employees ahead of elections and flaws with their voting system \u8211\'20\'13 allegations made in the Department of Labor\u8217\'20\'19s lawsuit.\par \par \uc2 In September 2021, days after Romero said he sent the \uc2 SIA\uc2  vice-president a cease and desist letter for continuing to meet and speak with management over changes and issues that he believes he should have been included in, he was informed by the vice-president that a recall election by the board was going to be held to remove him.\par \par \uc2 Then Romero said racist text messages were anonymously leaked about his removal as president. Other flight attendants started a Justice for Romero campaign and a third-party investigation into the texts was started by the SkyWest Inflight Association. Although he never saw any investigative report, Romero said he didn\u8217\'20\'19t hold any trust in it because they seemed to focus on trying to find out who leaked the messages rather than who wrote it.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey were trying to figure out who the whistleblower was compared to who the alleged perpetrator was and that pissed me off,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CThey said it was not conclusive.\u8221\'20\'1D He was moved to special projects from working as a flight attendant during the investigation and has since left the company.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI feel like they really just thought I was going to be somebody that\u8217\'20\'19s going to be a yes man,\u8221\'20\'1D concluded Romero. \u8220\'20\'1CThere is utterly no separation between management and the labor union, from the pay to the voter operating system. Flight attendants deserve to be able to have the opportunity to choose its representative labor organization.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The October 2023 lawsuit filed by AFA-CWA is still in the discovery process and the union recently filed an amended complaint to include new allegations that \uc2 SkyWest Airlines\uc2  managers have surveilled union organizing activities of flight attendants.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe \uc2 DOL\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s lawsuit again makes clear the SkyWest Inflight Association is an illegal company union operating at the behest of management and not for Flight Attendants it claims to represent,\u8221\'20\'1D said AFA-CWA in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1CAs we have seen, \uc2 SkyWest\uc2  management will do whatever they can \u8211\'20\'13 including firing long-time workers \u8211\'20\'13 to intimidate and attempt to control Flight Attendants. SkyWest Flight Attendants are organizing to form a true union with the \uc2 Association of Flight Attendants-CWA\uc2  under the Railway Labor Act. SkyWest Flight Attendants want these legal rights at work, a real voice at their airline, protection as aviation\u8217\'20\'19s first responders, and the ability to collectively bargain at the nation\u8217\'20\'19s largest regional airline.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 SkyWest Airlines\uc2  did not answer questions relating to Romero\u8217\'20\'19s allegations about the SkyWest Inflight Association or about the allegations of discrimination he says he experienced. Commenting in response to the lawsuit filed by the \uc2 AFA\uc2 , a spokesperson said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe \uc2 Association of Flight Attendants\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 (\uc2 AFA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s) lawsuit is baseless and without merit, and we are confident the courts will agree when the facts are recognized. \uc2 SkyWest\uc2  has a legally binding collective bargaining agreement with \uc2 SIA\uc2  as recognized by federal courts, the Department of Labor and in accordance with the Railway Labor Act. The bottom line is that \uc2 SkyWest Airlines\uc2  and \uc2 SIA\uc2  are separate organizations whose collaboration has gained \uc2 SkyWest\uc2  flight attendants the best overall pay and benefits in the regional airline industry.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The current president of SkyWest Inflight Association, Brent Coates, said in a statement: \u8220\'20\'1CWe value the time and effort of each of our leaders, past and present, and have absolutely no tolerance for racism or discrimination of any kind.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe opinions of a former \uc2 SIA\uc2  official \u8211\'20\'13 who was on \uc2 SIA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Board for less than a year (some years ago) and left office long before their term would have expired \u8211\'20\'13 is a poor measure of \uc2 SIA\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s impact and success in negotiating what is clearly the best contract in the regional industry.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWith respect to both lawsuits, \uc2 SIA\uc2  is confident in our positions. In the \uc2 AFA\uc2  suit, we have already filed counterclaims alleging violations of the rights of \uc2 SIA\uc2  and the SkyWest Flight Attendants under several federal and state laws. We look forward to responding to both lawsuits in court. \uc2 SIA\uc2  remains focused on providing the highest level of professional representation by listening to and actively advocating for SkyWest Flight Attendants.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 This story was amended on 14 August 2024 to correct that the \uc2 US Department of Labor\uc2  filed a lawsuit against SkyWest Airlines Inflight Association, not \uc2 SkyWest Airlines\uc2  itself. It also clarified that the Railway Labor Act, not the National Labor Relations Act, governs airline employees.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240814ek8e001bc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
