\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Middle East crisis: US accelerates military deployment to region amid reports Iran may attack within days \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Sammy Gecsoyler \par \uc2 3,409 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 August 2024\par 14:06 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 US defence secretary \uc2 Lloyd Austin\uc2  orders USS Abraham Lincoln strike group to quicken transit to Middle East and deploys guided missile submarine, says PentagonSee all our Middle East crisis coverage\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 This blog is now closing. Thank you for following along. Below is a roundup of today\u8217\'20\'19s stories:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The UK, France and Germany have said there must be \u8220\'20\'1Cno further delay\u8221\'20\'1D in agreeing to a ceasefire in Gaza and called on Iran and its allies to refrain from attacks against {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/israel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Israel}}}\uc2  that would further escalate tensions. In a joint statement released on Monday, they endorsed the latest push by the US, Qatar and Egypt to broker an agreement to end the 10-month-old war.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Gaza officials told AFP on Monday that they had identified 75 bodies of Palestinians killed in a weekend strike by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/israel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Israel}}}\uc2  on a school building where rescuers reported at least 93 dead. The Israeli military claimed that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/aug/10/israel-strikes-on-gaza-school-site-kills-almost-100-palestinian-officials-say"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Saturday\u8217\'20\'19s pre-dawn strike on the Al-Tabieen religious school}}}\uc2  compound in Gaza City killed at least 19 Palestinian militants who were allegedly using it as a base.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 US defence secretary \uc2 Lloyd Austin\uc2  ordered the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/aug/12/us-military-strike-group-jets-submarine-middle-east-iran-attack-israel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deployment of a guided missile submarine}}}\uc2  to the Middle East amid escalating tensions in the region, the Pentagon said on Sunday. The moves come as the US and other allies push for Israel and \uc2 Hamas\uc2  to reach a ceasefire deal that could help calm soaring regional tensions after the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/jul/31/hamas-leader-ismail-haniyeh-death-raid-iran-home-israel-gaza-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 assassination of Hamas political leader Ismail Haniyeh}}}\uc2  in Tehran, for which Iran has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/aug/05/iran-says-it-has-moral-duty-to-punish-israel-law-breaking-and-adventurism"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 vowed to retaliate}}}\uc2 , as well as a senior \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2  commander in Beirut.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Josep Borrell\uc2 , the \uc2 EU\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s top diplomat, has said the bloc should consider sanctions in response to calls by Israel\u8217\'20\'19s far-right national security minister to cut off aid to Gaza, calling them an \u8220\'20\'1Cincitement to war crimes\u8221\'20\'1D. Writing on the X platform late on Sunday, \uc2 EU\uc2  foreign policy chief Borrell said the recent remarks by Itamar Ben-Gvir constitute \u8220\'20\'1Cincitement to war crimes,\u8221\'20\'1D adding that \u8220\'20\'1Csanctions must be on our EU agenda.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 142 people have been killed and 150 others have been injured by Israeli strikes in Gaza in the past 48 hours, the Palestinian health ministry has said, as the overall death toll from the war nears 40,000. On Monday, the health ministry said 39,897 Palestinians have been killed and 92,152 have been injured in Israel\u8217\'20\'19s military offensive on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/gaza"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gaza}}}\uc2  since 7 October.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Israeli finance minister \uc2 Bezalel Smotrich\uc2  has responded to the \uc2 EU\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s foreign policy chief, \uc2 Josep Borrell\uc2 , who had referenced the far-right politician when calling for the consideration of sanctions against Israel on Sunday ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/aug/12/middle-east-crisis-live-us-israel-iran-gaza-hamas-lebanon-hezbollah?page=with:block-66b9d6c68f0875be70416761#block-66b9d6c68f0875be70416761"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 see post at 11.09BST}}}\uc2  ).\par \par \uc2 Writing on X, Smotrich accused Borrell of \u8220\'20\'1Csiding with terror\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 enltrBorrell, who doesn\u8217\'20\'19t stop misleading the public by claiming that the \uc2 IDF\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s retaliatory bombing in Gaza is worse than that of Nazi Germany, and who had the audacity to call the \uc2 IDF\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Operation Arnon aimed at rescuing the hostages a \u8220\'20\'1Cmassacre of the Palestinian people\u8221\'20\'1D has clearly\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/VWIiYd3EQT"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/VWIiYd3EQT}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 ????? ???????' (@bezalelsm) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/bezalelsm/status/1822958017567957114?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 August 12, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ryanair\uc2 , the low-cost Irish airline, is canceling all flights to and from Ben Gurion International Airport outside Tel Aviv from Tuesday until 26 August \u8220\'20\'1Cdue to operational restrictions which are beyond our control.\u8221\'20\'1D The airline did provide any further details.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.43pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Vatican has called on Iran to refrain \u8220\'20\'1Cin every way\u8221\'20\'1D from escalating a potential conflict in the Middle East after the assassination of \uc2 Ismail Haniyeh\uc2 , the political leader of \uc2 Hamas\uc2 , in Tehran last month.\par \par \uc2 The Israeli government has officially declined to comment on Haniyeh\u8217\'20\'19s death, but the strike was widely acknowledged as an Israeli operation both inside the country and beyond.\par \par \uc2 The Vatican secretary of state, Cardinal \uc2 Pietro Parolin\uc2 , appealed instead for Tehran to embrace dialogue, negotiation and peace, during a phone call Monday with Iran\u8217\'20\'19s new president, Masoud Pezeshkian.\par \par \uc2 Parolin spoke with Pezeshkian to congratulate him on the start of his mandate.\par \par \uc2 According to a Vatican statement, Parolin \u8220\'20\'1Cexpressed the Holy See\u8217\'20\'19s serious concern about what is happening in the Middle East, reiterating the need to avoid in any way the widening of the very serious conflict under way and preferring instead dialogue, negotiation and peace.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 75 bodies identified after Israeli strike on school building, Gaza officials say\par \par \uc2 Gaza officials told AFP on Monday that they had identified 75 bodies of Palestinians killed in a weekend strike by Israel on a school building where rescuers reported at least 93 dead.\par \par \uc2 The Israeli military said that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/aug/10/israel-strikes-on-gaza-school-site-kills-almost-100-palestinian-officials-say"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Saturday\u8217\'20\'19s pre-dawn strike on the Al-Tabieen religious school}}}\uc2  compound in Gaza City killed at least 19 Palestinian militants who were using it as a base.\par \par \uc2 AFP was unable to independently verify the toll.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere are 93 dead in the Al-Tabieen school strike, 75 of them have been identified,\u8221\'20\'1D Gaza civil defence agency spokesperson Mahmud Bassal told AFP. \u8220\'20\'1CThe others have not yet been identified because some bodies are torn and charred by the bombardment.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He said the dead included 11 children and six women.\par \par \uc2 Amjad Aliwa, an emergency doctor at Al-Ahli hospital in Gaza City, confirmed that 75 people killed in the strike had been identified.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere are still bodies (whose identities are unknown) that are completely destroyed,\u8221\'20\'1D he told AFP. \u8220\'20\'1CThere are also some families who have been displaced to the south (of the Gaza Strip) and cannot come to identify their loved ones.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Israeli news website Walla, citing the military, reported that 38 militants were killed in the strike.\par \par \uc2 Asked by AFP about the report, the Israeli military said that it would respond later.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.59pm BST\par \par \uc2 Reuters reports that Israel's air force has suspended travel abroad for its service personnel, a military spokesperson said.\par \par \uc2 The region is bracing for possible attacks against Israel by Iran and its allies after the killing of senior members of militant groups \uc2 Hamas\uc2  and \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Safety instructions from the military for the general public remained unchanged.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 A hospital in southern Gaza has received the bodies of 13 people, including a child, who were killed in Israeli strikes on Khan Younis, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 The strikes came as Israel has ordered mass evacuations from Gaza\u8217\'20\'19s second-largest city in recent days, claiming Palestinian militants are firing rockets from the area. Khan Younis suffered heavy destruction earlier this year during a major Israeli air and ground offensive.\par \par \uc2 An AP journalist counted the bodies at the nearby Nasser hospital and saw funeral prayers being held Monday morning.\par \par \uc2 The dead include a medic who was killed along with two others in a strike on his house, according to the hospital records.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.05pm BST\par \par \uc2 This footage from Gaza City shows the moment an Israeli airstrike hit a house in the suburb of Sheikh Radwan on Sunday. One person was killed and several others were wounded, according to Palestinian medics. According to Reuters, the cameraman who filmed the video said the Israeli army had notified people of a possible strike in the area.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.37am BST\par \par \uc2 142 Palestinians killed in Gaza in past 48 hours\par \par \uc2 142 people have been killed and 150 others have been injured by Israeli strikes in Gaza in the past 48 hours, the Palestinian health ministry has said, as the overall death toll from the war nears 40,000.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, the health ministry said 39,897 Palestinians have been killed and 92,152 have been injured in Israel\u8217\'20\'19s military offensive on Gaza since 7 October.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.09am BST\par \par \uc2 EU\uc2  should consider sanctions against after Israeli minister calls for aid cut off in Gaza, top diplomat says\par \par \uc2 Josep Borrell\uc2 , the \uc2 EU\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s top diplomat, has said the bloc should consider sanctions in response to calls by Israel\u8217\'20\'19s far-right national security minister to cut off aid to Gaza, calling them an \u8220\'20\'1Cincitement to war crimes\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Writing on the X platform late on Sunday, \uc2 EU\uc2  foreign policy chief Borrell said the recent remarks by Itamar Ben-Gvir constitute \u8220\'20\'1Cincitement to war crimes,\u8221\'20\'1D adding that \u8220\'20\'1Csanctions must be on our EU agenda.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In his own post on X and in media interviews, Ben-Gvir said that instead of agreeing to a potential ceasefire deal, Israel should block the entry of humanitarian aid and fuel to Gaza until \uc2 Hamas\uc2  releases all of the hostages, saying that doing so would bring the militant group to its knees.\par \par \uc2 Ben-Gvir has also repeatedly called for Israel to permanently reoccupy Gaza, rebuild Jewish settlements there and encourage the \u8220\'20\'1Cvoluntary\u8221\'20\'1D migration of Palestinians from the territory.\par \par \uc2 Ben-Gvir, a key member of prime minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s governing coalition, has threatened to bring the government down if it makes too many concessions in the ceasefire talks.\par \par \uc2 Borrell called on Israel\u8217\'20\'19s government to \u8220\'20\'1Cunequivocally distance itself from these incitements to commit war crimes,\u8221\'20\'1D and to engage \u8220\'20\'1Cin good faith\u8221\'20\'1D with ceasefire negotiations mediated by the US, Qatar and Egypt.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.28am BST\par \par \uc2 The overseers of the Geneva conventions, the core of international humanitarian law that seeks to protect civilians, detainees and wounded soldiers in war, have said they are being \u8220\'20\'1Cdisregarded\u8221\'20\'1D and have called on the world to recommit to the framework on its 75th anniversary.\par \par \uc2 The Geneva conventions, which have been adopted by nearly all the world\u8217\'20\'19s countries since they were finalised on 12 August 1949, are back on their heels as armed militia groups and national forces regularly disregard the rules of war.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CInternational humanitarian law is under strain, disregarded, undermined to justify violence,\u8221\'20\'1D president Mirjana Spoljaric of the \uc2 International Committee of the Red Cross\uc2 , which oversees the conventions, said on Monday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe world must recommit to this robust protective framework for armed conflict, one that follows the premise of protecting life instead of justifying death,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 The conventions, with roots dating to the 19th century, aims to set rules around the conduct of war: they ban torture and sexual violence, require humane treatment of detainees and mandate searches for missing persons.\par \par \uc2 The conventions \u8220\'20\'1Creflect a global consensus that all wars have limits,\u8221\'20\'1D Spoljaric told reporters at \uc2 ICRC\uc2  headquarters in Geneva. \u8220\'20\'1CThe dehumanization of both enemy fighters and civilian populations is a path to ruin and disaster.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Red Cross says the conventions are needed now more than ever: It has counted more than 120 active conflicts around the world, a six-fold increase from the half-century anniversary in 1999.\par \par \uc2 These days, many countries and combatants exploit loopholes in international humanitarian law or interpret it as they see fit. Hospitals, schools and ambulances have come under fire, aid workers and civilians are killed, and countries refuse access to detainees.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.09am BST\par \par \uc2 Iran has the \u8220\'20\'1Cright to an appropriate and deterrent response\u8221\'20\'1D against Israel to ensure regional stability, the country\u8217\'20\'19s acting foreign minister \uc2 Ali Bagheri Kani\uc2  told his Chinese counterpart on Monday, Reuters reports, citing state media.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.30am BST\par \par \uc2 Designated humanitarian zones in Khan Younis are shrinking, Al Jazeera reports, as Israel goes ahead with another military operation in the city.\par \par \uc2 On Saturday night, Israel expanded evacuation orders in Khan Younis, forcing tens of thousands of Palestinian residents and displaced families to leave in the dark as explosions from tank shelling reverberated around them.\par \par \uc2 Hani Mahmoud, reporting from the ground in Khan Younis for Al Jazeera, said:\par \par \uc2 Here, the ongoing mass evacuation is causing a great deal of difficult living conditions as people are pushed into a smaller area after the Israeli military cut off part of the humanitarian zone and included it in the red zone.\par \par \uc2 The Hamad residential complex, that is in the western part of Khan Younis, which used to be part of the humanitarian zones, was designated in the past months as an area for people to shelter in.\par \par \uc2 But not any more. This has shrunk the humanitarian zones in the western part of Khan Younis city and other areas, just causing further difficult living conditions in an area already overcrowded and running out of space.\par \par \uc2 People don\u8217\'20\'19t have basic necessities or basic supplies to cope and sustain their lives in these unusually difficult living conditions.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.51am BST\par \par \uc2 Air France\uc2  and its subsidiary \uc2 Transavia France\uc2  have again extended the suspension of their flights to Beirut, through Wednesday 15 August, because of continued tensions in the region, the Associated Press reports.\par \par \uc2 The flights have been suspended since 29 July because of the "security situation in Lebanon" and their resumption "will be subject to a new assessment of the situation on the ground", \uc2 Air France\uc2  said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 The airline said "the safety of its clients and crews are its absolute priority".\par \par \uc2 Clients with reservations for flights before 18 August can annul or modify their trips without cost.\par \par \uc2 Numerous international companies have ceased serving Beirut over fears of a military escalation between Israel and \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 However, \uc2 Air France\uc2  said it continues to operate its flights to Tel Aviv even though some international carriers, such as Italy\u8217\'20\'19s ITA, have suspended their flights until at least 15 August.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.13am BST\par \par \uc2 UK, France and Germany call for 'no further delay' to Gaza ceasefire\par \par \uc2 The UK, France and Germany have said there must be \u8220\'20\'1Cno further delay\u8221\'20\'1D in agreeing to a ceasefire in Gaza and called on Iran and its allies to refrain from attacks against Israel that would further escalate tensions.\par \par \uc2 In a joint statement released on Monday, they endorsed the latest push by the US, Qatar and Egypt to broker an agreement to end the 10-month-old war.\par \par \uc2 The mediators have spent months trying to get the sides to agree to a three-phase plan in which \uc2 Hamas\uc2  would release the remaining hostages in exchange for Palestinians imprisoned by Israel and Israel would withdraw from Gaza.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe agree that there can be no further delay. We have been working with all parties to prevent escalation and will spare no effort to reduce tensions and find a path to stability.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe fighting must end now, and all hostages still detained by \uc2 Hamas\uc2  must be released. The people of Gaza need urgent and unfettered delivery and distribution of aid.,\u8221\'20\'1D the statement said.\par \par \uc2 It was signed by French president Emmanuel Macron, German chancellor \uc2 Olaf Scholz\uc2  and British prime minister \uc2 Keir Starmer\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The statement also called on Iran and its allies to refrain from any retaliatory attacks that would further escalate regional tensions after the killing of two senior militants last month in Beirut and Tehran.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.33am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.29am BST\par \par \uc2 Opening summary\par \par \uc2 Hello and welcome to today's blog.\par \par \uc2 US defence secretary \uc2 Lloyd Austin\uc2  has ordered the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/aug/12/us-military-strike-group-jets-submarine-middle-east-iran-attack-israel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deployment of a guided missile submarine}}}\uc2  to the Middle East amid escalating tensions in the region, the Pentagon said on Sunday.\par \par \uc2 Austin also ordered the USS Abraham Lincoln strike group, equipped with F-35 fighters, to accelerate its deployment to the Middle East, the Pentagon said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 The moves come as the US and other allies push for Israel and \uc2 Hamas\uc2  to reach a ceasefire deal that could help calm soaring regional tensions after the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/jul/31/hamas-leader-ismail-haniyeh-death-raid-iran-home-israel-gaza-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 assassination of Hamas political leader Ismail Haniyeh}}}\uc2  in Tehran, for which Iran has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/aug/05/iran-says-it-has-moral-duty-to-punish-israel-law-breaking-and-adventurism"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 vowed to retaliate}}}\uc2 , as well as a senior \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2  commander in Beirut.\par \par \uc2 Israeli defence minister Yoav Gallant spoke on Sunday with Austin and told him Iran\u8217\'20\'19s military preparations suggested Iran was getting ready for a large-scale attack on Israel, Axios reporter \uc2 Barak Ravid\uc2  posted on X, citing a source.\par \par \uc2 Iran\u8217\'20\'19s official news agency said on Sunday that its elite Revolutionary Guards were holding a military drill in the country\u8217\'20\'19s west that would continue until Tuesday. The drills, which started on Friday, were ongoing in the province of Kermanshah, close to the border with Iraq, to \u8220\'20\'1Cenhance combat readiness and vigilance\u8221\'20\'1D, an armed forces official told IRNA.\par \par \uc2 In other developments:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Hamas\uc2  has urged Gaza mediators to implement a ceasefire plan presented by US president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  instead of holding more talks. International mediators had invited Israel and the Palestinian militant group to resume talks towards a long-sought truce and hostage-release deal, amid the growing fears of a wider regional conflict. Israel has accepted the invitation from the US, Qatar and Egypt for a round of talks planned for Thursday. However, \uc2 Hamas\uc2  said on Sunday it wanted the implementation of a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/may/31/biden-hamas-israel-gaza-ceasefire-plan"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 truce plan laid out by Biden}}}\uc2  on 31 May and later endorsed by the \uc2 UN\uc2  security council, \u8220\'20\'1Crather than going through more negotiation rounds or new proposals\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 An Israeli was killed and another wounded by Palestinian gunmen who opened fire on a main road in the occupied West Bank on Sunday, Israel\u8217\'20\'19s ambulance service and military said, with the armed wing of militant faction \uc2 Hamas\uc2  claiming responsibility. The Israeli military said it was pursuing the suspected assailants, blocking routes and conducting searches.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Later on Sunday, \uc2 Hamas\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 al-Qassam Brigades said its West Bank-based fighters killed an Israeli soldier at point-blank range in the Mehola settlement in the West Bank\u8217\'20\'19s Jordan Valley and \u8220\'20\'1Creturned to their bases safely\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Lebanon\u8217\'20\'19s Hezbollah\uc2  said an Israeli airstrike killed two of the group\u8217\'20\'19s fighters in Taybeh village on Sunday, with the health ministry reporting another death from an attack days ago. The Israeli military said it struck several \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2  military structures throughout Sunday. Separately, the health ministry said a Lebanese man who succumbed to injuries sustained in an Israeli strike \u8220\'20\'1Cseveral days ago\u8221\'20\'1D on the southern village of Beit Lif was a \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2  fighter, not a civilian as earlier reported. \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2  said that overnight into Monday it launched salvos of rockets \u8220\'20\'1Cin response\u8221\'20\'1D to the Israeli fire, targeting troops in northern Israel.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Thousands of people have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/aug/11/thousands-flee-khan-younis-israel-warns-offensive-gaza"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fled Khan Younis }}}\uc2  after the Israeli military warned of a new operation to flush out \uc2 Hamas\uc2  militants that it says have regrouped in the southern Gaza city. In al-Jala, a neighbourhood in the city\u8217\'20\'19s south that the Israel military had previously designated a humanitarian zone, residents on Sunday packed their belongings, uncertain where to seek refuge. Israel said rockets had been fired from the area. \uc2 Philippe Lazzarini\uc2 , head of the \uc2 UN agency for Palestinian refugees\uc2 , posted on X: \u8220\'20\'1CThe people of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/gaza"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gaza}}}\uc2  are trapped & have nowhere to go. Just in the past few days, more than 75,000 people have been displaced in southwest Gaza.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The US vice-president, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , said \u8220\'20\'1Cyet again far too many civilians\u8221\'20\'1D had been killed, after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/article/2024/aug/10/israel-strikes-on-gaza-school-site-kills-almost-100-palestinian-officials-say"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Israeli strikes on a school site}}}\uc2  in northern Gaza killed at least 80 people on Saturday. \u8220\'20\'1CI mean, Israel has a right to go after the terrorists that are \uc2 Hamas\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CBut as I have said many, many times, they also have, I believe, an important responsibility to avoid civilian casualties.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 European Union\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s chief diplomat, \uc2 Josep Borrell\uc2 , said there was \u8220\'20\'1Cno justification\u8221\'20\'1D for the attack on the Gaza City school, while the White House said it was \u8220\'20\'1Cdeeply concerned\u8221\'20\'1D about it. Egypt, Qatar and Saudi Arabia condemned the attack. A spokesperson for the \uc2 Palestinian Authority\uc2  president, \uc2 Mahmoud Abbas\uc2 , urged the US to \u8220\'20\'1Cput an end to the blind support that leads to the killing of thousands of innocent civilians, including children, women and the elderly\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Israeli military acknowledged Saturday\u8217\'20\'19s strike on the al-Tabeen school, claiming it hit a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/hamas"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hamas}}}\uc2  command centre within the school and that it had taken steps to reduce the risk of harming civilians. \uc2 Hamas\uc2  denied having a base at the school.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 An airstrike on a vehicle in eastern Syria near the porous border with Iraq killed at least five fighters from pro-Iran units, two security sources in the region told Reuters. One of the sources said the strike was carried out by a drone, but could not specify which military the drone belonged to. The second source said it targeted fighters as they changed shifts at a checkpoint, Reuters reported.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240812ek8c000xd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
