\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 Paramount Global\uc2  to cut 15% of its US workforce before \uc2 Skydance\uc2  merger\b0\par\par\uc2 Guardian staff and agencies \par \uc2 347 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 August 2024\par 10:41 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Company behind \uc2 Paramount Pictures\uc2 , Nickelodeon and CBS writes down value of its cable networks by nearly $6bn\par \par \uc2 The entertainment conglomerate behind {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/paramount-pictures"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Paramount Pictures}}}\uc2  is to cut about 2,000 jobs in a bid to reduce costs ahead of a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/film/article/2024/jul/08/paramount-merger-skydance-redstone-cbs-mtv-nickelodeon"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 merger with the independent film studio Skydance}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Paramount Global\uc2 , which also owns {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/media/cbs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 CBS}}}\uc2 , Nickelodeon and the UK\u8217\'20\'19s Channel 5, announced plans to cut about 15% of its US workforce alongside its latest earnings on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The company, which has been hit hard by the decline of cable TV, wrote down the value of its cable networks by nearly $6bn, even as the company\u8217\'20\'19s streaming business reported its first quarterly profit.\par \par \uc2 The impairment reflects a shrinking audience for cable TV networks such as Nickelodeon, \uc2 MTV\uc2  and \uc2 Comedy Central\uc2 , a decline that translates to lower advertising revenue. The announcement comes a day after \uc2 Warner Bros Discovery\uc2  took a $9bn write-down on its TV assets.\par \par \uc2 The pending merger with \uc2 Skydance Media\uc2  forced Paramount to reassess the value of each of its units to better reflect their worth to the company, resulting in the write-down. The magnitude of the reconciliation dragged Paramount into an operating loss of $5.3bn for the second quarter.\par \par \uc2 Absent this charge, the media company would have reported an adjusted operating income of $867m, or 54 cents a share, ahead of Wall Street\u8217\'20\'19s forecasts of per-share earnings of 12 cents, according to \uc2 LSEG\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The company\u8217\'20\'19s streaming business, which includes the Paramount+ subscription service and its free, ad-supported sibling, PlutoTV, posted its first quarterly profit, fueled by growth in subscription and ad revenue. The direct-to-consumer unit reported an operating income of $26m in the second quarter, compared with a loss of $424m a year ago.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are on track to reach domestic profitability for Paramount+ in 2025,\u8221\'20\'1D the Paramount co-CEOs, \uc2 George Cheeks\uc2 , \uc2 Chris McCarthy\uc2  and \uc2 Brian Robbins\uc2 , said in a joint statement.\par \par \uc2 Paramount stock rose 6% in extended trading.\par \par \uc2 Reuters contributed reporting\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240809ek89001e2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
