\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  boost union credentials in event at \uc2 UAW\uc2  local\b0\par\par\uc2 Alice Herman \par \uc2 618 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 August 2024\par 21:26 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Auto workers president hails Democratic presidential ticket and denounces Trump: \u8216\'20\'18the choice cannot be any clearer\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 At a union hall in the Detroit area on Thursday, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/kamala-harris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kamala Harris}}}\uc2  and her running mate, the Minnesota governor, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/tim-walz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tim Walz}}}\uc2 , addressed members of the \uc2 United Auto Workers (UAW)\uc2  at a campaign stop intended to play up the Democratic candidates\u8217\'20\'19 support for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-unions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unions}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 During the town hall-style event, which was held at the headquarters of \uc2 UAW\uc2  Local 900, Harris and Walz emphasized their support for organized labor and slammed \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for his anti-union record.\par \par \uc2 Members of Local 900 were among the first to go on strike last year, when 3,300 workers from a Wayne county plant producing pickup trucks and SUVs walked out on 15 September. During the strike, which ended with \uc2 UAW\uc2  ratifying contracts with Ford, \uc2 GM\uc2  and \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  that secured 25% wage increases and cost-of-living adjustments, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/26/biden-joins-uaw-strike-update-detroit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Joe Biden visited the picket line}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 becoming the first US president in history to do so.\par \par \uc2 Unions, which already overwhelmingly backed Harris, welcomed Walz \u8211\'20\'13 who signed a raft of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jun/07/minnesota-pro-worker-paid-leave-union"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 worker protections and pro-union bills}}}\uc2  into law in 2023 \u8211\'20\'13 on to the Democratic party ticket.\par \par \uc2 Sean Fain, the president of the union, introduced Harris and Walz, contrasting the candidates with Trump and JD Vance, who have attempted to court workers in recent months but whose policy records are notably anti-union.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou know, this is a \u8216\'20\'18which side are you on\u8217\'20\'19 moment, and the choice cannot be any clearer,\u8221\'20\'1D said Fain. Trump and Vance, Fain said, \u8220\'20\'1Cspent their lives serving themselves, representing the billionaire class and enriching themselves at the expense of the working class\u8221\'20\'1D. He shot back at Trump, who called the \uc2 UAW\uc2  president a \u8220\'20\'1Cstupid person\u8221\'20\'1D during a Fox News interview that aired this month.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  calls me stupid,\u8221\'20\'1D said Fain. \u8220\'20\'1CYou know why? Because he thinks auto workers are stupid. But we\u8217\'20\'19re not stupid. We don\u8217\'20\'19t fall for Trump\u8217\'20\'19s alternative facts, what we call lies.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 During their remarks, Walz and Harris spoke appreciatively of the \uc2 UAW\uc2 , drawing a sharp distinction between their position on labor and Trump\u8217\'20\'19s.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI couldn\u8217\'20\'19t be prouder to stand with \uc2 UAW\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D said Walz, who spoke about Trump\u8217\'20\'19s handling of the Covid-19 pandemic and his anti-union posture. Speaking about the rightwing presidential playbook, Project 2025, Walz said one of the goals was to \u8220\'20\'1Cget rid of labor unions and get rid of the voices they bring, so they can do whatever the hell they want\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 During Harris\u8217\'20\'19s speech, the vice-president referred to a political \u8220\'20\'1Cperversion\u8221\'20\'1D of the Republican party, \u8220\'20\'1Cwhere there\u8217\'20\'19s a suggestion that somehow strength is about making people feel small, making people feel alone, but isn\u8217\'20\'19t that the very opposite of what we know, unions know, to be strong? It\u8217\'20\'19s about the collective. It\u8217\'20\'19s about knowing that no one should ever be made to fight alone.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Since launching her campaign, Harris has turned to the ideas of freedom and individual liberties \u8211\'20\'13 concepts long associated with the rhetoric of the conservative movement \u8211\'20\'13 and turned them back on Trump and the modern Republican party. In Harris\u8217\'20\'19s campaign rallies so far, abortion rights, LGBTQ+ rights and, in this speech, labor rights form the basis of freedom.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEven if you\u8217\'20\'19re not a member of a union, you better thank unions. I\u8217\'20\'19m here to say thank you, thank you, thank you to the sisters and brothers of \uc2 UAW\uc2  for all you are and all we will do over these next 89 days,\u8221\'20\'1D said Harris, exiting to Beyonc\u233\'00\'E9\u8217\'20\'19s Freedom, now a Harris campaign anthem.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240808ek88003bj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
