\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 Warning signs of US recession may be bad news for \uc2 Kamala Harris\b0\par\par\uc2 Larry Elliott \par \uc2 724 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 August 2024\par 13:08 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Cracks in labour market provide Trump with evidence for his message that Biden has been disaster for the economyBusiness live \u8211\'20\'13 latest updates\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/news/2024/02/02/trump-and-his-allies-adjust-their-messaging-on-the-economy-as-it-steadily-improves-00139447"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 message}}}\uc2  to US voters has been consistent as he seeks to win a second term in the White House: the economy under \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has been a disaster.\par \par \uc2 Until recently the hard data has not supported Trump\u8217\'20\'19s argument. The US has been comfortably the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/new-atlanticist/seven-charts-that-will-define-the-g7-summit/#:~:text=US%20leads%20G7%20economies%20in%20economic%20rebound&text=But%20the%20bottom%20line%20is,growth%20as%20China%3A%205%20percent."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fastest-growing}}}\uc2  of the G7 leading industrial nations since the Covid pandemic. Unemployment has been low by historic standards. America\u8217\'20\'19s self-sufficiency in energy meant it suffered a less severe inflation shock than Europe after Russia\u8217\'20\'19s invasion of Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Yet the former US president now has some evidence to back up his case. The latest set of US jobs figures, released last week, showed the labour market {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/article/2024/aug/02/us-economy-jobs-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cooling fast}}}\uc2 . Payroll growth in July slowed to 114,000 \u8211\'20\'13 about half the average of 215,000 in the previous 12 months and well below economists\u8217\'20\'19 expectations. The unemployment rate rose from 4.1% to 4.3%.\par \par \uc2 That set alarm bells ringing. Financial markets have been betting heavily on the US economy being able to shrug off the impact of higher interest rates. The latest GDP figures \u8211\'20\'13 showing annual growth of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bea.gov/news/2024/gross-domestic-product-second-quarter-2024-advance-estimate#:~:text=Real%20gross%20domestic%20product%20(GDP,real%20GDP%20increased%201.4%20percent."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 close to 3%}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 supported that view.\par \par \uc2 But the cracks in the labour market prompted fears that the economy might now be heading for a hard landing. The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/article/2024/aug/05/japan-nikkei-index-225-asia-stock-markets-slump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 12% drop}}}\uc2  in Japan\u8217\'20\'19s Nikkei index was in large part driven by concerns that the world\u8217\'20\'19s biggest economy might be cooling fast.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  has a rule of thumb measure \u8211\'20\'13 known as the Sahm rule \u8211\'20\'13 for gauging whether the US economy is in recession. Named after the economist \uc2 Claudia Sahm\uc2 , this states that when the three-month moving average of the US unemployment rate is 0.5 percentage points or more above its low over the prior 12 months, the economy is in the early months of recession.\par \par \uc2 Last week\u8217\'20\'19s jobless report from the Bureau of Labour Statistics showed the Sahm rule was on the brink of being triggered. As the consultancy Capital Economics pointed out, the rule will be met next month unless the unemployment rate falls back.\par \par \uc2 Historically, the Sahm rule has been a good predictor of looming US recessions, and it has been quoted widely in recent days by those arguing that the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  has left it too long to cut interest rates. There has been speculation that, having fallen \u8220\'20\'1Cbehind the curve\u8221\'20\'1D, the Fed may not even wait until its next scheduled meeting next month, and may announce an emergency cut in the coming days.\par \par \uc2 Some economists warn against putting too much store by the Sahm rule. \uc2 Dhaval Joshi\uc2 , an analyst at \uc2 BCA Research\uc2 , said: \u8220\'20\'1CA decoupling between robust growth in the economy and steadily rising unemployment is unprecedented in our lifetimes. Through the past 60 years, whenever the US unemployment rate has increased by 0.5% in a year, taking it to the cusp of recession, GDP growth has also been on the cusp of recession. That is, until now.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Joshi said unemployment was rising not because of widespread layoffs but because labour supply had been increasing faster than labour demand. The stock market looked more vulnerable to a recession than the real economy. Tech stocks, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/article/2024/aug/03/why-big-seven-tech-companies-hit-ai-boom-doubts-shares"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in particular those exposed to the artificial intelligence boom}}}\uc2 , have been among the heaviest fallers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRight now, if we should fear a US recession, the question is: a recession in what? As in 2000-01, the biggest risk is a severe recession in the frothy parts of the stock market,\u8221\'20\'1D said Joshi.\par \par \uc2 But it is not just rising unemployment. There are other warning signs for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  as she seeks to fend off Trump\u8217\'20\'19s attacks on the current administration\u8217\'20\'19s economic record.\par \par \uc2 The performance of the delivery company UPS is often seen as a gauge of how well the US economy is doing. Last month it failed to meet analysts\u8217\'20\'19 estimates and pared back its growth forecasts for the rest of 2024.\par \par \uc2 With the presidential election only three months away, the economy is not about to plunge into immediate recession. But signs that households are reining in their spending is bad news for the Democrat presidential hopeful.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240805ek85001rx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
