\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 US chip factory workers say it\u8217\'20\'19s a \u8216\'20\'18struggle to survive\u8217\'20\'19 on their wages as industry booms\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 932 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 August 2024\par 11:22 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Companies stand to gain billions in federal funds and tax breaks as employees suffer in poor working conditions\par \par \uc2 As chip manufacturers grapple for billions of dollars in federal funds and tax breaks designed to boost the US semiconductor industry, they face growing calls from inside their factories to improve working conditions and pay.\par \par \uc2 Workers and labour unions are urging key companies in the sector to \u8220\'20\'1Cdo the right thing\u8221\'20\'1D and prioritize the wellbeing of employees over the wealth of their shareholders.\par \par \uc2 Dozens of employees at \uc2 Analog Devices Inc\uc2  (ADI), a chipmaker in Oregon, demanding living wages, paid shutdowns and safe working conditions as it vies for a slice of the $39bn in federal funds provided by the Chips and Science Act, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/statements-releases/2022/08/09/fact-sheet-chips-and-science-act-will-lower-costs-create-jobs-strengthen-supply-chains-and-counter-china/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed}}}\uc2  by Joe Biden in 2022.\par \par \uc2 In interviews with the Guardian, workers at ADI\u8217\'20\'19s Beaverton plant described a \u8220\'20\'1Creal struggle to survive\u8221\'20\'1D on their salaries while the industry booms. ADI did not respond to multiple requests for comment.\par \par \uc2 Companies across the sector have faced greater scrutiny of their labor practices. In January, \uc2 TSMC{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.manufacturingdive.com/news/tsmc-deal-arizona-labor-union-chip-factory/704890/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reached}}}\uc2  an agreement with local unions, while Micron {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cwa-union.org/news/releases/micron-chips-funding-commitment-respect-right-to-organize-union"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 agreed}}}\uc2  in April to meet with workers to discuss workers\u8217\'20\'19 rights at new chip plants and to work on a labor peace agreement.\par \par \uc2 At ADI, more than 100 workers have signed a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://adi-workers-united.solidarity.tech/adi-workers-demand-living-wages-paid-shutdowns-safe-working-conditions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 petition}}}\uc2  so far urging the company to increase pay, end mandatory shutdowns that places workers on furloughs and improve safety around hazardous chemicals.\par \par \uc2 Those behind the petition claimed they have even greater support, but said many workers fear retaliation for signing the petition. A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sierraclub.org/oregon/blog/2024/07/labor-community-organizations-stand-chip-workers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 coalition}}}\uc2  of environmental organizations and unions, including the \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2 , Sierra Club and Communications Workers of America, have publicly supported the effort.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs it stands to receive millions of public dollars, we expect ADI to do the right thing and guarantee that its workers have the benefits and protections they are demanding,\u8221\'20\'1D said Carl Kennebrew, president of the industrial division of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.iue-cwa.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Communications Workers of America, IUE-CWA}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 One operator at the ADI plant, Robbie Garecht, described working regularly with hydrofluoric acid. He has had to pour the chemical, which can immediately cause caustic burns upon contact with skin or tissue, into a funnel without a sensor to know when it\u8217\'20\'19s full and having to stand awkwardly to try to avoid spilling it. This has been a consistent issue plaguing workers at the plant, he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe definitely would all be safer if we had a specialized team that did these kinds of things and was well-trained or compensated for it,\u8221\'20\'1D said Garecht, \u8220\'20\'1Crather than whoever is assigned to it. Those chemicals are required elements you need to make semiconductors, so it\u8217\'20\'19s always going to be an inherently dangerous job. But it just seems they don\u8217\'20\'19t take that into account with how well they\u8217\'20\'19re going to compensate us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Workers are pushing for a $27 minimum wage at the semiconductor plant, which they say is the minimum required to live in the Beaverton area. They are currently paid around $21 an hour.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a real struggle to survive on what they pay us,\u8221\'20\'1D Garecht said. \u8220\'20\'1CEven when I found the cheapest studio apartment I could find in the area for me and my six year old, I still can not afford to sustain myself.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ips-dc.org/report-maximizing-the-benefits-of-the-chips-program/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  published by the Institute for Policy Studies in July called for greater measures to ensure federal funds are not used by corporations to further increase executive compensation and stock repurchases.\par \par \uc2 ADI paid $25.5m to their CEO \uc2 Vincent Roche\uc2  in total compensation in 2023, the report noted: 527 times the company\u8217\'20\'19s median worker pay. The company has also spent $9bn on stock buybacks since 2019 and has planned another $2bn in stock buybacks.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re essentially getting all this influx of funding, their stock is at an all time high and they\u8217\'20\'19re spending money on stock buybacks and expansions, and they\u8217\'20\'19re not dedicating funding towards the workers who are the whole reason they\u8217\'20\'19re making this money,\u8221\'20\'1D said Ben Coffey, another ADI worker in Beaverton. \u8220\'20\'1CMost people I work with are making some kind of compromise or sacrifice to be able to continue working there. I can\u8217\'20\'19t sustain myself without having a roommate, without watching my budget.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He criticized recent comments from \uc2 Tina Kotek\uc2 , the Oregon governor, who recently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apps.oregon.gov/oregon-newsroom/OR/GOV/Posts/Post/governor-kotek-announces-additional-finalized-oregon-chips-contracts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  millions of dollars in state funding for chip manufacturers including \uc2 Analog Devices\uc2 . One state senator was quoted as saying the investment would help create more \u8220\'20\'1Cfamily-wage\u8221\'20\'1D jobs.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CGovernor \uc2 Tina Kotek\uc2  wants to grow more family-wage jobs, but this isn\u8217\'20\'19t a family-wage job,\u8221\'20\'1D said Coffey. \u8220\'20\'1CThis is hardly a studio apartment job. I think people are under a misconception that because the industry is booming, workers are doing well. And that just simply isn\u8217\'20\'19t the case.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 ADI workers are also pushing for an end to plant shutdowns that place workers on furloughs, forcing them to use their vacation time or go into vacation debt in order to continue being paid for those shutdowns. The most recent shutdown took place over two weeks last December.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMost people started the year coming back, essentially, in a vacation deficit. So they had to work back for the vacation time that they had to expend for their two weeks off that they didn\u8217\'20\'19t ask for,\u8221\'20\'1D added Coffey. \u8220\'20\'1CWhat we\u8217\'20\'19re asking for is a fair share. We\u8217\'20\'19re just asking to be able to sustain ourselves.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240805ek85001gv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
