\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Seven major US labor unions call on Biden to \u8216\'20\'18shut off military aid to Israel\u8217\'20\'19\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 439 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 July 2024\par 16:58 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Letter to US president says: \u8216\'20\'18our unions are horrified that our tax dollars are financing this ongoing tragedy\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Seven major US labor unions representing about 6 million workers sent a letter to Joe Biden on Tuesday calling on his administration to \u8220\'20\'1Cimmediately halt all military aid to Israel\u8221\'20\'1D ahead of a visit to the US from \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 , Israel\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister, this week.\par \par \uc2 The unions that signed on to the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ASKF012G-ZuMQ2cK0zePLm3PaXY72Q3Q/view"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 letter }}}\uc2  include the \uc2 Association of Flight Attendants\uc2  (\uc2 AFA\uc2 ), \uc2 American Postal Workers Union\uc2  (APWU), International Union of Painters (IUPAT), \uc2 National Education Association (NEA)\uc2 , \uc2 Service Employees International Union\uc2  (\uc2 SEIU\uc2 ), \uc2 United Auto Workers (UAW)\uc2  and United Electrical Workers (UE).\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur unions are hearing the cries of humanity as this vicious war continues,\u8221\'20\'1D said Mark Dimondstein, the APWU president, in a press release. \u8220\'20\'1CWorking people and our unions are horrified that our tax dollars are financing this ongoing tragedy. We need a ceasefire now, and the best way to secure that is to shut off US military aid to Israel.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In the letter, the unions expressed concerns that the US president\u8217\'20\'19s three-part ceasefire plan announced in May 2024 has not been fully accepted as violence in Gaza has persisted.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLarge numbers of Palestinian civilians, many of them children, continue to be killed, reportedly often with US-manufactured bombs. Rising tensions in the region threaten to ensnare even more innocent civilians in a wider war. And the humanitarian crisis deepens by the day, with famine, mass displacement, and destruction of basic infrastructure including schools and hospitals. We have spoken directly to leaders of Palestinian trade unions who told us heart-wrenching stories of the conditions faced by working people in Gaza,\u8221\'20\'1D wrote the unions in the letter.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe time to act decisively to end this war is now. Stopping US military aid to Israel is the quickest and most sure way to do so, it is what US law demands, and it will show your commitment to securing a lasting peace in the region.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Earlier this year, US labor unions {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.laborforceasefire.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 launched}}}\uc2  the National Labor Network for Ceasefire, which has been signed by dozens of local unions around the US, including the letter signatories and \uc2 National Nurses United\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The letter comes as activists are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wjla.com/news/local/palestine-protests-israeli-prime-minister-benjamin-netanyahu-congress-address-international-court-justice-advisory-opinion-israel-aid-united-states-metropolitan-police-department-street-closures-parking-restrictions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 planning }}}\uc2  protest demonstrations in Washington DC this week over Netanyahu\u8217\'20\'19s visit, his first to the US since 7 October. Thousands of protesters are expected to descend on Washington DC to call for an end to the US aid to Israel that has been fueling the war in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240723ek7n0023d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
FF
