\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Unions rally round Harris as Trump makes populist appeal to workers\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 1,300 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 July 2024\par 11:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Labor unions who back Harris are keen to see continuation of Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s strong record of union support\par \par \uc2 US unions have begun to rally round Vice-President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  as Democrats and Republicans gear up for a fight over the labor vote in November.\par \par \uc2 The unions who have rallied to Harris so far are keen to see a continuation of the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s strong record of union support. Biden has been touted as the most pro-union president ever, and became the first sitting president to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/sep/26/biden-joins-uaw-strike-update-detroit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 walk a picket line}}}\uc2  during the \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  strike last year.\par \par \uc2 Harris, too, has been a vocal union supporter and is already racking up endorsements.\par \par \uc2 The 1.9 million-member \uc2 Service Employees International Union\uc2  (\uc2 SEIU\uc2 ) was among the first to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.seiu.org/2024/07/seius-verrett-seiu-is-all-in-for-kamala-harris-a-leader-who-will-fight-for-workers-and-beat-donald-trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  endorse }}}\uc2  Harris. Harris has close ties to the union and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pbs.org/newshour/politics/harris-announces-final-rules-on-minimum-nursing-home-staffing-standards"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  new safe staffing standards for nursing home workers with the union earlier this year.\par \par \uc2 The vice-president has also secured the backing of other unions, including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cwa-union.org/news/releases/communications-workers-america-endorses-kamala-harris-president"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Communications Workers of America}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ibew.org/media-center/Articles/24Daily/2407/240722_VicePresidentKamalaHarris"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 International Brotherhood of Electrical}}}\uc2 , the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.aft.org/press-release/aft-executive-council-unanimously-endorses-kamala-harris-president"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 American Federation of Teachers,}}}\uc2  the \uc2 United Food and Commercial Workers\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/UFWupdates/status/1815156550870482985"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the United Farm Workers}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://home.nuhw.org/2024/07/21/national-union-of-healthcare-workers-endorses-kamala-harris-for-president/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the National Union of Healthcare Workers}}}\uc2 , and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/GoIUPAT/status/1815406659419935187"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the International Union of Painters and Allied Trades}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Other major unions have yet to make an endorsement of Harris after endorsing Biden, including the National Education Association and United Auto Workers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor years,Vice-President Harris has shown a real willingness to listen to our members and working people everywhere about the issues that matter most to them,\u8221\'20\'1D said United Food and Commercial Workers international president \uc2 Marc Perrone\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs a US senator, she was a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/2020/08/06/opinions/why-grocery-store-workers-deserve-hazard-pay-harris-perrone/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 vocal supporter}}}\uc2  for essential worker protections during the pandemic. During her tenure as vice president, she was critical in the fight to lower prescription drugs and cast the tie-breaking vote to pass the Emergency Pension Plan Relief Act of 2021, safeguarding the retirements of over 350,000 union workers.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In contrast, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has only {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://wisconsinwatch.org/2024/04/trump-biden-election-law-enforcement-endorsement-police-unions/#:~:text=So%20far%20in%20the%202024,Wisconsin%20Watch's%20request%20for%20information."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 received}}}\uc2  the endorsement of the International Union of Police Association and the Florida Police Benevolent Association.\par \par \uc2 Union activists drove large numbers of members to the polls for Biden in 2020 and in the 2022 midterms. Having won in 2016 backed by voters in union strongholds in the midwest, Trump has once again positioned himself as the voice for workers and the working class.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s campaign to win over working-class and union member voters was much in evidence at the Republican convention last week. His vice-presidential pick, JD Vance, has been highly {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/07/20/business/wall-street-republicans-trump-jd-vance.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 critical of Wall Street}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vance.senate.gov/press-releases/senator-vance-visits-uaw-picket-line-in-toledo-ohio/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 also supported }}}\uc2  last year\u8217\'20\'19s auto strike.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe need a leader who\u8217\'20\'19s not in the pocket of big business, but answers to the working man, union and nonunion alike,\u8221\'20\'1D Vance told the convention.\par \par \uc2 The first night of the convention ended with a speech from the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/15/teamsters-union-president-sean-obrien-rnc-trump-speech"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 president}}}\uc2 , a first for the union. Sean O\u8217\'20\'19Brien thanked Trump \u8220\'20\'1Cfor opening the \uc2 RNC\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s doors\u8221\'20\'1D to the union.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  have yet to make an endorsement but O\u8217\'20\'19Brien\u8217\'20\'19s appearance has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/jul/12/teamsters-boss-gop-convention-speech-backlash"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 criticized}}}\uc2  by some members and labor leaders over the stark differences between Trump and the Biden administration on labor rights.\par \par \uc2 For all of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s blue-collar rhetoric, his policy record is more in line with pro-business, anti-union Republican orthodoxy.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://substack.perfectunion.us/p/over-five-dozen-billionaires-are?utm_campaign=post&utm_medium=web"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Over 60 billionaires }}}\uc2  have backed his most recent campaign as he intends to make substantial tax cuts for the wealthy permanent if re-elected; net tax cuts of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.americanprogressaction.org/article/comparing-trumps-haphazard-2500-tax-increase-to-bidens-targeted-tariffs/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $325,000 annually }}}\uc2  for households in the 0.1% of most wealthy households, while increasing taxes on average of $1,600 per middle class household annually if the tax cuts are extended.\par \par \uc2 During the strikes led by the \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2 , Trump consistently criticized the union\u8217\'20\'19s leaders and held his own rally with attendees who held signs claiming they were union members in support of Trump. They were later {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/09/27/us/politics/trump-autoworkers-detroit.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 outed}}}\uc2  as non-union members and non-auto workers.\par \par \uc2 In Wisconsin, Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nbcnews.com/business/business-news/foxconn-plant-once-touted-trump-13-000-job-juggernaut-will-n1264793"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 touted }}}\uc2  in 2017 that the \uc2 FoxConn\uc2  factory would be \u8220\'20\'1Cthe eighth wonder of the world\u8221\'20\'1D and create 13,000 jobs in the state, though the project never panned out.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt was a failure,\u8221\'20\'1D said Kent Miller, president and business manager of the Wisconsin Laborers\u8217\'20\'19 District Council.\par \par \uc2 Biden administration legislation, including the Inflation Reduction Act and the infrastructure bill, directly benefited members in Wisconsin, said Miller. He also cited the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s improvement of union pensions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat was brought up to President Trump when he was in office, and the only thing that got accomplished was the trillion dollar tax break. He did not fix pensions, he did not create infrastructure bills,\u8221\'20\'1D said Miller.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe policy speaks for itself and it\u8217\'20\'19s very clear.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Trump \u8220\'20\'1Cmade it harder for individuals to form a union, and put union-busting people in positions at the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  [\uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2 ].\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Throughout his administration, Trump made several policy changes that attacked labor unions and favored employers over workers.\par \par \uc2 Under Trump, the \uc2 NLRB{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.bloomberglaw.com/daily-labor-report/nlrb-empowers-employers-to-cut-off-union-dues-collections"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 allowed employers}}}\uc2  to halt union dues collections once a union contract expires, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/nlrb-overturns-obama-era-ruling-on-jointly-employed-workers-1513302992"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 overturned}}}\uc2  an Obama-era rule that allowed workers working as contractors or for franchises to unionize.\par \par \uc2 He also consistently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bna.com/trump-wants-21-n57982088623/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 proposed }}}\uc2  slashing the funding of the \uc2 NLRB\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 An {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.americanprogressaction.org/article/8-ways-the-biden-administration-has-fought-for-working-people-by-strengthening-unions/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 analysis }}}\uc2  conducted by the \uc2 Center for American Progress\uc2  found the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  ordered corporations to reinstate more fired workers in Biden\u8217\'20\'19s first year in office than the agency had in all four years of Trump\u8217\'20\'19s presidency.\par \par \uc2 Republicans have also stymied efforts to pass the Pro Act, legislation aimed at modernizing current labor laws in the US and strengthening workers\u8217\'20\'19 rights to unionize. Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://trumpwhitehouse.archives.gov/wp-content/uploads/2020/02/SAP_HR-2474.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 threatened }}}\uc2  to veto the legislation if it passed the House and Senate.\par \par \uc2 Trump\u8217\'20\'19s nominations to the \uc2 US supreme court\uc2  paved the way for the 5-4 decision in the 2018 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/opinions/17pdf/16-1466_2b3j.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Janus case}}}\uc2 , which ruled that public sector workers who are represented by a union can not be required to pay union dues.\par \par \uc2 In 2018, the Trump administration {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonexaminer.com/news/2003622/trump-administration-proposes-major-overhaul-of-the-postal-service/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 proposed }}}\uc2  an overhaul of the \uc2 United States Postal Service\uc2 , including stripping workers of the right to collectively bargain wages.\par \par \uc2 In 2015 during his first presidential campaign, Trump {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://archive.nytimes.com/www.nytimes.com/politics/first-draft/2015/11/20/donald-trump-says-hed-absolutely-require-muslims-to-register/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  he would prefer to construct buildings without unions when asked on the subject. He has a history of using non-union workers for construction projects for his businesses, but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ibew.org/media-center/Articles/16Daily/1607/Trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 using }}}\uc2  union labor for construction work at Mar-a-Lago and his own homes and he had a reputation, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ibew.org/media-center/Articles/16Daily/1607/Trump"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  according to the IBEW}}}\uc2 , for deceiving workers on pay for the work they completed.\par \par \uc2 Future clashes between Trump and Harris over who supports workers are also likely to center on Project 2025, a conservative manifesto developed by dozens of former Trump administration officials. Project 2025 includes {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://static.project2025.org/2025_MandateForLeadership_FULL.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 plans}}}\uc2  to further {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://aflcio.org/press/releases/afl-cio-highlights-anti-worker-foundation-trumps-second-term-agenda"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 attack labor rights}}}\uc2 , including banning unions for public service workers and letting companies stop paying overtime.\par \par \uc2 Harris has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.whitehouse.gov/briefing-room/speeches-remarks/2024/05/21/remarks-by-vice-president-harris-at-the-service-employees-international-union-quadrennial-convention/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 touted}}}\uc2  the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s strong record on labor rights. \u8220\'20\'1CPresident Biden and I are proud to lead the most pro-union administration in our nation\u8217\'20\'19s history,\u8221\'20\'1D she said during an \uc2 SEIU\uc2  convention in May, before listing the Biden White House\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to make workplaces safe, ban non-compete agreements, and make it easier for service workers to organize.\par \par \uc2 Some union leaders had publicly come out for Biden\u8217\'20\'19s withdrawal. Harris may not have secured the nomination yer, but she seems well positioned to take over Biden\u8217\'20\'19s legacy as a pro-union leader.\par \par \uc2 J\u8217\'20\'19nee DeLancey, a \uc2 UFCW\uc2  member who is a grocery store worker at Town & Country Market, in Seattle, said: \u8220\'20\'1CAs a union that is majority women, that has a diverse membership of many people of color, and of immigrants, we are very excited to have such a community-rooted and worker-driven candidate to support.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240723ek7n0018k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
