\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 DoJ sues Texas-based child migrant shelter provider for rife sexual abuse\b0\par\par\uc2 Erum Salam \par \uc2 520 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 July 2024\par 17:19 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Southwest Key, operating 29 shelters for unaccompanied minors, has received over $6bn in federal funds since 2008\par \par \uc2 Employees of the country\u8217\'20\'19s largest provider of housing to unaccompanied migrant children encountered at the US\u8217\'20\'19s southern border have been sexually abusing and harassing the children in their care for nearly a decade, the US justice department alleges in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.justice.gov/opa/pr/justice-department-sues-southwest-key-sexual-abuse-and-harassment-children-shelters#:~:text=HHS%20will%20continue%20to%20work,every%20child%20in%20HHS%20custody.%E2%80%9D"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lawsuit}}}\uc2  filed on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Southwest Key operates 29 shelters across Texas, Arizona and California, housing and feeding undocumented children between the ages of 13 and 17, who come mostly from Guatemala, Honduras and El Salvador, crossing the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-mexico-border"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US-Mexico border}}}\uc2  without their parents.\par \par \uc2 These children remain in the shelter until they are reunited with their immediate families or placed with a relative or other vetted sponsor while their immigration cases are litigated.\par \par \uc2 Southwest Key has partnered with the federal government on immigration at the border for nearly 20 years, and has received more than {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usaspending.gov/search/?hash=deb4495e178877b2c30235c5a9c4ab3e"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $6b in federal funding}}}\uc2  since 2008 from the departments of health and human services, education, labor, justice and others.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFrom at least 2015 through at least 2023, multiple Southwest Key employees have subjected unaccompanied children in their care to repeated and unwelcome sexual abuse, harassment, and misconduct and a hostile housing environment, including severe sexual abuse and rape, solicitation of sex acts, solicitation of nude photos, entreaties for sexually inappropriate relationships, sexual comments and gestures, leering, and inappropriate touching,\u8221\'20\'1D the lawsuit says.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn some cases, Southwest Key employees threatened children to maintain their silence.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Through the lawsuit, the justice department aims for Southwest Key\u8217\'20\'19s practices to be declared discriminatory, and therefore in violation of the Fair Housing Act, and seeks monetary damages to compensate the children allegedly harmed in Southwest Key\u8217\'20\'19s care, as well as \u8220\'20\'1Ccivil penalties against Southwest Key to vindicate the public interest\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn search of the American dream, children often endure perilous journeys on their migration north to the southern border,\u8221\'20\'1D said US attorney Alamdar S Hamdani for the southern district of Texas, the federal district court working with the justice department\u8217\'20\'19s civil rights division and the US attorney\u8217\'20\'19s office for the western district of Texas, where the lawsuit was filed.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe sexual harassment alleged in the complaint would destroy any child\u8217\'20\'19s sense of safety, turning what was an American dream into a nightmare,\u8221\'20\'1D Hamdani said.\par \par \uc2 Southwest Key denies the justice department\u8217\'20\'19s allegations.\par \par \uc2 In a statement to the Guardian on Friday, the organization wrote: \u8220\'20\'1CSouthwest Key Programs\u8217\'20\'19 primary focus is the safety, health, and well-being of each one of the children and youth we care for. We continue to review the complaint, and it does not present the accurate picture of the care and commitment our employees provide to the youth and children. We are in constant communication and continue to closely partner with the Office of Refugee Resettlement (ORR), as we have done so for the past two decades to ensure the children and youth entrusted to our care are safe with us during their short stay with Southwest Key.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240719ek7j001ju\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
