\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Uber\uc2  and \uc2 Lyft\uc2  agree to minimum pay and benefits for Massachusetts drivers\b0\par\par\uc2 Sarah Betancourt \par \uc2 955 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 June 2024\par 14:34 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Ride-share companies sign off on $175m settlement that will give workers paid sick leave and other protections\par \par \uc2 Uber\uc2  and \uc2 Lyft\uc2  drivers will be guaranteed among the highest wages in the US for ride-share workers under a historic deal agreed with Massachusetts prosecutors.\par \par \uc2 Andrea Campbell, the state\u8217\'20\'19s attorney general, and the two companies agreed to a $175m settlement on Thursday evening that requires a minimum pay floor of $32.50 per hour, and introduces a slew of other benefits and protections that drivers didn\u8217\'20\'19t already have.\par \par \uc2 The resolution to four years of litigation between the parties also resulted in a settlement of $174m to be paid by the companies: $148m from \uc2 Uber\uc2  and $27m from \uc2 Lyft\uc2 . Most will be distributed as restitution to current and former drivers who were underpaid by the companies. More information about who will qualify for those payments and how to file a claim will be released in the coming weeks.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFor years, these companies have underpaid their drivers and denied them basic benefits,\u8221\'20\'1D said Campbell. \u8220\'20\'1CToday\u8217\'20\'19s agreement holds \uc2 Uber\uc2  and \uc2 Lyft\uc2  accountable and provides their drivers, for the very first time in Massachusetts, guaranteed minimum pay, paid sick leave, occupational accident insurance and healthcare stipends.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Massachusetts now joins {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nyc.gov/site/dca/news/018-24/mayor-adams-first-annual-increase-minimum-pay-rate-app-based-restaurant-delivery#:~:text=The%20$19.56%20rate%20reflects%20the,with%20an%20adjustment%20for%20inflation."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pbs.org/newshour/politics/uber-and-lyft-say-theyll-operate-in-minnesota-after-legislature-passes-driver-pay-compromise#:~:text=The%20House%20agreement%20announced%20Saturday,the%20state%20under%20those%20rates."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Minnesota}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.uber.com/blog/washington-driver-flexibility-law/#:~:text=Starting%20December%2031,%202022,%20you,a%20$3%20per-trip%20minimum"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Washington}}}\uc2  and other states in setting a minimum pay rate for drivers.\par \par \uc2 Drivers will also benefit from access to paid sick leave if they work 15 hours weekly, as well as a stipend for health benefits and occupational accident insurance. They can accrue up to 40 hours annually of paid sick leave, which will be bought through stipends to buy into the state\u8217\'20\'19s program for paid family and medical leave.\par \par \uc2 Both \uc2 Uber\uc2  and \uc2 Lyft\uc2  don\u8217\'20\'19t intend to pull out of Massachusetts and operations will continue. The changes will go into effect on 15 August and will be adjusted annually for inflation.\par \par \uc2 Ed Booth has been driving for \uc2 Lyft\uc2  for more than seven years. He said he usually makes a lot more than the new floor for wages, but it depends on what hours he works and whether there\u8217\'20\'19s a surge of customers \u8211\'20\'13 like at 2am when young people leave closing bars.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThen all of a sudden, you\u8217\'20\'19ll get all this cash windfall that will bring your average back up to somewhere around $40, $45,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 He described himself as an independent guy who has owned many businesses, including a current one in web development. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve been treating this like my own business,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, adding that he doesn\u8217\'20\'19t want any union involvement in the future.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou know, the health insurance, I\u8217\'20\'19m gonna take advantage of it,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. He\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Ca little bit\u8221\'20\'1D concerned that many new drivers will sign up to take advantage of the hourly floor, creating more competition, but he\u8217\'20\'19s confident he can handle it.\par \par \uc2 Jeremy Bird, \uc2 Lyft\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s executive vice president of driver experience, called the moment a \u8220\'20\'1Chuge win for Massachusetts drivers that secures their freedom to earn when, where and however long they want\u8221\'20\'1D. He said that on any given day, the flexible work on the \uc2 Lyft\uc2  platform provides an average of 8,500 drivers in Massachusetts independence to earn while attending school and caring for families.\par \par \uc2 Uber\uc2  media relations referred the Guardian to a blogpost in which Tony West, \uc2 Uber\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s chief legal officer, wrote that the agreement is \u8220\'20\'1Can example of what independent, flexible work with dignity should look like in the 21st century\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn taking this opportunity, we\u8217\'20\'19ve resolved historical liabilities by constructing a new operating model that balances both flexibility and benefits,\u8221\'20\'1D West said.\par \par \uc2 The accord doesn\u8217\'20\'19t take a stance on the classification of drivers, allowing them to continue to act as contractors.\par \par \uc2 That\u8217\'20\'19s the one thing that made the settlement a mixed bag for Henry De Groot, co-founder of the organization Massachusetts Drivers United. He often works 30 hours from Friday to Sunday as a driver.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COn the one hand, a massive victory for drivers. That delivers real advancements in terms of an earnings guarantee in terms of paid sick leave, healthcare and other important basic protections of employment law,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. But he\u8217\'20\'19s disappointed because Campbell\u8217\'20\'19s office didn\u8217\'20\'19t \u8220\'20\'1Cpursue enforcement of the law here. There\u8217\'20\'19s no ruling on employment status.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Drivers will be paid the minimum of $32.50, and will be able to make more \u8211\'20\'13 the wage will apply for when drivers are en route to pick up passengers or transporting them. Some drivers complained that the companies won\u8217\'20\'19t be required to pay for the time when they\u8217\'20\'19ve logged on to their apps, but haven\u8217\'20\'19t chosen a customer\u8217\'20\'19s ride request.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBy setting the amount at $32.50, we were trying to account for the time the drivers are waiting as well,\u8221\'20\'1D said Abby Taylor, the Massachusetts deputy attorney general, who worked on the case.\par \par \uc2 For health insurance, drivers will be offered a \u8220\'20\'1Cpooled health insurance benefit\u8221\'20\'1D for anyone who drives more than 15 hours per week, boiling down to an insurance stipend to pay for a plan through the state\u8217\'20\'19s health connector.\par \par \uc2 The agreement also allows an appeals process for drivers to push back on deactivations.\par \par \uc2 Then attorney general \uc2 Maura Healey\uc2 , who is now governor, launched the lawsuit in 2020, alleging the ride share companies were boosting their profits by treating drivers as contractors and denying them benefits that employees would receive.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur lawsuit against \uc2 Uber\uc2  and \uc2 Lyft\uc2  was always about fairness for drivers,\u8221\'20\'1D she said on Thursday night in a statement, calling the wages \u8220\'20\'1Chistoric\u8221\'20\'1D and a benefit to \u8220\'20\'1Cright the wrongs of the past\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240628ek6s002xo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
