\par\par \uc2 Film\par \b \uc2 Film and TV crew members reach deal with Hollywood studios to avert strike\b0\par\par\uc2 Dani Anguiano \par \uc2 523 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 June 2024\par 19:08 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Iatse union agrees tentative three-year deal with \uc2 Disney\uc2 , \uc2 Netflix\uc2  and others over pay, AI protections and residuals\par \par \uc2 The union that represents film and television crews has reached an agreement with Hollywood studios that will stave off a major strike \u8211\'20\'13 a welcome development after the industry saw significant labor turmoil last year.\par \par \uc2 The International Alliance of Theatrical Stage Employees (Iatse) and the \uc2 Alliance of Motion Picture and Television Producers\uc2  (\uc2 AMPTP\uc2 ) announced on Tuesday they had a tentative three-year agreement that will affect about 50,000 crew members.\par \par \uc2 If approved, the deal will bring pay hikes, artificial intelligence protections and streaming residuals for union members, including costume designers, hair stylists, make-up artists, art directors, set painters, camera technicians and editors. Union members will vote on whether or not to ratify the agreement.\par \par \uc2 The news brought relief in Hollywood, where the industry has not yet recovered from being shut down for much of last year. Actors and writers went on strike last year and the months-long work stoppages effectively brought film and television production to a halt. This year, workers have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.latimes.com/entertainment-arts/business/newsletter/2024-05-21/hollywoods-weak-recovery-is-hurting-jobs-how-much-better-will-it-get-the-wide-shot"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  struggling to find work because there are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.latimes.com/entertainment-arts/business/story/2024-05-28/hollywood-crew-unemployed-fewer-jobs-la-production-decline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fewer jobs}}}\uc2  available as the industry slows and as studios have cut back on spending.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 AMPTP\uc2 , which represents studios, streaming services and companies including \uc2 Disney\uc2 , \uc2 Netflix\uc2 , \uc2 Warner Bros Discovery\uc2  and Amazon Prime, is the same group that struggled to reach a deal with writers and actors last year.\par \par \uc2 Last week, almost 400 industry members, including Mark Ruffalo, Kerry Washington, Ryan Coogler and Seth Rogen, signed a letter in solidarity with the union, expressing support for their demands and urging the studios to offer a fair contract, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://deadline.com/2024/06/letter-of-solidarity-hollywood-guilds-iatse-basic-crafts-mark-ruffalo-quinta-brunson-1235978947/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Deadline}}}\uc2  reported.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese crew members dedicate their lives to their artistry and to their departments \u8211\'20\'13 working long hours in often challenging conditions to bring stories to life,\u8221\'20\'1D the letter stated. \u8220\'20\'1CBeing able to do their jobs safely and compensated fairly is essential for our membership to be able to do our jobs. \u8216\'20\'18Nothing moves without the crew.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Iatse contract was set to expire in July, but now, with a tentative agreement in hand, Hollywood is unlikely to see another major strike this year. Members must still vote to ratify the deal, and a separate agreement affecting about 20,000 crew members across the US is still under negotiation.\par \par \uc2 Iatse has not yet released the full terms of its tentative agreement with the studios, but said in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://iatse.net/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/FINAL-and-Formatted-Basic-Agreement-Finalized-Joint-Letter-tzfix.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2  that it \u8220\'20\'1Cincludes new protections around artificial intelligence, including language that ensures no employee is required to provide AI prompts in any manner that would result in the displacement of any covered employee.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The deal will also bring scale rate increases of 7%, 4%, and 3.5% over three years, triple time for workers any time their work day exceeds 15 hours, and payments from studios to help cover a shortfall in the union\u8217\'20\'19s health insurance budget.\par \par \uc2 The union will release a complete summary of the tentative agreement later this week, it said.\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press contributed to this report\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240626ek6q002s1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
