\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 DC coffee chain lists CEOs and Uber lobbyist as baristas to halt union drive\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 803 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 June 2024\par 18:06 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Compass Coffee is accused of hiring 124 additional people before union election next month\par \par \uc2 A coffee chain in the Washington DC area is accused of hiring dozens of friends of management, including other local food service executives and an Uber lobbyist, in an effort to defeat a union election scheduled for 16 July.\par \par \uc2 Workers at seven Compass Coffee locations, more than a third of the company\u8217\'20\'19s stores, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/business/2024/05/31/compass-coffee-workers-seven-stores-launch-union-drive/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  their intent to unionize in May 2024. The company has 18 cafes in Washington DC and northern Virginia and its coffee can be purchased in grocery stores throughout the area.\par \par \uc2 In a post on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 /X, Compass Coffee United accused the coffee chain of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/CompassCoffeeU/status/1803568899398492416/photo/2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hiring}}}\uc2  124 additional people at cafes that are attempting to unionize. The union has also accused the company of manipulating worker schedules retroactively to try to make the new employees eligible to vote in the union election.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe received their first voter list. There were 43 people on the Georgetown cafe list, most of whom I have never met or seen in the cafe before,\u8221\'20\'1D said Penina Meier-Silverman, a shift supervisor at the Georgetown Compass Coffee store. \u8220\'20\'1CSo the cafes are just flooded with new baristas. We also saw that they were forging schedules for days that have already passed. So they put people on the schedule for days that have passed that were never at work.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Union organizing began more than a year ago due to ongoing issues at the company including the elimination of tips for workers, unfair disciplinary actions and broken equipment issues, said Meier-Silverman.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CReally all we\u8217\'20\'19re asking for is just respect, safe working conditions, fair compensation, and benefits, fundamentally, which all equates to just human decency and respect in the workplace,\u8221\'20\'1D added Meier-Silverman. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s been a very clear response that they intend to do everything in their power to pack this election and kill it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The union has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nlrb.gov/case/05-CA-344384"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed}}}\uc2  an unfair labor practice charge with the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  against Compass Coffee over their conduct. Meier-Silverman said they intended to file numerous charges over the mass new hires and alleged retaliation workers have experienced since the union campaign went public. She noted that she was written up for talking with a customer about the union.\par \par \uc2 Among the new baristas {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/CompassCoffeeU/status/1803568899398492416"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cited}}}\uc2  by the union are other local restaurant managers, including the Union Kitchen CEO and co-founder, Cullen Gilchrist. Gilchrist has presided over a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://dcist.com/story/23/07/28/union-kitchen-dc-petition-remove-labor-union/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tumultuous}}}\uc2  union organizing campaign over the past couple of years at Union Kitchen, a local specialty grocery chain in the Washington DC area.\par \par \uc2 He did not respond to multiple requests for comment.\par \par \uc2 After publication, Liz \u8220\'20\'1CTizzy\u8221\'20\'1D Brown, a member of Uber\u8217\'20\'19s federal affairs team, said: \u8220\'20\'1CI recently attended a training on June 9 alongside several other new hires at \uc2 Compass\uc2 , and as part of that training I signed the same paperwork everyone there did.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHowever, I never worked a shift beyond that initial training, and as soon as this all came to light I reached out to \uc2 Compass\uc2  and asked to be removed from their employment system. This was entirely in my personal capacity as Tizzy Brown, and has nothing to do with my full-time job.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Senator Bernie Sanders criticized Compass Coffee over the hirings in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/BernieSanders/status/1804505866567115242"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 post on X}}}\uc2  on Saturday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CClaiming that a lobbyist from Uber & CEOs from other companies are workers in order to rig a union election is totally absurd & disgusting,\u8221\'20\'1D Sanders wrote. \u8220\'20\'1CI strongly support Compass Workers and call on Compass Coffee DC to respect the rights of their workers to organize & end its union busting.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Compass Coffee United has also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/CompassCoffeeU/status/1804268672405406029"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cited}}}\uc2  issues with an impostor account on X, which has copied posts from their union account and made pro-Palestine posts, with the union noting they will poll members on that and similar issues after winning the union election.\par \par \uc2 Michael Haft, the owner and CEO of Compass Coffee, said in an email: \u8220\'20\'1CWe believe all employees of Compass Coffee at the locations that have been petitioned are eligible. The list reflects the current employees at the time of the vote. As such, we will stay in close communication with our partners to ensure the most up-to-date list on the 14th as there is often normal turnover and growth in the service industry, especially seasonally, and we expect our final list to be reflective of that.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He added: \u8220\'20\'1CDue to privacy concerns, we have a longstanding policy not to comment on individual employees without their consent.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The workers are seeking to unionize with the \uc2 SEIU\uc2 -affiliated Workers United, which represents more than 450 \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  stores that have unionized. According to organizers, 84% of workers signed union authorization cards.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240624ek6o001gy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
