\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Greed\u8217\'20\'19: John Deere rolls out hundreds of US layoffs and sends work to Mexico\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 708 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 June 2024\par 11:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Agricultural equipment company plans to move production out of the country in move condemned by workers\par \par \uc2 US workers at John Deere plants have accused the company of acting on \u8220\'20\'1Cgreed\u8221\'20\'1D as America\u8217\'20\'19s most famous agricultural equipment company plans to shift more production to Mexico.\par \par \uc2 The company \u8211\'20\'13 famous for its green tractors and leaping deer logo \u8211\'20\'13 has announced layoffs of several hundred workers over the last several months with more layoffs planned for later this year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe get wind of more layoffs daily, it seems, and it\u8217\'20\'19s causing uncertainty all over,\u8221\'20\'1D said a longtime John Deere worker at the Harvester Works plant in East Moline, Illinois, who requested to remain anonymous for fear of retaliation. \u8220\'20\'1CThe only reason for \uc2 Deere\uc2  to do this is greed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 They cited the company\u8217\'20\'19s recent profits. John Deere {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.deere.com/en/news/all-news/fy23-fourth-quarter-earnings/#:~:text=For%20fiscal%2Dyear%202023%2C%20net,per%20share%2C%20in%20fiscal%202022."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  a profit of over $10bn in fiscal year 2023 and its CEO John May {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/news/reuters.com,2024:newsml_FWN3E00G6:0-deere-co-says-ceo-john-c-may-s-2023-total-compensation-was-26-7-mln-vs-20-3-mln-in-2022-sec-filing/#:~:text=Deere%20%26%20Co%20DE%3A-,DEERE%20%26%20CO%20SAYS%20CEO%20JOHN%20C.,WAS%20ABOUT%20284%20TO%201"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 received}}}\uc2  $26.7m in total compensation. John Deere {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s22.q4cdn.com/253594569/files/doc_financials/2023/ar/2023-deere-company-annual-report.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 spent over $7.2bn }}}\uc2  on stock buybacks in 2023 and provided shareholders with more than $1.4bn in dividends.\par \par \uc2 The worker said: \u8220\'20\'1COur harvester plant is still in production and management has been quiet. They\u8217\'20\'19re not doing the normal \u8216\'20\'18time to talk\u8217\'20\'19 meetings as they have in recent past. My belief is that they don\u8217\'20\'19t want people to know they are losing their jobs until they get everything built for the year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe know a layoff is coming, we don\u8217\'20\'19t know if, how many or when it will happen. We\u8217\'20\'19re expecting to finish production in mid-August and believe we will see a large layoff then.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In October last year, John Deere {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kwqc.com/2023/09/20/breaking-john-deere-harvester-works-announces-indefinite-layoffs/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  250 indefinite layoffs at the Illinois plant. Another 34 workers were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wqad.com/article/money/business/john-deere/john-deere-lay-off-34-employees-moline-cylinder-works/526-4ee7bd6e-34a4-46c0-842a-426970ca4d69"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 laid off}}}\uc2  in May.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this year, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.desmoinesregister.com/story/money/business/2024/05/21/with-sales-slowing-deere-lays-off-more-in-iowa/73777714007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 at least 650 jobs}}}\uc2  were cut at John Deere\u8217\'20\'19s plants in Iowa, with 500 jobs cut in Waterloo and 150 jobs cut at the Ankeny plant. Another {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.desmoinesregister.com/story/money/business/2024/06/03/john-deere-employees-take-early-retirement-as-layoffs-loom/73921113007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 103 workers}}}\uc2  took an early retirement offer at the Ottumwa plant after the company announced plans to cut more jobs at the plant later this year and shift that production to Mexico.\par \par \uc2 Chris Laursen, 53, is one of the employees at the Ottumwa plant who took the early retirement, citing concerns about being laid off given he was terminated last year but through his union won his job back. He had worked there for 22 years.\par \par \uc2 Laursen said: \u8220\'20\'1C[For] a lot of these communities, like mine in Ottumwa, losing John Deere would be an extremely big loss. It\u8217\'20\'19s a town of 28,000, and the only other manufacturing is a pork processing facility, so it doesn\u8217\'20\'19t leave a lot of options for jobs.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA multinational corporation like \uc2 Deere\uc2  sees Mexico as pretty attractive for a cheap labor source: they can import steel cheaper there and bring it across the border and sell it to the majority of their market in the US. It\u8217\'20\'19s a sign of the times, perpetuating what\u8217\'20\'19s been going on with the loss of manufacturing here in America, good union jobs and otherwise.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 KWWL News 7, a local NBC News affiliate in Iowa, reported that John Deere {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kwwl.com/news/waterloo/sources-john-deere-to-lay-off-global-production-and-salaried-employees/article_47465ef0-1f77-11ef-9c3d-47b75137ccd8.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sent out }}}\uc2  an email to workers stating plans of further layoffs in the third quarter of this year, but the number of layoffs were not provided.\par \par \uc2 Deere{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ourquadcities.com/news/local-news/deere-moving-some-production-from-dubuque-to-mexico-by-2026/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  plans to move production of skid steer loaders and compact track loaders from a Dubuque plant to Mexico by late 2026.\par \par \uc2 In 2022, the company had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/markets/us/deere-move-cab-production-mexico-amid-tight-us-labor-market-2022-06-03/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  plans to move cab production from Iowa to Mexico, impacting 250 employees.\par \par \uc2 John Deere stated its 2023 annual report that it employs {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s22.q4cdn.com/253594569/files/doc_financials/2023/ar/2023-deere-company-annual-report.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 33,800 workers}}}\uc2  in the US and Canada.\par \par \uc2 The layoffs come in the wake of a strike of more than 10,000 workers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/oct/14/john-deere-workers-strike-contract-union"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 represented }}}\uc2  by the \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  at 14 John Deere plants in Iowa, Illinois, Kansas, Colorado and Georgia in October 2021. The strike led headlines during {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2021/oct/23/striketober-unions-strikes-workers-lasting-change"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Striketober\u8217\'20\'19}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 a month of large scale industrial actions around the US. The John Deere strike ended in November that year when workers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.desmoinesregister.com/story/money/business/2021/11/17/uaw-john-deere-strike-2021-vote-results-contract-end/8619898002/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ratified}}}\uc2  a new six-year union contract agreement.\par \par \uc2 John Deere did not respond to multiple requests for comment.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240607ek67001jm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
