\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 UAW\uc2  seeks new election at \uc2 Mercedes-Benz\uc2  in Alabama after losing vote\b0\par\par\uc2 Guardian staff and agency \par \uc2 408 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 May 2024\par 19:35 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  filed petition Friday, accusing company of \u8216\'20\'18relentless\u8217\'20\'19 campaign including firings and captive-audience meetings\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 United Auto Workers (UAW) union\uc2  is seeking a new election at a \uc2 Mercedes-Benz\uc2  vehicle plant in Alabama after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/17/uaw-mercedes-alabama-union-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 losing a vote}}}\uc2  there last week, according to a petition filed on Friday with the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  (\uc2 NLRB\uc2 ).\par \par \uc2 The union accused Mercedes of engaging \u8220\'20\'1Cin a relentless anti-union campaign\u8221\'20\'1D including the firing of employees who were pro-union and holding frequent captive-audience meetings to spread anti-union views, according to the filing.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe sincerely hoped the \uc2 UAW\uc2  would respect our team members\u8217\'20\'19 decision. Throughout the election, we worked with the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  to adhere to its guidelines and we will continue to do so as we work through this process,\u8221\'20\'1D a Mercedes spokesperson said.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UAW\uc2  lost when about 56% of the nearly 5,000 workers at the Vance, Alabama, plant and nearby battery factory voted against unionizing.\par \par \uc2 The defeat just over a week ago came amid the \uc2 UAW\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s ambitious union-organizing campaign to recruit 150,000 non-union autoworkers around the US, and after riding a historic win last month at a \uc2 Volkswagen\uc2  plant in Chattanooga, Tennessee, where the \uc2 UAW\uc2  won a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/19/volkswagen-unionize-uaw-tennessee?CMP=share_btn_url"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 landslide victory}}}\uc2  with 73% of workers voting to unionize.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UAW\uc2  in its new filing said Mercedes\u8217\'20\'19 efforts to influence the vote constituted unfair labor practices and prevented a free choice by employees, warranting a new election.\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  said a regional director will review the union\u8217\'20\'19s objection and could decide to call for a hearing in the coming weeks.\par \par \uc2 The fight at Mercedes was much more contentious than at VW, where the company took a neutral stance, the union and labor experts said of US union relations with the management of the two rival German vehicle brands.\par \par \uc2 For example, Mercedes leaders frequently pointed to signs inside the plant urging employees to vote no, according to workers and photos reviewed by Reuters.\par \par \uc2 Mercedes also replaced the chief executive of its US business in the weeks leading up to the vote and encouraged employees to give him a chance, which some workers said added strength to the anti-union campaign.\par \par \uc2 Southern states have for decades successfully fought off unionization drives in an attempt to keep down labor costs \u8211\'20\'13 a practice critics have called the \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.instagram.com/uaw.union/p/C6txNYTsJ7g/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alabama discount}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240525ek5p00209\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
