\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Farm owners in California mass shooting to pay workers $450,000\b0\par\par\uc2 Maya Yang \par \uc2 524 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 May 2024\par 01:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Workplace killings in 2023 revealed hazardous working conditions of migrant farmworkers in Half Moon Bay\par \par \uc2 The owners of two mushroom farms in northern California where a disgruntled employee shot and killed seven people last year will pay a total of more than $450,000 in back wages and damages to 62 employees.\par \par \uc2 In an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dol.gov/newsroom/releases/whd/whd20240520-0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announcement}}}\uc2  released on Monday following an extensive investigation, the US labor department said the payment is an element of administrative settlements reached by the department\u8217\'20\'19s wage and hour division with California Terra Garden and Concord Farms.\par \par \uc2 The government\u8217\'20\'19s announcement comes after the incident in which the accused gunman, 67-year old Chunli Zhao, opened fire {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/jan/23/at-least-seven-dead-in-northern-california-shootings"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 on two farms}}}\uc2  in Half Moon Bay, a small community approximately 30 miles south of San Francisco, on 23 January 2023, killing seven workers and injuring another.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to investigators, Zhao said that prior to the shooting, he had had an argument with a supervisor who insisted he pay $100 in repairs following a forklift incident that Zhao said was not his fault. According to Zhao, a co-worker intentionally hit the forklift with a bulldozer, the San Francisco Chronicle {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sfchronicle.com/bayarea/article/half-moon-bay-mass-shooting-dispute-over-100-17752986.php"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2 . Zhao, a Chinese citizen, has pleaded {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.mercurynews.com/2024/02/29/accused-half-moon-bay-gunman-arraigned-on-murder-charges-in-2023-shooting-spree/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 not guilty}}}\uc2  to multiple murder charges.\par \par \uc2 Zhao worked at Concord Farms previously and was later an employee at California Terra Garden.\par \par \uc2 The deadly shooting and the labor department\u8217\'20\'19s investigation revealed the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.smcgov.org/ceo/news/county-launches-task-force-improve-living-conditions-farm-laborers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hazardous working conditions}}}\uc2  that many migrant farmworkers have been subjected to in San Mateo county.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur investigators found workers at California Terra Gardens and Concord Farms housed in sickening conditions, forced to sleep near garbage and with insects all around,\u8221\'20\'1D Alberto Raymond, the labor department\u8217\'20\'19s wage and hour division assistant district director, said in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.dol.gov/newsroom/releases/whd/whd20240520-0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 At California Terra Garden, investigators found that 39 workers were housed in cramped cargo containers, garages and dilapidated trailers, were forced to sleep on filthy mattresses and were exposed to insects and trash. According to the labor department, the farm\u8217\'20\'19s owners, Xianmin Guan and his wife, Liming Zhu, illegally deducted money from workers\u8217\'20\'19 pay for the substandard housing.\par \par \uc2 At Concord Farms, investigators found that its owner, Grace Tung, housed workers in moldy, makeshift rooms in a greenhouse infested with bugs. Tung also violated federal regulations by shortchanging workers who were not paid appropriate overtime, the labor department said.\par \par \uc2 As part of the settlements, California Terra Garden has agreed to pay totals of $84,074 directly to 39 workers to recoup the employers\u8217\'20\'19 illegal housing deductions, and $42,494 in civil money penalties to resolve its housing, wage-disclosure and record-keeping violations.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Concord Farms has agreed to pay a total of $370,107 in overtime wages and liquidated damages to 10 workers, as well as a total of $4,242 in late wages to 23 workers. It has also agreed to pay $29,049 in civil money penalties to address its various violations.\par \par \uc2 The civil penalties are in addition to the more than $450,000 in back wages and damages to be paid to the 62 employees from both farms.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240522ek5m003e9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
