\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18You feel like you\u8217\'20\'19re in prison\u8217\'20\'19: workers claim Amazon\u8217\'20\'19s surveillance violates labor law\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 774 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 May 2024\par 19:14 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Exclusive: employees at a Missouri warehouse file charges against firm alleging use of \u8216\'20\'18intrusive algorithms\u8217\'20\'19 to deter union efforts\par \par \uc2 Amazon has been accused of using \u8220\'20\'1Cintrusive algorithms\u8221\'20\'1D as part of a sweeping surveillance program to monitor and deter union organizing activities.\par \par \uc2 Workers at a warehouse run by the technology giant on the outskirts of St Louis, Missouri, are today filing an unfair labor practice charge with the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  (\uc2 NLRB\uc2 ).\par \par \uc2 A copy of the charge, seen by the Guardian, alleges that Amazon has \u8220\'20\'1Cmaintained intrusive algorithms and other workplace controls and surveillance which interfere with Section 7 rights of employees to engage in protected concerted activity\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 There have been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vox.com/recode/2020/10/6/21502639/amazon-union-busting-tracking-memo-spoc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 several}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2020/10/24/how-amazon-prevents-unions-by-surveilling-employee-activism.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports}}}\uc2  of Amazon surveilling workers over union organizing and activism, including human resources monitoring employee message boards, software to track union threats and job listings for intelligence analysts to monitor \u8220\'20\'1Clabor organizing threats\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUs coming together to file this charge will hold Amazon accountable. We don\u8217\'20\'19t want this becoming the norm,\u8221\'20\'1D Wendy Taylor, a packer at Amazon\u8217\'20\'19s STL8 fulfillment center in Saint Peters, Missouri, since August 2020 and an organizing committee member, said in an interview. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s out of control.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have an injury crisis and we\u8217\'20\'19re being watched and you feel like you\u8217\'20\'19re in prison. We just want people to know we have a right to organize, the right to form a union and the right to have a safer work environment.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Eileen Hards, an Amazon spokesperson, said: \u8220\'20\'1CTo be clear, there\u8217\'20\'19s been no finding of unlawful activity by the \uc2 NLRB\uc2 . The fact is this charge, which was just filed, has yet to be investigated or proven.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Artificial intelligence can be used by warehouse employers like Amazon \u8220\'20\'1Cto essentially have 24/7 unregulated and algorithmically processed and recorded video, and often audio data of what their workers are doing all the time\u8221\'20\'1D, said Seema N Patel, a fellow and lecturer at Stanford Law School. \u8220\'20\'1CIt enables employers to control, record, monitor and use that data to discipline hundreds of thousands of workers in a way that no human manager or group of managers could even do.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Taylor said: \u8220\'20\'1CAmazon tracks our every move. They know every move you make, when you\u8217\'20\'19re working, when you\u8217\'20\'19re not working. They surveil you with their cameras. Managers surveil you with their laptops because they can pull up your profile and a bar changes a certain color when you\u8217\'20\'19re not active \u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEvery move you make is being tracked, so you feel uncomfortable, and you\u8217\'20\'19re not able to really communicate with your co-workers about the unsafe work environment you\u8217\'20\'19re in, or the inhumane working conditions because of the dangerous rates that are so high that we must meet quotas.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Taylor said she got involved with organizing at the warehouse after she was injured on the job at Amazon after tripping on an empty pallet and being told to return to work. Her own doctor {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.stlpr.org/economy-business/2023-08-03/st-peters-amazon-employees-file-osha-complaint-saying-work-conditions-caused-injuries"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 diagnosed}}}\uc2  her with a torn meniscus.\par \par \uc2 In 2023, she and several of her co-workers filed a complaint with Osha over safety concerns at the STL8 warehouse. Workers have also organized and submitted petitions to Amazon {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ksdk.com/article/money/business/amazon-st-peters-missouri-warehouse/63-b9b8d8bc-1c63-4400-828f-a09aa5df5ad5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 demanding}}}\uc2  clean drinking water and clean, breathable bathrooms at the warehouse.\par \par \uc2 Amazon is appealing a recent Osha {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.stltoday.com/news/local/business/osha-cites-st-peters-amazon-warehouse-as-federal-lawmakers-push-for-tighter-regulations/article_9d358b4c-08a2-11ef-b911-6780d8b15f27.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 citation}}}\uc2  issued at the warehouse for failing to report workplace injuries.\par \par \uc2 Taylor also recently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2024/05/02/senator-takes-aim-at-amazons-labor-practices-with-federal-quota-bill.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appeared}}}\uc2  in Washington DC as part of the introduction of a bill in the \uc2 US Senate\uc2 , the Warehouse Worker Protection Act, aimed at reining in productivity quotas at Amazon and other warehouse employers. Amazon has denied using fixed productivity quotas, rather than relying on various performance indicators.\par \par \uc2 Labor leaders and government officials have been calling for action to address the use of AI tools to monitor labor organizing activities, and the potential impacts of the technology on workers\u8217\'20\'19 rights.\par \par \uc2 The general counsel of the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  issued a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.law.georgetown.edu/poverty-journal/blog/labor-organizing-and-ai-surveillance-in-the-workplace/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 memo}}}\uc2  in 2022 announcing its intent to protect workers from artificial intelligence-enabled monitoring of labor organizing activities.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month in Europe, more than 20 leaders of labor unions representing more than 8 million workers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://uniglobalunion.org/news/amazon-surveillance-letter/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called}}}\uc2  for a crackdown on Amazon\u8217\'20\'19s surveillance of workers in the workplace by European data authorities.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWorkers have the right to talk to each other about their working conditions and share information with the intention of taking collective action,\u8221\'20\'1D Patel, of Stanford Law School, added. \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s what the \uc2 National Labor Relations\uc2  Act does and even those minimal but important rights are being majorly threatened, if not blatantly violated.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240521ek5l001ba\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
