\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Academic workers at UC Santa Cruz strike over crackdown on Gaza protests\b0\par\par\uc2 Dani Anguiano in Los Angeles \par \uc2 657 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 May 2024\par 19:48 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Union says response of University of California to pro-Palestine demonstrations violates rights of advocates and workers\par \par \uc2 Academic workers at the \uc2 University of California, Santa Cruz\uc2 , took to the picket line on Monday morning as part of a rolling strike in protest against the university system\u8217\'20\'19s response to pro-Palestine demonstrations.\par \par \uc2 The campus is the first in the University of California to do so as part of a systemwide protest against the public university, which union members argue violated the rights of pro-Palestinian advocates and workers.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 United Auto Workers (UAW) union\uc2 , which represents 48,000 graduate workers in California\u8217\'20\'19s vast university system, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/17/university-california-worker-strike-gaza-protester"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voted to authorize}}}\uc2  a strike last week. The union has accused the University of California of unfair labor practices, including allowing violent attacks on pro-Palestine protesters, summoning police to arrest union members participating in protests, and unilaterally changing working conditions, among other charges.\par \par \uc2 The strike is expected to cause widespread disruption within the University of California system, which has more than 280,000 students at its 10 campuses across the state.\par \par \uc2 Officials with the University of California have said the strike is illegal, violating their collective bargaining agreement, and has in turn filed an unfair labor practice charge against the union.\par \par \uc2 The action comes amid a huge wave of protests over the war in Gaza at universities across the US. In the last month, more than 3,000 people have been arrested on US college campuses as universities have cracked down on demonstrators and associated encampments with often militarized responses.\par \par \uc2 UC campuses have been the site of tense clashes, arrests and violence. In late April, a masked group of people marched on campus and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/may/01/ucla-campus-violence-protests"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 violently attacked}}}\uc2  pro-Palestine protesters as law enforcement looked on without intervening for hours. Days later police raided the Gaza solidarity encampment on campus and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/02/ucla-palestine-protests-encampment-arrests"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 arrested}}}\uc2  hundreds of people.\par \par \uc2 Last week at the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/16/campus-protest-encampment-uc-irvine-removed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 University of California, Irvine}}}\uc2 , police officers arrested 50 people as part of a crackdown on a pro-Palestine encampment and threatened students and faculty with batons and munitions.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COver the last two weeks UC has allowed appalling violence and intimidation against members of our academic community who exercised their right to protest,\u8221\'20\'1D Douglas Grion Filho, a union member at UC Santa Cruz, said in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/uaw_4811/status/1791512207563583777"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 video}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The union has described the university\u8217\'20\'19s actions as \u8220\'20\'1Cunlawful and unacceptable\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The university has said the union\u8217\'20\'19s demands are \u8220\'20\'1Cpolitical demands that are outside the terms of the collective bargaining agreement\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis strike is illegal,\u8221\'20\'1D Melissa Matella, the associate vice-president of systemwide labor relations, said in a statement. \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 UAW\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s decision to strike over non-labor issues violates the no-strike clause of their contracts with UC and sets a dangerous and far-reaching precedent that social, political and cultural issues \u8211\'20\'13 no matter how valid \u8211\'20\'13 that are not labor-related can support a labor strike.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The union has asked for amnesty for all academic employees, students, faculty and staff who face disciplinary action or arrest because of recent protests and divestment from weapons manufacturers and other companies profiting from the war in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 The union has opted for rolling strikes among the campuses, beginning at UC Santa Cruz, where there are roughly 2,000 members.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe ball is in UC\u8217\'20\'19s court \u8211\'20\'13 and the first step they need to take is dropping all criminal and disciplinary proceedings against our colleagues,\u8221\'20\'1D Rafael Jaime, the president of \uc2 UAW\uc2  4811, said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 While graduation season is in full swing, protests have continued to roil US universities. \uc2 Drexel University in Philadelphia\uc2  has remained on lockdown as protesters have ignored the campus president\u8217\'20\'19s request to disband a pro-Palestinian encampment.\par \par \uc2 The Drexel president, \uc2 John Fry\uc2 , described it as \u8220\'20\'1Cintolerably disruptive\u8221\'20\'1D. Protesters have accused the university and city police of harassment.\par \par \uc2 The Associated Press contributed to this report\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240520ek5k002s1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
