\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Blow to \uc2 UAW\uc2  as Mercedes workers in Alabama vote against unionization\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 758 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 May 2024\par 21:52 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Workers in Tuscaloosa vote against bid to unionize, as \uc2 UAW\uc2  president Shawn Fain hails impact of campaign despite defeat\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  has failed in its effort to unionize workers at two \uc2 Mercedes-Benz\uc2  plants in Tuscaloosa, Alabama, in a blow to the union\u8217\'20\'19s plans to build its membership in the southern states.\par \par \uc2 The loss on Friday comes amid the \uc2 UAW\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s ambitious union-organizing campaign to organize 150,000 non-union auto workers around the US.\par \par \uc2 In April the \uc2 UAW\uc2  won a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/19/volkswagen-unionize-uaw-tennessee?CMP=share_btn_url"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 landslide victory}}}\uc2  at the \uc2 Volkswagen\uc2  plant in Chattanooga, Tennessee, where 73% of workers voted to unionize.\par \par \uc2 The final vote was 2,642 against union representation and 2,045 for. Fifty-six per cent of workers voted no.\par \par \uc2 Southern states have for decades successfully fought off unionization drives in an attempt to keep down labor costs \u8211\'20\'13 a practice critics have called the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.instagram.com/uaw.union/p/C6txNYTsJ7g/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAlabama discount\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMercedes is a better place thanks to this campaign,\u8221\'20\'1D said Shawn Fain in a press conference after the results were announced. He cited the end of two-tier wages and a replacement of the chief executive as some of the successes workers won during the organizing campaign.\par \par \uc2 He said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe federal government and the \uc2 German government\uc2  are currently investigating Mercedes for the intimidation and harassment that they inflicted on their own workers, and we intend to follow that process.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 At Mercedes, the union faced significantly more aggressive opposition to worker organizing efforts than at \uc2 Volkswagen\uc2 , including from Republican elected officials and business groups that campaigned against the union vote.\par \par \uc2 David Johnston, a worker at the Mercedes battery plant since August 2022, said he jumped at the chance to work at Mercedes when he heard they were directly hiring.\par \par \uc2 But promises and claims that were made to him when he was hired became exposed as false or misleading, he said, such as workers never being forced to work Sundays, or the two-tier wage system, and unilateral changes made by the company.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey have changed their own handbook many times since I was originally hired, in just two years. They have also changed our schedules. My schedule personally has changed about six times since I was hired on,\u8221\'20\'1D said Johnston.\par \par \uc2 These factors and his previous experience working under a union contract inspired him to support the unionization effort, he said. Johnston said \uc2 Mercedes-Benz\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s attempt to dissuade workers from unionizing had only assisted workers\u8217\'20\'19 organizing efforts.\par \par \uc2 Mercedes-Benz\uc2  moved to head off the union drive by eliminating a two-tier wage system at the plants. That decision came after it was announced 30% of workers had signed union authorization cards.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat quite honestly backfired for the company. It really showed workers that they\u8217\'20\'19ve been listening to us the whole time, but did not care about us,\u8221\'20\'1D said Johnston. \u8220\'20\'1CIt wasn\u8217\'20\'19t until we decided that we wanted to union that the company even would respond to us.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis isn\u8217\'20\'19t political, regardless of what the governor wants to say. This isn\u8217\'20\'19t something that the \uc2 UAW\uc2  came down to us seeking us to join them. This was us going to them asking them to represent us, that we would be allowed to call the shots on how we organized, and this has been 100% worker-driven. The people that are going to unionize are the people that live in the south.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Now workers will push for a first union contract at \uc2 Volkswagen\uc2  as the \uc2 UAW\uc2  sets its sights on expanding their union wins in the auto industry. The \uc2 UAW\uc2  has so far announced reaching 30% thresholds of workers signing union authorization cards at a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://uaw.org/we-keep-toyota-running-workers-at-critical-toyota-plant-launch-campaign-to-join-the-uaw/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Toyota engine plant }}}\uc2  in Troy, Missouri, in March and at the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://alabamareflector.com/2024/05/14/at-montgomery-rally-hyundai-workers-describe-difficult-working-conditions/#:~:text=UAW%20said%20in%20February%20that,faced%20push%20back%20from%20management."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Hyundai plant}}}\uc2  in Montgomery, Alabama, in February.\par \par \uc2 Sharon Block, a law professor at Harvard Law School and former \uc2 NLRB\uc2  official, said: \u8220\'20\'1CThere are legal avenues open to the \uc2 UAW\uc2  to challenge the outcome.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs Mercedes\u8217\'20\'19 anti-union campaign ramped up, the \uc2 UAW\uc2  filed a number of unfair labor practice charges with the \uc2 NLRB\uc2 , alleging that Mercedes crossed the line from strongarm to unlawful tactics in the plants. In addition, there is an investigation under way into whether Mercedes violated German law by undertaking such an aggressive anti-union campaign in the US.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for \uc2 Mercedes-Benz\uc2  said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe look forward to continuing to work directly with our team members to ensure MBUSI is not only their employer of choice, but a place they would recommend to friends and family.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240517ek5h0030e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
