\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Graduate workers in California to strike over treatment of Gaza protesters\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 524 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 May 2024\par 18:21 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Widespread disruption expected after workers vote to hold series of strikes, starting Monday with UC Santa Cruz\par \par \uc2 California\u8217\'20\'19s huge university system is facing widespread disruption after workers voted to hold a series of strikes in protest of its treatment of Gaza protesters.\par \par \uc2 The University of California (UC) has more than 280,000 students and 227,000 faculty and staff on campuses across the state.\par \par \uc2 Members of the \uc2 United Auto Workers (UAW)\uc2 , which represents 48,000 graduate workers throughout the system, voted to authorize a strike on Wednesday. On Friday, the union {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://x.com/uaw_4811/status/1791512269077254277"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called}}}\uc2  on graduate workers at UC Santa Cruz to walk off the job on Monday. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://lookout.co/ucsc-grad-student-workers-among-those-voting-on-strike-over-palestine-encampment-crackdowns/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 About 2,000 graduate workers}}}\uc2  are represented by the union at UC Santa Cruz.\par \par \uc2 The vote was called in response to charges of unfair labor practices filed against universities over their response to Gaza protests where union members were attacked by counter-protesters and police.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/01/uaw-ceasefire-gaza"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 UAW called}}}\uc2  for a ceasefire in Gaza in December. Best known for its representation of auto workers, the \uc2 UAW\uc2  is planning to engage in a series of \u8220\'20\'1Cstand up\u8221\'20\'1D strikes where the union\u8217\'20\'19s executive board will call on campuses to strike on a rolling basis. The tactic was used in the \uc2 UAW\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/30/uaw-contract-gm-strike-end-update"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 successful strike}}}\uc2  against the big three US automakers late last year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAt the heart of this is our right to free speech and peaceful protest,\u8221\'20\'1D said Rafael Jaime, a graduate worker in the English department at the \uc2 University of California at Los Angeles\uc2  (UCLA) and president of \uc2 UAW\uc2  4811.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf members of the academic community are maced and beaten down for peacefully demonstrating on this issue, our ability to speak up on all issues is threatened. As days pass with no remedies for UC\u8217\'20\'19s unfair labor practices, academic workers on more and more campuses are preparing to stand up to demand that our rights to free speech, protest and collective action be respected.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Graduate workers at UCLA, the \uc2 University of Southern California\uc2 , the \uc2 University of California at San Diego\uc2 , Brown University and \uc2 Harvard University\uc2  have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/article/2024/may/02/university-of-california-union-strike-vote-gaza-protests"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed}}}\uc2  unfair labor practice charges with the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  over how their university administrations unilaterally changed policies and responded to Gaza protests.\par \par \uc2 According to the union, UC Riverside and \uc2 UC Berkeley\uc2  have been negotiating with protesters over their demands for transparency on university investments and divestment from Israel and weapons contractors and manufacturers contributing to the war in Gaza. The union is also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.uaw4811.org/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 demanding}}}\uc2  amnesty for all academic workers who face disciplinary action and arrest for participating in the protests.\par \par \uc2 The University of California administration has claimed the strikes are illegal despite the union classifying them as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nlrb.gov/strikes#:~:text=A%20strike%20may%20be%20unlawful,strike%20for%20an%20unlawful%20object."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unfair labor practice strikes}}}\uc2  that are protected activity.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe University strongly disagrees with the \uc2 UAW\uc2  that any exception to this general rule applies and strongly believes that the action is an unlawful strike,\u8221\'20\'1D stated the administration in response to the strike vote. \u8220\'20\'1CIn response to an unlawful strike, the University will take action with the Public Employment Relations Board (PERB) to assert that the strike is unlawful.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240517ek5h002pc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
