\par\par \uc2 Technology\par \b \uc2 Apple\uc2  store workers vote to authorize first strike over bargaining delays\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 722 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 May 2024\par 01:15 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Maryland employees at first US Apple store to unionize take historic step as progress for a first contract has stagnated\par \par \uc2 Workers at the first \uc2 Apple\uc2  store in the US to have unionized, in Towson, Maryland, have voted to authorize a strike as progress in bargaining for a first contract has stagnated.\par \par \uc2 They could be the first \uc2 Apple\uc2  retail store workers to ever go on strike.\par \par \uc2 International Association of Machinists and Aerospace Workers\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 (IAM) Coalition of Organized Retail Employees (IAM Core) represents 100 workers at the \uc2 Apple\uc2  store who had their union election win certified in May 2022. They are one of two \uc2 Apple\uc2  stores in the US to have successfully unionized, the other being a location in Oklahoma City.\par \par \uc2 David DiMaria, the machinists union\u8217\'20\'19s lead organizer at the Towson Apple store, said the strike authorization vote is the first step in the process before a strike sanction vote.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have more bargaining dates coming up,\u8221\'20\'1D said DiMaria. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re going to go to the table. We\u8217\'20\'19re hoping the company will bargain in good faith, but frankly what we\u8217\'20\'19ve seen over the past year or so is that they really haven\u8217\'20\'19t been, and we filed charges based on that they\u8217\'20\'19re not living up to their obligation under federal law to bargain in good faith with the union.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 DiMaria said the union is hoping \uc2 Apple\uc2  will follow federal labor law and live up to its own code of conduct corporate policies, and that over the past year of bargaining there hasn\u8217\'20\'19t been much progress on key issues for a first contract.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this year, the union conducted a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.goiam.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/02/Worker%E2%80%99s-Rights-Assessment-Response.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 survey}}}\uc2  of \uc2 Apple\uc2  workers in response to the company\u8217\'20\'19s workers\u8217\'20\'19 rights assessment, where workers alleged the company has retaliated against workers for trying to unionize and has requested \uc2 Apple\uc2  sever its relationship with union avoidance consultants.\par \par \uc2 All we\u8217\'20\'19re asking for is to follow the law\par \par \uc2 David DiMaria\par \par \uc2 Workers are pushing for higher wages, improvements to work-life balance, and fair scheduling practices in a first contract, while {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.goiam.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/IMG_1881.jpeg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tentative agreements}}}\uc2  have been reached on several other issues.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Apple\uc2  has a certain image, they have a supplier code of conduct that recognizes employees rights to organize, they have their own human rights code of conduct. And their behavior is just completely a 180 of what they purport to say their policy practice. So they\u8217\'20\'19re really not living up to their credo, their policies, their code of conduct. It\u8217\'20\'19s just, it\u8217\'20\'19s really disappointing,\u8221\'20\'1D added DiMaria.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis really now rests with the board of directors. If \uc2 Apple\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s not going to do the right thing, it\u8217\'20\'19s because the board of directors of this company have not put pressure on the CEO to actually just follow the law. And that\u8217\'20\'19s really all we\u8217\'20\'19re asking for is to follow the law.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Amid, an uptick in union organizing efforts among its workers, \uc2 Apple\uc2  has faced numerous allegations of unfair labor practice charges filed with the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  over its union opposition.\par \par \uc2 Four unfair labor practice charges are currently pending before administrative law judges after \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  (\uc2 NLRB\uc2 ) regional offices issued complaints finding merit in the charges. One of the complaints, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nlrb.gov/case/05-CA-306442"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 issued}}}\uc2  in November, stems from the Towson store, alleging \uc2 Apple\uc2  provided benefits to non-union workers while withholding them from union members at the store.\par \par \uc2 Four {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nlrb.gov/case/14-CA-285708"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 settlements}}}\uc2  covering five unfair labor practice charges have been reached with \uc2 Apple\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 On 6 May, the \uc2 NLRB{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nlrb.gov/case/02-CA-295979"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 upheld}}}\uc2  an administrative judge ruling that found \uc2 Apple\uc2  unlawfully interrogate workers and confiscated and prohibited union flyers at the World Trade Center Apple store location.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAt \uc2 Apple\uc2 , we work hard to provide an excellent experience for our retail team members and empower them to deliver exceptional service for our customers. We deeply value our team members and we\u8217\'20\'19re proud to provide them with industry-leading compensation and exceptional benefits. As always, we will engage with the union representing our team in Towson respectfully and in good faith,\u8221\'20\'1D said an \uc2 Apple\uc2  spokesperson on the strike vote.\par \par \uc2 They added on the unfair labor practice charges and \uc2 NLRB\uc2  complaint issued in November 2023: \u8220\'20\'1CWe strongly deny these claims and look forward to providing the full set of facts to the \uc2 NLRB\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240515ek5f00109\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
