\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Mercedes workers in Alabama face anti-union message \u8216\'20\'18barrage\u8217\'20\'19 before election\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 785 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 May 2024\par 10:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 United Auto Workers union\uc2  sees two of German-owned carmaker\u8217\'20\'19s plants as key in effort to unionize industry in southern US\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 United Auto Workers (UAW) union\uc2  is setting its sights on its next big union victory in the south, at two \uc2 Mercedes-Benz\uc2  plants in Vance and Woodstock, Alabama.\par \par \uc2 Coming off the historic union election win at the \uc2 Volkswagen\uc2  plant in Chattanooga, Tennessee, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/business/autos-transportation/mercedes-benz-workers-vote-uaw-membership-may-2024-04-18/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 5,200 workers}}}\uc2  are to begin voting in their union election from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://uaw.org/the-time-is-now-mercedes-workers-in-alabama-to-vote-for-union-may-13-17/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 13 May to 17 May}}}\uc2 . The \uc2 UAW\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s recent win at \uc2 Volkswagen\uc2  to represent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.bloomberglaw.com/bloomberg-law-analysis/volkswagen-election-was-labors-biggest-factory-flip-in-16-years"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  about 4,300 workers}}}\uc2  was one of the biggest union election wins in manufacturing in the past 16 years.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s just time for a change,\u8221\'20\'1D said Kay Finklea, a quality inspector who has worked at the \uc2 Mercedes-Benz\uc2  plant for 23 years.\par \par \uc2 Finklea said that the pay, benefits, and work hours had stagnated or worsened since she started and the balance between work and life had deteriorated.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey say we\u8217\'20\'19re supposed to work 10 hours a day, but they actually work us 12 hours a day, so by the time you get home, you\u8217\'20\'19re exhausted, beat, and you don\u8217\'20\'19t have time to do anything but get a quick bite, shower and lay down to get ready to wake up and do it all over again,\u8221\'20\'1D Finklea added.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMy thing is let\u8217\'20\'19s give ourselves a chance, let\u8217\'20\'19s invest in us, let\u8217\'20\'19s form our union and work to try to make things better for everybody.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UAW\uc2  has aimed its union-organizing effort at eliminating the \u8220\'20\'1CAlabama discount\u8221\'20\'1D, part of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/publication/rooted-racism-part1/?mc_cid=9f4d28fdab&mc_eid=131a3ffbe6"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 economic development model}}}\uc2  in the US south in which wages are kept lower than the rest of the US.\par \par \uc2 The union has highlighted the differences between the stagnant pay for workers and the immense profits of the automakers and the exorbitant salaries of executives.\par \par \uc2 Mercedes-Benz\uc2  has made $156bn in profits over the last decade and profits grew 200% in the past three years, according to the \uc2 UAW\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://uaw.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/Closing-Argument-v5a-FINAL.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Top wages}}}\uc2  at Mercedes, which vary based on seniority and department, currently lag behind the hourly wage gains the \uc2 UAW\uc2  won at the big three domestic automakers in late 2023.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UAW\uc2  has also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://uaw.org/living-large-at-mercedes-new-uaw-video-exposes-staggering-ceo-pay-at-mercedes-ahead-of-alabama-plant-union-vote/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 noted}}}\uc2  it would take two years for a production worker at top pay to make what a \uc2 Mercedes-Benz\uc2  executive makes in a week. \uc2 Mercedes-Benz\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s management board members gave themselves a 78% pay increase in 2023.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Mercedes-Benz\uc2  union election is the \uc2 UAW\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s second big test in the southern US. The union launched an organizing drive aimed at unionizing 150,000 autoworkers at non-union plants in the US after winning {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/uaw-strike-2023"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 historic gains}}}\uc2  in their contracts at \uc2 General Motors\uc2 , \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  and Ford last November.\par \par \uc2 Those gains won after a high-profile \u8220\'20\'1Cstand-up strike\u8221\'20\'1D incited significant support for unionizing among other autoworkers.\par \par \uc2 Rick Webster, who started working at the plant for a contractor in 2016 but officially began working for Mercedes in October 2022, said: \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s time for Alabama workers to stand up and unite not just at Mercedes, but at Hyundai, \uc2 Honda\uc2  and \uc2 Toyota\uc2 . It\u8217\'20\'19s time for everybody to stand up and have a voice and we need to end the Alabama discount.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Webster said that since the union drive had gone public, Mercedes management had inundated workers with texts, emails, messages and meetings urging workers to vote no in the union election. Local elected officials and business groups, including the Republican governor of Alabama, \uc2 Kay Ivey\uc2 , have vehemently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GovernorKayIvey/status/1783546603795628221"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 opposed}}}\uc2  the \uc2 UAW\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s organizing efforts.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UAW\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://uaw.org/uaw-files-charges-in-germany-against-mercedes-benz-companys-anti-union-campaign-against-u-s-autoworkers-violates-new-german-law-on-global-supply-chain-practices/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed}}}\uc2  several unfair labor practice charges against \uc2 Mercedes-Benz\uc2  over the company\u8217\'20\'19s opposition to the union campaign, including filing charges in Germany, where the company is headquartered.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt is a daily barrage of text messages, emails, and there\u8217\'20\'19s an app we have for work for every kind of announcement you can think of and we\u8217\'20\'19re getting two to three notifications daily. Every day before the shift, we have to sit in the team room and watch anti-union videos,\u8221\'20\'1D said Webster. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s just been a constant barrage. Everybody is just sick and tired of it.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Mercedes-Benz\uc2  has denied allegations of labor law violations but has openly opposed the unionization effort.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CMBUSI [Mercedes-Benz US International] fully respects our team members\u8217\'20\'19 choice whether to unionize and we look forward to participating in the election process to ensure every Team Member has a chance to cast their own secret-ballot vote, as well as having access to the information necessary to make an informed choice,\u8221\'20\'1D a \uc2 Mercedes-Benz\uc2  spokesperson said in an email.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240513ek5d001be\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
