\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Union plans strike vote over crackdown on University of California Gaza protests\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 1,049 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 May 2024\par 11:49 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 UAW\uc2  Local 4811, largest union of academic workers, also says it will file unfair labor charges over university use of \uc2 LAPD\uc2  on protesters\par \par \uc2 The largest union of academic workers, which represents more than 48,000 graduate student workers throughout the University of California system, will hold a strike authorization vote as early as next week in response to how universities have cracked down on students\u8217\'20\'19 Gaza protests.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe use and sanction of violent force to curtail peaceful protest is an attack on free speech and the right to demand change, and the university must sit down with students, unions, and campus organizations to negotiate, rather than escalate,\u8221\'20\'1D read an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.uaw4811.org/updates/strike-authorization-vote-announcement"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announcement}}}\uc2  of the strike vote from \uc2 UAW\uc2  local 4811.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this year, the union voted by a margin of more than nine to one in favor of supporting a ceasefire, according to the announcement.\par \par \uc2 Graduate workers last {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/dec/10/university-of-california-strike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 went on strike}}}\uc2  in November 2022 over a new union contract; it was the largest strike in US higher education history. They recently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://uaw5810.org/2024/03/01/we-are-officially-one-big-union-uaw-4811/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 merged}}}\uc2  two \uc2 UAW\uc2  locals, 2865 and 5810, under the single \uc2 UAW\uc2  local 4811.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe have been calling on the University of California to de-escalate and negotiate with the protesters over their very urgent and moral concerns and it failed to do that and it failed to protect students and workers and allowed this violence to occur,\u8221\'20\'1D Rafael Jaime, co-president of \uc2 UAW\uc2  4811 and a graduate worker at UCLA, said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re holding a strike authorization vote to hold the university accountable and demand the university respect the members\u8217\'20\'19 right to protected speech and right to protest.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 He said the union also plans to file unfair labor practice charges against the University of California over the university\u8217\'20\'19s use of the Los Angeles police department (\uc2 LAPD\uc2 ) against protesters, and for changing policies unilaterally in response to the protests without bargaining.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis is the defining issue of our generation, and it\u8217\'20\'19s really important for all, not just workers at the University of California, but across the entire nation, to speak up and to ensure every worker has the right to speak on this issue,\u8221\'20\'1D added Jaime.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe believe all workers, all students, have a fundamental right to engage in protests and engage in free speech, and universities need to respect that right.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 United Auto Workers union\uc2 , with 400,000 active members and over 500,000 retirees, is the largest US union to call for a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/01/uaw-ceasefire-gaza#:~:text=The%20UAW%20is%20now%20the,more%20than%20580%2C000%20retired%20workers."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ceasefire}}}\uc2  in Gaza, which they did in December.\par \par \uc2 UAW\uc2  president Shawn Fain recently reaffirmed the union\u8217\'20\'19s position. \u8220\'20\'1COur union has been calling for a ceasefire for six months. This war is wrong and this response against students and academic workers, many of them \uc2 UAW\uc2  members, is wrong,\u8221\'20\'1D Fain said in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://uaw.org/comment-from-uaw-president-shawn-fain-on-mass-arrests-of-anti-war-protestors/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2  on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Graduate student workers are also calling on the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  to weigh in on how universities have responded to pro-Palestinian protests, and whether those responses violate US labor laws and collective bargaining agreements.\par \par \uc2 The Graduate Labor Organization at Brown University has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.browndailyherald.com/article/2024/03/glo-files-federal-labor-complaint-against-university-alleges-retaliatory-threat"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed }}}\uc2  several unfair labor practice charges against the university in regards to pro-Palestinian protests and the university\u8217\'20\'19s responses to them.\par \par \uc2 Forty-one students at Brown were arrested, and charges remain, despite the pro-Palestinian encampment dispersing as part of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.browndailyherald.com/article/2024/04/brown-university-to-vote-on-divestment-at-october-corporation-meeting-encampment-to-be-voluntarily-cleared"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 negotiations}}}\uc2  that include a planned vote by the university\u8217\'20\'19s highest governing body for October on divesting from companies affiliated with Israel. The charges filed by the union allege that Brown unilaterally changed protest policies without bargaining, and made threats of retaliation toward union members for participating in pro-Palestine campus protests.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s really about the university trying to leverage this fact that, as graduate workers, we do have student status, and kind of using that as a workaround for violating labor law. This has been their playbook on a whole host of issues,\u8221\'20\'1D said Michael Ziegler, political director of the Graduate Labor Organization and graduate worker at Brown.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn the past five years, we\u8217\'20\'19ve had something like 20 protests on the main green, and there was never any issue \u8211\'20\'13 the university didn\u8217\'20\'19t take these actions. This is new, and I think a dangerous attempt by them to clamp down on the rights of speech and protected concerted action.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 UAW\uc2  local 872, which represents around 3,000 graduate workers at the \uc2 University of Southern California\uc2 , has recently filed an unfair labor practice charge against the university over arrests of at least five union members. The union has called for charges to be dropped against all 93 protesters who were arrested on 24 April, and for the university to accede to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.uscannenbergmedia.com/2024/04/25/usc-divest-from-death-coalition-reiterates-goals-of-alumni-park-occupation/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 demands}}}\uc2  from USC Divest from Death Coalition.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUSC\u8217\'20\'19s summoning of \uc2 LAPD\uc2  riot police to arrest their own students and workers for peacefully demonstrating is abhorrent and wrong,\u8221\'20\'1D said Maile McCann, a local 872 member and PhD candidate in the civil engineering department at USC.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe administration\u8217\'20\'19s actions show an alarming disregard for our right as students and union members to engage in peaceful demonstrations, and their decisions have put international students in particular at serious risk. USC\u8217\'20\'19s unnecessary escalation has resulted in a shameful waste of public resources for the purposes of silencing dissent.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for USC said in an email: \u8220\'20\'1CWe believe the charge is without merit, and [we] intend to defend our position before the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for Brown University said in response to the unfair labor practice charges, \u8220\'20\'1Cindividuals are not absolved from abiding by Brown policies by virtue of union membership.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe University of California is deeply alarmed, concerned and disappointed that our \uc2 UAW\uc2 -represented academic employees would choose this moment of crisis to take a vote to engage in an unlawful work stoppage. UC values these employees and asks them to join it in supporting our communities at this time,\u8221\'20\'1D a spokesperson for the University of California system said in an email. \u8220\'20\'1CThere is no basis under the contract or the law for \uc2 UAW\uc2  to engage in a work stoppage. Further, given the vulnerable status of our communities at this moment, a strike vote by \uc2 UAW\uc2  is essentially a vote to take advantage of and exploit this complex and impactful situation.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240502ek52003h2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
