\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 He led a strike at \uc2 Kellogg\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s. Now he\u8217\'20\'19s aiming for a Nebraska Senate seat\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 712 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 April 2024\par 16:25 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Dan Osborn is challenging incumbent \uc2 Deb Fischer\uc2  in a \u8216\'20\'18long shot\u8217\'20\'19 bid to prove the state still has an \u8216\'20\'18independent spirit\u8217\'20\'19\par \par \uc2 Pennsylvania, Wisconsin, Arizona, Georgia and Nevada \u8211\'20\'13 these are the swing states most pundits expect will decide the 2024 election. No one has deep-red Nebraska on that list. But a 48-year-old pipefitter and union organizer from Omaha is hoping to change that.\par \par \uc2 Three years ago, Dan Osborn led the Nebraska leg of a US-wide {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2021/oct/07/kelloggs-workers-strike-offshore-jobs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 strike against}}}\uc2  the cereal giant \uc2 Kellogg\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s as the company pushed for concessions in a new union contract despite posting record profits during the Covid-19 pandemic.\par \par \uc2 Now he\u8217\'20\'19s taking on \uc2 Deb Fischer\uc2 , a Republican senator, who is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ballotpedia.org/United_States_Senate_election_in_Nebraska,_2024"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 running}}}\uc2  for her third \uc2 US Senate\uc2  term in a state that hasn\u8217\'20\'19t elected a Democrat to the Senate in 18 years. Osborn is running as an independent and says he hasn\u8217\'20\'19t yet decided who will get his vote come November but his pro-labor, pro-choice views are unlikely to sit well with conservative Republicans.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis from the beginning was considered a long shot,\u8221\'20\'1D said Osborn. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19ve enjoyed proving people wrong from the very beginning of this and I look forward to continue proving people wrong, that this isn\u8217\'20\'19t impossible. I want to show that Nebraska has an independent spirit.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Nebraska is historically a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ballotpedia.org/Party_control_of_Nebraska_state_government"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stronghold}}}\uc2  for Republicans. A Democrat has not won a \uc2 US Senate\uc2  seat to represent the state since Ben Nelson in 2001. An independent hasn\u8217\'20\'19t won since George Norris in 1936.\par \par \uc2 Despite the odds, Osborn\u8217\'20\'19s campaign is off to an impressive start. A November 2023 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://projects.fivethirtyeight.com/polls/senate/2024/nebraska/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poll}}}\uc2 , the only one conducted so far for the race, put Osborn at 40% to 38% for Fischer, with 18% undecided. Osborn has also fundraised {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.norfolkneradio.com/news/osborn-boasts-record-fundraising-numbers/article_10d5311e-f75b-11ee-8178-db74ee7d73fe.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than $600,000 so far}}}\uc2 , a record for an independent candidate in the state, primarily from small donors.\par \par \uc2 Osborn said he was approached to run by railroad workers in Nebraska who have been disgruntled with Fischer over {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ksnblocal4.com/2024/04/19/omaha-man-running-sen-deb-fischers-seat/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 her refusal}}}\uc2  to support the Railroad Safety Act.\par \par \uc2 The bill was drafted in response to the East Palestine, Ohio, disaster as railroad workers and unions have decried poor working conditions and safety issues driven by railroad corporations, which Osborn has pointed out are big donors to his opponent. In contrast, Fischer had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.desmog.com/2017/07/25/senator-backed-rail-companies-introduces-new-bill-would-de-regulate-rail-industry/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 introduced}}}\uc2  legislation to further deregulate the railroad industry.\par \par \uc2 Improving railroad safety is a part of Osborn\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://osbornforsenate.com/platform/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 campaign platform}}}\uc2 , along with cannabis legalization, enacting congressional term limits, lowering tax rates for small business owners and the middle class, and improving pay and support for veterans.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re dealing with people like \uc2 Deb Fischer\uc2  who take corporate Pac money and they vote accordingly,\u8221\'20\'1D added Osborn. \u8220\'20\'1CThey are not for the workers, for the people, they\u8217\'20\'19re for corporations.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 His former employer \uc2 Kellogg\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s has also hit the headlines, with \uc2 Kellogg\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s CEO, \uc2 Gary Pilnick\uc2 , stating {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/feb/27/kelloggs-ceo-cereal-for-dinner"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 during an appearance }}}\uc2  on CNBC that poor families facing financial distress should consider eating cereal for dinner.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis just goes to show how out of touch CEOs are with regular people,\u8221\'20\'1D said Osborn.\par \par \uc2 Osborn is a long shot for Nebraska but he\u8217\'20\'19s hoping that his story will resonate with people who are fed up with business as usual and a 1% that seem to think \u8220\'20\'1Clet them eat cereal\u8221\'20\'1D is an answer to income inequality. He cited a 2020 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://time.com/5888024/50-trillion-income-inequality-america/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 report}}}\uc2  that calculated the redistribution of wealth in the US from the bottom 90% of earners to the top 1% of earners, finding that $50tn has been taken in redistributed income in recent decades.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHow does that happen on everybody\u8217\'20\'19s watch? It\u8217\'20\'19s because the special interests and corporations own the politicians and they vote accordingly,\u8221\'20\'1D concluded Osborn. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m tired of it and I think people are starting to wake up to that fact because we\u8217\'20\'19re all hurting right now. I\u8217\'20\'19m hurting. I\u8217\'20\'19m still working 40-50 hours as a steamfitter while I\u8217\'20\'19m running for Senate and my dollar doesn\u8217\'20\'19t stretch like it used to, I\u8217\'20\'19m getting hurt at the gas pump, I\u8217\'20\'19m getting hurt at the grocery stores and everybody else is too.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240429ek4t001xl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
