\par\par \uc2 Technology\par \b \uc2 Workers accuse \uc2 Google\uc2  of \u8216\'20\'18tantrum\u8217\'20\'19 after 50 fired over Israel contract protest\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 974 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 April 2024\par 11:16 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Tech giant fired number of people who protested against $1.2bn Project Nimbus, which supports Israeli military and government\par \par \uc2 Google\uc2  has been accused of throwing a \u8220\'20\'1Ctantrum\u8221\'20\'1D after sacking more than 50 workers in response to a protest over the company\u8217\'20\'19s military ties to the Israeli government \u8211\'20\'13 firings that have shone a light on a controversial project and long-simmering tensions between staff and management.\par \par \uc2 The workers were sacked following protests at \uc2 Google\uc2  offices in New York City and Sunnyvale, California, organized by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.notechforapartheid.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 No Tech for Apartheid}}}\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 an alliance of \uc2 Google\uc2  and \uc2 Amazon\uc2  workers who have been protesting against a $1.2bn contract with the Israeli government called {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2021/oct/12/google-amazon-workers-condemn-project-nimbus-israeli-military-contract"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Project Nimbus}}}\uc2  that they claim will make it \u8220\'20\'1Ceasier for the Israeli government to surveil Palestinians and force them off their land\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Initially, \uc2 Google{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usatoday.com/story/tech/2024/04/23/google-firings-pro-palestinian-protests-cloud-computing/73427928007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fired}}}\uc2  28 workers over the protests and then fired more than 20 workers a few days later.\par \par \uc2 The firings are the largest to occur since Israel\u8217\'20\'19s military campaign in response to the 7 October 2023 terrorist attack by \uc2 Hamas\uc2  in which about 1,200 people were killed and more than 200 hostages were taken. Since then, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ohchr.org/en/press-releases/2024/04/un-human-rights-chief-deplores-harrowing-killings-children-and-women-rafah"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more than 34,000 Palestinians}}}\uc2  have been killed in Gaza, including more than 14,000 children and 9,670 women.\par \par \uc2 Google\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cio.com/article/220027/google-workers-hold-sit-in-to-protest-retaliation.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fired and reprimanded}}}\uc2  workers for participating in protests before, such as over a 2018 walkout and sit-in protest about sexual harassment issues at the company, but not previously to this extent. In March, \uc2 Google{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2024/03/08/google-fires-employee-who-protested-israel-tech-event-shuts-forum.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fired}}}\uc2  a cloud engineer who protested against an Israel tech event in New York City.\par \par \uc2 Emaan Haseem, a software engineer at \uc2 Google\uc2  and organizer with No Tech for Apartheid, was one of the fired workers. \u8220\'20\'1CMany of us had just recently gotten promoted. I was the fastest promoted person underneath my manager,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 This was a peaceful protest, she said, \u8220\'20\'1Cwith high visibility, high transparency, that we {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/NoTechApartheid/status/1780278895058518468"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 livestreamed}}}\uc2 . Everything and everybody could see how it went.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Haseem said the sit-in protests were a response to \uc2 Google\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s refusal to engage with workers\u8217\'20\'19 concerns.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLook at the way \uc2 Google\uc2  has overreacted, so emotionally, and has lashed out at 50 workers over this contract rather than giving any more transparency, clarity, or attempting to prove they are not especially providing the Israeli military resources to aid and abet their genocide and continue their apartheid,\u8221\'20\'1D added Haseem. \u8220\'20\'1CThey fully had the option to do that but instead they chose to throw a tantrum and take it out on 50 workers, many of whom were not involved in the sit-in.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt was done so emotionally, so irrationally, that \uc2 Google\uc2  has also taken its mask off in the process. It has shown its honest and true self, how contradictory they are, how they don\u8217\'20\'19t actually care about doing the right thing, about not being evil, about their values where we should speak up and speak out against anything wrong that we see happening in our work or in the workplace.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Since the contract was awarded in 2021, workers at \uc2 Google\uc2  and \uc2 Amazon\uc2  have been organizing in opposition to the corporations\u8217\'20\'19 joint contract with the Israeli military and government.\par \par \uc2 The $1.2bn contract to provide cloud services \u8220\'20\'1Callows for further surveillance of and unlawful data collection on Palestinians, and facilitates expansion of Israel\u8217\'20\'19s illegal settlements on Palestinian land\u8221\'20\'1D, according to an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2021/oct/12/google-amazon-workers-condemn-project-nimbus-israeli-military-contract"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 op-ed}}}\uc2  workers wrote in 2021.\par \par \uc2 The firings have disrupted the financial stability of workers, Haseem said, but she and others affected have received significant support from co-workers and others. She also said that one of the biggest challenges with the campaign against Project Nimbus was outreach and educating others on the issues \u8211\'20\'13 something which \uc2 Google\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s firings had only facilitated.\par \par \uc2 Hasan Ibraheem, a \uc2 Google\uc2  software engineer in New York who was fired and arrested for participating in the protest, said he and other workers were put on administrative leave, losing corporate access, and then fired the next day by email en masse.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe don\u8217\'20\'19t know of anyone who had actually been reached out to by HR. We were asked no questions. There was no consulting with us. No one asked us anything. It was just a very cold mass email sent out, you are now fired, goodbye, because they don\u8217\'20\'19t want to deal with us, they want to silence us and we\u8217\'20\'19re not going to stay silent,\u8221\'20\'1D said Ibraheem. \u8220\'20\'1CWe don\u8217\'20\'19t want our labor to be used for aiding a genocide and that\u8217\'20\'19s why we did that action and we are going to continue fighting to have this project dropped.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The workers declined to comment on any potential legal proceedings they may pursue in response to the firings. No Tech for Apartheid called the firings \u8220\'20\'1Cillegal\u8221\'20\'1D in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://medium.com/@notechforapartheid/statement-from-google-workers-with-the-no-tech-for-apartheid-campaign-on-googles-indiscriminate-28ba4c9b7ce8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 blogpost}}}\uc2  in response to \uc2 Google\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s actions.\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for \uc2 Google\uc2  said in an email on the firings: \u8220\'20\'1CWe continued our investigation into the physical disruption inside our buildings on April 16, looking at additional details provided by coworkers who were physically disrupted, as well as those employees who took longer to identify because their identity was partly concealed \u8211\'20\'13 like by wearing a mask without their badge \u8211\'20\'13 while engaged in the disruption. Our investigation into these events is now concluded, and we have terminated the employment of additional employees who were found to have been directly involved in disruptive activity.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 They denied firing any employees not involved. \uc2 Google\uc2  also denied protesters\u8217\'20\'19 characterizations of Project Nimbus, stating: \u8220\'20\'1CWe have been very clear that the Nimbus contract is for workloads running on our commercial cloud by Israeli government ministries, who agree to comply with our {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cloud.google.com/terms"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Terms of Service}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cloud.google.com/terms/aup"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Acceptable Use Policy}}}\uc2 . This work is not directed at highly sensitive, classified, or military workloads relevant to weapons or intelligence services.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240427ek4r000xh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
