\par\par \uc2 Technology\par \b \uc2 GMB launches legal action against \u8216\'20\'18out of control\u8217\'20\'19 \uc2 Amazon\uc2  at Coventry warehouse\b0\par\par\uc2 Heather Stewart \par \uc2 625 \uc2 words\par \uc2 26 April 2024\par 12:11 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par 40\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Employment tribunal sought over claims firm tried to induce workers to leave union in long-running row\par \par \uc2 The GMB is taking legal action against \uc2 Amazon\uc2  in the long-running battle for recognition at its Coventry warehouse, accusing the US firm of trying to \u8220\'20\'1Cinduce\u8221\'20\'1D staff to leave the union.\par \par \uc2 An employment tribunal claim is being lodged on behalf of five workers at the large site, known as BHX4.\par \par \uc2 The GMB cites practices including anti-union messages appearing on message boards, and workers being called into meetings lasting an hour or more, at which they claim managers are critical of unions.\par \par \uc2 They say QR codes have also been displayed around the building, which, when scanned by a staff member, automatically generate an email to the GMB\u8217\'20\'19s membership department, cancelling their membership.\par \par \uc2 Amanda Gearing, a GMB senior organiser, said: \u8220\'20\'1CThis is a company out of control. \uc2 Amazon\uc2  is a multibillion-pound corporation, doing everything in its power to stop minimum wage workers from forming a union.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Under the Trade Union and Labour Relations (Consolidation) Act 1992, it is unlawful for an employer to make an offer to a worker, \u8220\'20\'1Cfor the sole or main purpose of inducing the worker not to be or seek to become a member of an independent trade union\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Lawyers working with the GMB believe the presence of the QR codes may constitute such an offer.\par \par \uc2 Rosa Curling, a director of Foxglove Legal, which is involved in the case, said workers had been \u8220\'20\'1Chustled into anti-union propaganda seminars, then have a QR code shoved in their face that terminates their membership with just one click to quit. If only it was so easy to quit \uc2 Amazon\uc2  Prime!\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Paul Nowak, the general secretary of the TUC, said: \u8220\'20\'1CGood employers recognise the value of unions. But \uc2 Amazon\uc2  is throwing everything at trying to stop workers from organising for better pay and conditions and from having an independent voice at work.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIts union-busting tactics should have no place in Britain, and are further proof of why Labour\u8217\'20\'19s new deal for working people is so badly needed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 An \uc2 Amazon\uc2  spokesperson said: \u8220\'20\'1COur employees have the choice of whether or not to join a union. They always have.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe regularly review our pay to ensure we offer competitive wages and benefits. Our minimum starting pay has increased to \u163\'00\'A312.30 and \u163\'00\'A313 per hour depending on location, that\u8217\'20\'19s a 20% increase over two years and 50% since 2018. We also work hard to provide great benefits, a positive work environment and excellent career opportunities.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The tribunal case underlines the fraught relationship between unions and management, as they prepare for a legally binding ballot on union recognition at the site.\par \par \uc2 The independent watchdog the Central Arbitration Committee {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2024/apr/19/amazon-uk-recognise-union-gmb-ballot-coventry-warehouse"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 granted the GMB the right to call the ballot}}}\uc2  earlier this month. It is likely to take place within weeks.\par \par \uc2 To secure recognition, the GMB will need to win a majority of support in the ballot. The \u8220\'20\'1Cyes\u8221\'20\'1D voters must also represent at least 40% of the more than 3,000 workers on site.\par \par \uc2 The GMB has been painstakingly building up its membership at the Coventry site and other nearby warehouses over many years.\par \par \uc2 Workers have held a series of strikes over the past year, demanding \u163\'00\'A315 an hour and the right to negotiate with management over pay and conditions.\par \par \uc2 On Black Friday in November, they were joined on the picket line by members of unions representing \uc2 Amazon\uc2  workers in continental Europe and the US.\par \par \uc2 The multinational is well known to be sceptical about the value of working with unions, and has been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/feb/26/amazon-trader-joes-starbucks-anti-union-measures"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 accused of union-busting tactics}}}\uc2  by the US labour regulator.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240426ek4q001jt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
