\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 UAW\uc2  secures historic union election win at Tennessee Volkswagen plant\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 567 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 April 2024\par 19:51 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Vote makes Chattanooga factory first auto plant in US south to unionize via election since the 1940s\par \par \uc2 Volkswagen\uc2  workers at the carmaker\u8217\'20\'19s Chattanooga plant in Tennessee have voted to unionize with the \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2 , a historic victory for the union and the labor movement\u8217\'20\'19s efforts to expand to the southern United States.\par \par \uc2 The vote was the first union election to be held as part of the \uc2 UAW\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s ambitious organizing drive {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.freep.com/story/money/cars/2023/11/29/uaw-public-organize-automakers/71731333007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 aimed}}}\uc2  at unionizing 150,000 workers at non-union auto plants around the US.\par \par \uc2 The win makes the Chattanooga factory the first auto plant in the south to unionize via election since the 1940s.\par \par \uc2 The union made the call late Friday night after some 2,200 ballots had been counted in favor of unionizing. The plant has about 4,300 eligible voters.\par \par \uc2 The victory is a milestone toward expanding union efforts in the southern US, where labor unions have historically faced aggressive opposition and union density has lagged far behind other parts of the US.\par \par \uc2 Workers at a Mercedes plant in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/05/mercedes-benz-alabama-union-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Vance, Alabama}}}\uc2 , are set to vote on whether to join the \uc2 UAW\uc2  in mid-May. Shawn Fain, the \uc2 UAW\uc2  president, is also targeting \uc2 Tesla\uc2 , whose boss, \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , has vigorously {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2023/dec/20/elon-musk-unions-tesla"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fought unionization}}}\uc2  efforts.\par \par \uc2 Workers at the plant in Chattanooga voted against the union in 2014 and 2019 in closely contested elections. In 2014, the \uc2 UAW{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tennessean.com/story/money/cars/2014/07/10/uaw-establish-local-union-chattanooga-vw-plant/12467703/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tried }}}\uc2  to partner with \uc2 Volkswagen\uc2  management to push for a works council similar to ones the company has in Germany, where \uc2 Volkswagen\uc2  is headquartered. But the plans faced significant backlash from anti-union groups and \uc2 Bob Corker\uc2 , the Republican US senator whose staff was in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/blogs/congress-blog/labor/202685-corker-must-come-clean-on-the-volkswagen-union-election/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 contact }}}\uc2  with anti-union groups over messaging before the election.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UAW\uc2  had been expected to win its latest vote given the firm support of workers beforehand, a quick turnaround from filing for the election to holding it, and a changing culture and landscape that has seen the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/510281/unions-strengthening.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US labor movement}}}\uc2  and the \uc2 UAW\uc2  surge in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.timesfreepress.com/news/2024/apr/14/uaw-viewed-more-favorably-than-unfavorably-in/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 popularity}}}\uc2  after the \uc2 UAW\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/uaw-strike-2023"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 successful strike}}}\uc2  against the US\u8217\'20\'19s domestic automakers last year.\par \par \uc2 Against that background, Republican elected officials had been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://nz.news.yahoo.com/tennessee-republican-volkswagen-union-vote-155048007.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 less eager}}}\uc2  to come out against the \uc2 UAW\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe \uc2 UAW\uc2  is sending a strong signal that big change may be coming to places where most thought the labor movement was dead and buried,\u8221\'20\'1D said professor Sharon Block, executive director of the Center for Labor and a Just Economy at Harvard Law School.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn the wake of the settlement of the strikes at the Big Three this fall, the transplant auto companies in the south gave their workers wage increases \u8211\'20\'13 the \uc2 UAW\uc2  bump \u8211\'20\'13 thinking that they could buy off their workers on the cheap. The \uc2 UAW\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s organizing campaign throughout the transplant companies in the south is a bet that workers can\u8217\'20\'19t be bought off so cheaply. The \uc2 UAW\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s message to these workers is: \u8216\'20\'18Don\u8217\'20\'19t settle for crumbs.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for \uc2 Volkswagen\uc2  said in an email before the vote: \u8220\'20\'1CWe respect our workers\u8217\'20\'19 right to a democratic process and to determine who should represent their interests. We fully support an \uc2 NLRB\uc2  vote so every team member has a chance to a secret ballot vote on this important decision.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Volkswagen\uc2  is proud of our working environment in Chattanooga that provides some of the best-paying jobs in the area.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240420ek4k0005l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
