\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Victories would be nothing less than an earthquake\u8217\'20\'19: can \uc2 UAW\uc2  win in the south?\b0\par\par\uc2 Steven Greenhouse \par \uc2 1,456 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 April 2024\par 12:23 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 United Auto Workers\uc2  faces first real test in campaign to unionize 13 automakers across US as \uc2 Volkswagen\uc2  workers vote in Tennessee\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 United Auto Workers (UAW)\uc2  has launched an ambitious campaign to unionize 13 non-union automakers across the US, and the first big test begins this Wednesday when 4,300 \uc2 Volkswagen\uc2  workers in Chattanooga, Tennessee, start voting on whether to unionize. Many VW workers are predicting victory.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re going to win,\u8221\'20\'1D said Lisa Elliott, a quality control worker at VW. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have the momentum. I know this will be a [historic] event.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Elliott has worked at VW since 2019 when the \uc2 UAW{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2014/apr/21/volkswagen-tennessee-auto-workers-union-drops-appeal-lost-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 narrowly lost}}}\uc2  a unionization vote in Chattanooga, but she says the mood today is far different. She said most workers are jazzed about unionizing because of the \uc2 UAW\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/oct/30/uaw-contract-gm-strike-end-update"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 big victory}}}\uc2  in last fall\u8217\'20\'19s strike and contract fight with \uc2 General Motors\uc2 , Ford and \uc2 Stellantis\uc2 , which owns \uc2 Jeep\uc2  and Chrysler.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI support a union because we don\u8217\'20\'19t have a voice now, and there are some serious issues that need to be addressed,\u8221\'20\'1D Elliott said. \u8220\'20\'1CIf the union wins here, it will definitely encourage workers in the other factories.\u8221\'20\'1D The vote in Chattanooga runs from Wednesday through Friday.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UAW\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s campaign has targeted 13 companies, including \uc2 Toyota\uc2 , Tesla and Hyundai, that have roughly 150,000 workers at 36 non-union plants. After VW, the next vote will be at the Mercedes plant in Vance, Alabama, where a supermajority of the 5,000 workers have signed cards requesting a unionization vote.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI have great confidence that the union drive will be successful,\u8221\'20\'1D said Jeremy Kimbrell, a worker at Mercedes\u8217\'20\'19 Vance plant since 1999. \u8220\'20\'1CA majority of workers have already voiced that they\u8217\'20\'19re with the union, and very few are openly against.\u8221\'20\'1D The \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  has not yet set a date for the vote.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA victory at \uc2 Volkswagen\uc2  would make a victory at Mercedes much more likely,\u8221\'20\'1D said Joseph McCartin, a labor historian at Georgetown and co-author of Labor in America: A History. \u8220\'20\'1CVictories at both \uc2 Volkswagen\uc2  and Mercedes would be nothing less than an earthquake. This would be the biggest breakthrough in private-sector organizing in decades. It would mean that the anti-union citadel [in the south] that has repulsed effort after organizing effort has been breached.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Stephen Silvia, a political science professor at American University who has written a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cornellpress.cornell.edu/book/9781501769702/the-uaws-southern-gamble/#bookTabs=1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 book about the failed unionization drives}}}\uc2  at VW, Mercedes and \uc2 Nissan\uc2  plants in the south, says several important developments make victories much more likely this time around. \u8220\'20\'1CThe \uc2 UAW\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s strikes last year show that the \uc2 UAW\uc2  can deliver,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CIt really was a turning point for the \uc2 UAW\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 For 30 years, Silvia said, the \uc2 UAW\uc2  was focused on fighting austerity and often agreed to concessions, but \u8220\'20\'1Cwhen Shawn Fain came in as \uc2 UAW\uc2  president [in March 2023], he turned things around and focused on making gains for the workers\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UAW\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s deal with Detroit\u8217\'20\'19s automakers includes {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.freep.com/story/money/cars/ford/2023/10/25/uaw-strike-ford-reaches-tentative-deal-with-union-sources-say/71318908007/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 raises of 25%}}}\uc2  over four and a half years \u8211\'20\'13 more than the total raises won in the previous 22 years. The contracts also call for improved pensions, restoring the cost-of-living allowance, increasing the top wage to $40 an hour and raising starting pay by 68%.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf they\u8217\'20\'19re doing a union drive, they can now point to last fall\u8217\'20\'19s contract settlement and say, \u8216\'20\'18This is what the union can do for you.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D Silvia said. \u8220\'20\'1CThey couldn\u8217\'20\'19t say that before.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Another change is that anti-union politicians in the south haven\u8217\'20\'19t, at least so far, campaigned as fiercely against the union as in the past \u8211\'20\'13 perhaps because the GOP is trying harder to woo blue-collar voters. Moreover, GOP governors are no longer in as powerful a position to scare workers by threatening to deny their plants big subsidies and thereby jeopardize a plant\u8217\'20\'19s survival. A major reason VW workers voted against unionizing in 2014 \u8211\'20\'13 712 against to 626 for \u8211\'20\'13 was that Tennessee\u8217\'20\'19s then governor, Bill Haslam, and state lawmakers had {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/6cb93e9857e145ec80e2246933217ff1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 threatened to withhold $300m}}}\uc2  in subsidies to build a second production line at the Chattanooga plant if the workers voted to unionize. VW workers feared that if their plant had just one production line, it might not survive. Now there is little fear of the plant closing because VW added an expensive production line in 2022 to make its all-electric ID.4 compact SUV.\par \par \uc2 To be sure, southern politicians have spoken out against the \uc2 UAW\uc2 . Tennessee\u8217\'20\'19s governor, Bill Lee, said, \u8220\'20\'1CIt would be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://newschannel9.com/news/local/tennessee-governor-says-a-union-at-chattanoogas-volkswagen-plant-would-be-a-big-mistake-united-auto-workers-assembly-line-vw-wages-hours-benefits"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a big mistake}}}\uc2  for [the VW] workers to risk their future\u8221\'20\'1D by unionizing. Alabama\u8217\'20\'19s governor, Kate Ivey, wrote, \u8220\'20\'1CAlabama has become a national leader in automotive manufacturing, and all this was achieved without a unionized workforce \u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.madeinalabama.com/2024/01/gov-ivey-unions-want-to-target-one-of-alabamas-crown-jewel-industries-but-im-standing-up-for-alabamians-and-protecting-our-jobs/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Unfortunately, the Alabama model}}}\uc2  for economic success is under attack.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.al.com/news/2024/04/union-president-blasts-gov-kay-ivey-alabama-auto-workers-are-fed-up-with-getting-screwed.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fain fired back}}}\uc2 , saying that Ivey \u8220\'20\'1Cdared to say that the economic model of the south is under attack. She\u8217\'20\'19s damn right it is! It\u8217\'20\'19s under attack because workers are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/UAW/status/1775299838923432057?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw%7Ctwcamp%5Etweetembed%7Ctwterm%5E1775299838923432057%7Ctwgr%5E34634137ac71ceada1604c37554b9c067a81c0f9%7Ctwcon%5Es1_&ref_url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.al.com%2Fnews%2F2024%2F04%2Funion-president-blasts-gov-kay-ivey-alabama-auto-workers-are-fed-up-with-getting-screwed.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fed up with getting screwed}}}\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Under Fain, the \uc2 UAW\uc2  has abandoned its top-down style of organizing, and that has increased the union\u8217\'20\'19s chances of winning. The \uc2 UAW\uc2  has let rank-and-file VW and Mercedes workers take far more control of their campaigns They fanned out quickly to collect pro-union cards, and the VW plant has 300 volunteer organizer captains.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe \uc2 UAW\uc2  has clearly taken a very creative, grassroots, militant approach to organizing and collective bargaining,\u8221\'20\'1D said Daniel Cornfield, a sociology professor at \uc2 Vanderbilt University\uc2  in Nashville. \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s a huge change.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Another big change is that the \uc2 UAW\uc2  has gone far to shed its reputation for corruption. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.autonews.com/static/section/content01.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 A corruption scandal}}}\uc2  in which \uc2 UAW\uc2  officials embezzled more than $3m and two former \uc2 UAW\uc2  presidents were sentenced to prison helped cause the \uc2 UAW\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s loss at VW in 2019. As a result of the scandal, the \uc2 UAW\uc2  agreed to have a federal monitor, and for the first time it established direct election of its president. Fain, an insurgent, won on an anti-concessions, anti-corruption platform.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI think Fain is a great guy,\u8221\'20\'1D said Kelcey Smith, a paint shop worker at the VW plant. \u8220\'20\'1CI believe in his vision for the union. He supports the workers.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Smith is very impressed by what Fain and the \uc2 UAW\uc2  achieved in their showdown with Detroit\u8217\'20\'19s automakers. When the \uc2 UAW\uc2  lost at \uc2 Volkswagen\uc2  in 2014 and 2019, Smith said, \u8220\'20\'1Cthe union didn\u8217\'20\'19t have anything on its plate for workers to look forward to. With what they accomplished with the big three, we feel they can accomplish that in the south.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Daiquiri Steele, an employment law professor at the University of Alabama, sees some important changes in the south. \u8220\'20\'1CPeople in Alabama are starting to see that the union can win,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CAt one point, it would have been unheard of, an exercise in futility. I don\u8217\'20\'19t think it\u8217\'20\'19s being perceived that way any more. With social media, people now have more access than ever to people who live outside the south. They can see that people in unionized settings have so much more than they have. That can influence people to say, \u8216\'20\'18How can I go about getting this, too?\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 At \uc2 Volkswagen\uc2 , a big issue is that many workers receive between 96 and 144 hours of paid time off a year (about 12 to 18 full-time days), but when VW closes the plant for a week or two during the year for maintenance, workers must use their paid time off if they want to be paid for those days the plant is closed. VW workers also complain that they don\u8217\'20\'19t receive paid sick days.\par \par \uc2 At Mercedes, workers complain that the Vance plant adopted a detested two-tier wage system in January 2020 and offered little in the way of raises for several years. After the union drive started, Mercedes ended two-tier and announced long-awaited raises. Nonetheless, VW and Mercedes workers remain upset that they earn several dollars less an hour than \uc2 UAW\uc2  members.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COne thing we say is, \u8216\'20\'18End the Alabama discount,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D said Kimbrell, the Mercedes worker. \u8220\'20\'1CWe have shown we can build cars as good as anybody in the world. The time is over when companies can just go to the south and pay people less money and treat them worse. We\u8217\'20\'19re sending the message, \u8216\'20\'18Come on down. Take advantage of the skills our workers offer, and we\u8217\'20\'19ll help you make profits. But if you come down, don\u8217\'20\'19t take advantage of the workers down here. End the discount.\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240417ek4h001bk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
