\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18No way\u8217\'20\'19: US labor watchdog refuses to bow to \uc2 SpaceX\uc2 , Amazon and \uc2 Starbucks\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 714 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 April 2024\par 20:42 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The \uc2 NLRB\uc2  general counsel has accused US\u8217\'20\'19s largest corporations of creating distractions to cover their law-breaking\par \par \uc2 The US\u8217\'20\'19s top labor lawyer has said her agency will not \u8220\'20\'1Csuccumb\u8221\'20\'1D to Amazon, \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  and \uc2 SpaceX\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s attempts to legally challenge the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  and its ability to enforce federal labor law.\par \par \uc2 Jennifer Abruzzo\uc2 , the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  general counsel, accused some of the US\u8217\'20\'19s largest corporations of \u8220\'20\'1Cjumping on the bandwagon\u8221\'20\'1D in mounting legal challenges to the labor watchdog, which has found itself at the center of the ongoing battle between the companies and a wave of unionizing efforts by workers.\par \par \uc2 Attorneys representing \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 SpaceX\uc2 , Amazon, Trader Joe\u8217\'20\'19s and \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  have all {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.epi.org/blog/whats-behind-the-corporate-effort-to-kneecap-the-national-labor-relations-board-spacex-amazon-trader-joes-and-starbucks-are-trying-to-have-the-nlrb-declared-unconstitutional/#:~:text=Rather%20than%20challenging%20the%20complaint,the%20agency's%20structure%20is%20unconstitutional."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 argued}}}\uc2  in recent months that the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.bloomberglaw.com/daily-labor-report/spacexs-bid-to-upend-nlrb-follows-signals-from-supreme-court"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NLRB is \u8220\'20\'1Cunconstitutional\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  and has overstepped its authority.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThere is no way, despite our very {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2022/aug/05/jennifer-abruzzo-nlrb-labor-lawyer-starbucks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 limited resources}}}\uc2  and board agents being overwhelmed with quite a number of cases \u8230\'20\'26 that we\u8217\'20\'19re going to succumb to the pressures imposed in addressing these challenges and in defending the constitutionality of our agency structure,\u8221\'20\'1D Abruzzo said at a webinar {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://rooseveltinstitute.org/event/preserving-the-administrative-state-threats-to-administrative-law-enforcement-in-the-courts/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 event}}}\uc2  hosted by the Roosevelt Institute.\par \par \uc2 Abruzzo, who was appointed by Joe Biden in 2021, said the legal challenges against the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  had been launched in retaliation for the agency doing its job.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese esoteric arguments came about why? Because we dared to issue a complaint against \uc2 SpaceX\uc2  after it unlawfully fired eight workers for speaking about their workplace concerns. And then Amazon jumps on the bandwagon, \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  jumps on the bandwagon, Trader Joe\u8217\'20\'19s, others get in on the action just because we\u8217\'20\'19re trying to hold them accountable for repeatedly violating workers\u8217\'20\'19 rights to organize and collectively bargain through representatives of their free choosing.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 SpaceX{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/26/anti-union-lawsuit-conservative-courts-musk-starbucks-trader-joes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed}}}\uc2  a lawsuit in court against the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  over a complaint issued by the agency that the company fired workers in response to a letter they wrote about workplace concerns and comments made by Musk.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 NLRB\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s constitutionality was upheld in a 1937 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://supreme.justia.com/cases/federal/us/301/1/#tab-opinion-1935607"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ruling}}}\uc2  before the United States supreme court and it is not yet certain the court will revisit that ruling. But the legal fight could {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://onlabor.org/understanding-the-latest-constitutional-attacks-on-the-nlrb/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 further delay}}}\uc2  union contract negotiations that have already been stalled by corporations including Amazon and \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  and stoked concerns over how the right-leaning supreme court would rule if it did decide to take up one of these cases.\par \par \uc2 Abruzzo noted there has also been an increase of employers seeking preliminary injunctions to try to delay or prevent the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  from engaging in enforcement actions against them. She cited several recent judgments the board obtained against \uc2 SpaceX\uc2  related to its severance agreements, against \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  over its prohibition of union-material distribution and a judgment against Amazon related to its employee off-duty access rules.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CUnfortunately, it seems to me they\u8217\'20\'19d rather spend their money initiating court litigation rather than improving their workers\u8217\'20\'19 lives and their own workplace operations,\u8221\'20\'1D added Abruzzo. \u8220\'20\'1CThere\u8217\'20\'19s also this secondary goal, I think, which is to divert attention away from the fact that they are actually lawbreakers who need to be held accountable in a timely manner. And frankly, that strategy is working. There\u8217\'20\'19s a lot of public reporting about the challenges as opposed to the law-breaking.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://aflcio.org/statements/icymi-president-biden-im-most-pro-union-president-american-history-and-i-make-no"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 touted}}}\uc2  himself as the \u8220\'20\'1Cmost pro-union president in history\u8221\'20\'1D and the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  under his administration has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2023/06/13/business/economy/nlrb-labor-ruling.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reversed}}}\uc2  several policies and decisions implemented by the board under Trump.\par \par \uc2 Since the Covid-19 pandemic and continuing under the Biden administration, the US labor movement has been experiencing a resurgence in union organizing, strikes and other labor actions. The \uc2 NLRB\uc2  recently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nlrb.gov/news-outreach/news-story/union-petitions-up-35-unfair-labor-practices-charge-filings-up-7-in-the"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported}}}\uc2  that in the first six months of the current fiscal year, October 2023 to March 2024, union election petitions rose 35% and unfair labor practice charge filings increased by 7% compared with the prior year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COur congressional mandate is to encourage peaceful resolution of industrial disputes and that depends on an effective means to vindicate public rights. It means we have to be able to operate and frankly. Even some who focus on employer interests have publicly said that there would be chaos at the workplace without a functioning \uc2 NLRB\uc2  and I completely agree with that,\u8221\'20\'1D Abruzzo concluded.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240410ek4a001jp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
