\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Mercedes-Benz\uc2  workers in Alabama file for union election\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 386 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 April 2024\par 14:04 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Car plant is second such in a southern state to ask the labor board to hold union election to join the United Autoworkers Union\par \par \uc2 Mercedes-Benz\uc2  workers in Vance, Alabama, have voted to hold an election to join the \uc2 United Auto Workers (UAW)\uc2 , the second car plant in a southern state to pass such a vote in the last month.\par \par \uc2 A supermajority of more than 5,000 workers at the plant have asked the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  (\uc2 NLRB\uc2 ) to organize an election. \uc2 Volkswagen\uc2  employees in Tennessee made the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/mar/18/volkswagen-workers-file-union-election-to-join-uaw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 same decision}}}\uc2  last month and will vote on whether to join the \uc2 UAW\uc2  later this month.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UAW\uc2  has long struggled to organize workers in southern car plants. The new wave of votes comes after the \uc2 UAW\uc2  won historic concessions from the US\u8217\'20\'19s big three automakers following a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/uaw-strike-2023"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 strike last year.}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe are voting for safer jobs at Mercedes,\u8221\'20\'1D said Moesha Chandler, an assembly team member at the Mercedes plant. \u8220\'20\'1CI\u8217\'20\'19m still young, but I\u8217\'20\'19m already having serious problems with my shoulders and hands. When you\u8217\'20\'19re still in your 20s and your body is breaking down, that\u8217\'20\'19s not right. By winning our union, we\u8217\'20\'19ll have the power to make the work safer and more sustainable.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Jacob Ryan, a team member at the Mercedes plant, argued workers need the union for issues such as forced Saturday shifts and unfair scheduling.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CRight now, the company keeps losing good people because they force them to work Saturdays at the last second, to take shifts that mess with their family lives. And the only choice people have is to take it or quit,\u8221\'20\'1D Ryan said. \u8220\'20\'1CWith the union, we\u8217\'20\'19ll have a voice for fair schedules that keeps workers at Mercedes.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Workers anticipate the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  will schedule a date for the union election in early May.\par \par \uc2 The organizing efforts have incited significant opposition from some Republican elected officials in the south, including \uc2 Kay Ivey\uc2 , the Alabama governor, business groups and automakers.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this week, the \uc2 UAW\uc2  filed unfair labor practice charges against \uc2 Mercedes-Benz\uc2  in the US and Germany over allegations of union busting. The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://uaw.org/uaw-files-charges-in-germany-against-mercedes-benz-companys-anti-union-campaign-against-u-s-autoworkers-violates-new-german-law-on-global-supply-chain-practices/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 allegations}}}\uc2  include claims of a retaliatory firing of a worker with stage 4 cancer. \uc2 Mercedes-Benz{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://finance.yahoo.com/news/mercedes-benz-rejects-anti-union-181043049.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 denied }}}\uc2  the allegations.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240405ek45001xr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
FF
