\par\par \uc2 World news\par \b \uc2 Middle East crisis: \uc2 World Central Kitchen\uc2  says only \u8216\'20\'18systemic change\u8217\'20\'19 can stop military failures as \uc2 IDF\uc2  sacks officers over aid worker deaths \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 Rachel Hall and Geneva Abdul \par \uc2 9,002 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 April 2024\par 14:12 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 WCK\uc2  says \uc2 IDF\uc2  deployed deadly force without regard to protocols in drone strikes in Gaza that killed seven aid workers. This live blog is closedIsraeli inquiry blames \uc2 WCK\uc2  aid killings on \u8216\'20\'18grave errors\u8217\'20\'19 by military personnel\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.57pm BST\par \par \uc2 Summary of the day so far\par \par \uc2 Here are all the key developments in the Middle East crisis from the past few hours:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Israeli military said Friday that it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/apr/05/middle-east-crisis-live-us-welcomes-israeli-plan-to-reopen-erez-crossing-for-gaza-aid?page=with:block-660ff2bd8f089151b4b2424c#block-660ff2bd8f089151b4b2424c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dismissed two officers and reprimanded three others}}}\uc2  for their roles in drone strikes in Gaza that killed seven aid workers on a food-delivery mission, saying they had mishandled critical information and violated the army\u8217\'20\'19s rules of engagement.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UN Human Rights Council\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/apr/05/middle-east-crisis-live-us-welcomes-israeli-plan-to-reopen-erez-crossing-for-gaza-aid?page=with:block-660fee168f089f4ce5208668#block-660fee168f089f4ce5208668"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 demanded a halt in all arms sales to Israel}}}\uc2 , highlighting warnings of \u8220\'20\'1Cgenocide\u8221\'20\'1D in its war in Gaza, which has killed more than 33,000 people.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The United States was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/apr/05/middle-east-crisis-live-us-welcomes-israeli-plan-to-reopen-erez-crossing-for-gaza-aid?page=with:block-660fe2408f08fd57229db452#block-660fe2408f08fd57229db452"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 looking into a media report}}}\uc2  that the Israeli military has been using artificial intelligence to help identify bombing targets in Gaza, White House national security spokesperson John Kirby told CNN in an interview on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 World Central Kitchen\uc2  (\uc2 WCK\uc2 ) on Friday said the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/apr/05/middle-east-crisis-live-us-welcomes-israeli-plan-to-reopen-erez-crossing-for-gaza-aid?page=with:block-660fdca98f089f4ce5208538#block-660fdca98f089f4ce5208538"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  IDF deployed deadly force}}}\uc2  without regard to its own protocols, chain of command and rules of engagement, and has called for an independent commission to investigate the killing of 7 aid workers.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/apr/05/middle-east-crisis-live-us-welcomes-israeli-plan-to-reopen-erez-crossing-for-gaza-aid?page=with:block-660ffc828f08fd57229db5e1#block-660ffc828f08fd57229db5e1"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 revealed the identity}}}\uc2  of the commander of Israel\u8217\'20\'19s Unit 8200, which is a closely guarded secret. He occupies one of the most sensitive roles in the military, leading one of the world\u8217\'20\'19s most powerful surveillance agencies, comparable to the \uc2 US National Security Agency\uc2 . Yet after spending more than two decades operating in the shadows , the controversial spy chief \u8211\'20\'13 whose name is Yossi Sariel \u8211\'20\'13 has left his identity exposed online.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 UN\uc2  Secretary-General \uc2 Antonio Guterres{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/apr/05/middle-east-crisis-live-us-welcomes-israeli-plan-to-reopen-erez-crossing-for-gaza-aid?page=with:block-660fff658f089f4ce5208765#block-660fff658f089f4ce5208765"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said he sincerely hopes}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/israel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Israel}}}\uc2  quickly and effectively boosts aid access to the Gaza Strip, describing the situation in the Palestinian enclave after six months of war as \u8220\'20\'1Cabsolutely desperate.\u8221\'20\'1D He was \u8220\'20\'1Cdeeply troubled\u8221\'20\'1D by reports that the Israeli military has been using artificial intelligence to help identify bombing targets in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/gaza"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gaza}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.52pm BST\par \par \uc2 Poland\u8217\'20\'19s deputy foreign minister handed a diplomatic note on Friday to Israel\u8217\'20\'19s ambassador protesting the killing of a Polish aid worker in an attack earlier this week on a convoy of aid workers in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 AP reports:\par \par \uc2 After the meeting, Deputy Foreign Minister Andrzej Szejna told reporters in Warsaw that he handed the protest note to Ambassador Yacov Livne after he was summoned because of the deaths of the \uc2 World Central Kitchen\uc2  workers.\par \par \uc2 Szejna described the Polish stance during the meeting as \u8220\'20\'1Cfirm.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 At the beginning, the ambassador apologised for this unprecedented event in the history of the civilised world, that is the bombing of a car in a humanitarian convoy heading with humanitarian aid to the famine-affected Gaza Strip.\par \par \uc2 Livne said on social media that during the meeting he expressed his \u8220\'20\'1Cpersonal deep sorrow and sincere apologies\u8221\'20\'1D for the deaths of the \uc2 World Central Kitchen\uc2  workers, including Polish citizen Damian Sob\u243\'00\'F3l.\par \par \uc2 Livne said:\par \par \uc2 We share in the grief of the families from the bottom of our hearts. I assured the Deputy Minister that Israel is fully committed to a transparent and thorough investigation of this grave tragedy\par \par \uc2 He said findings from the Israeli military published Friday \u8220\'20\'1Cshow our ongoing commitment to investigate what had happened in Gaza and take all appropriate measures to prevent such tragedies in the future.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Israeli military said Friday that it dismissed two officers and reprimanded three others for their roles in drone strikes in Gaza that killed seven aid workers on a food-delivery mission, saying they had mishandled critical information and violated the army\u8217\'20\'19s rules of engagement.\par \par \uc2 Szejna, who spoke to reporters before the dismissals were reported, said Poland expected a transparent investigation and compensation for the victim\u8217\'20\'19s family if it wants it.\par \par \uc2 He also said Poland wants the district prosecutor\u8217\'20\'19s office in Przemysl, where the Polish aid worker was from, to be allowed to participate in the investigation \u8220\'20\'1Cand in the entire criminal and disciplinary procedure against the soldiers responsible for this murder.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 UN\uc2  Secretary-General \uc2 Antonio Guterres\uc2  has said he sincerely hopes Israel quickly and effectively boosts aid access to the Gaza Strip, describing the situation in the Palestinian enclave after six months of war as \u8220\'20\'1Cabsolutely desperate.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Guterres told reporters:\par \par \uc2 When the gates to aid are closed, the doors to starvation are opened. More than half the population \u8211\'20\'13 over a million people \u8211\'20\'13 are facing catastrophic hunger. Children in Gaza today are dying for lack of food and water.\par \par \uc2 This is incomprehensible, and entirely avoidable. Nothing can justify the collective punishment of the Palestinian people.\par \par \uc2 The Israeli government has acknowledged mistakes. But the essential problem is not who made the mistakes, it is the military strategy and procedures in place that allow for those mistakes to multiply time and time again.\par \par \uc2 Fixing those failures requires independent investigations and meaningful and measurable changes on the ground.\par \par \uc2 196 humanitarian workers have been killed and we want to know why each one of them was killed.\par \par \uc2 Guterres also said he was \u8220\'20\'1Cdeeply troubled\u8221\'20\'1D by reports that the Israeli military has been using artificial intelligence to help identify bombing targets in Gaza. The Israeli military denies AI was used to identify suspected extremists and targets.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.30pm BST\par \par \uc2 US Secretary of State \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  has said that the US is carefully reviewing Israel\u8217\'20\'19s inquiry into the strike that killed seven \uc2 World Central Kitchen\uc2  aid workers this week, adding that Washington will be looking very carefully at what steps Israel is taking.\par \par \uc2 He told reporters in Brussels:\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s very important that Israel is taking full responsibility for this incident. It\u8217\'20\'19s also important that it appears to be taking steps to hold those responsible accountable. Even more important is that steps are being taken going forward to ensure that something like this can never happen again.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 Guardian\uc2  uncovers identity of secret top Israel military commander\par \par \uc2 The identity of the commander of Israel\u8217\'20\'19s Unit 8200 is a closely guarded secret. He occupies one of the most sensitive roles in the military, leading one of the world\u8217\'20\'19s most powerful surveillance agencies, comparable to the \uc2 US National Security Agency\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Yet after spending more than two decades operating in the shadows , \uc2 Guardian\uc2  reporters Harry Davies and Bethan McKernan can reveal how the controversial spy chief \u8211\'20\'13 whose name is Yossi Sariel \u8211\'20\'13 has left his identity exposed online.\par \par \uc2 The embarrassing security lapse is linked to a book he published on \uc2 Amazon\uc2 , which left a digital trail to a private \uc2 Google\uc2  account created in his name, along with his unique ID and links to the account\u8217\'20\'19s maps and calendar profiles.\par \par \uc2 The Guardian\uc2  has confirmed with multiple sources that Sariel is the secret author of The Human Machine Team, a book in which he offers a radical vision for how artificial intelligence can transform the relationship between military personnel and machines.\par \par \uc2 The full story is here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/apr/05/top-israeli-spy-chief-exposes-his-true-identity-in-online-security-lapse"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Top Israeli spy chief exposes his true identity in online security lapse}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 2.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.15pm BST\par \par \uc2 Our US blog is covering the pressure on President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to suspend weapons transfers to Israel.\par \par \uc2 US live politics blogger Chris Stein writes:\par \par \uc2 The fallout from Israel\u8217\'20\'19s killing of seven \uc2 World Central Kitchen\uc2  aid workers is continuing, with several of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s top Senate allies pressuring him for a decisive change in course on supporting its invasion of Gaza.\par \par \uc2 In {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.com/newsletters/playbook/2024/04/05/could-bibi-tank-ukraine-aid-00150755?nname=playbook&nid=0000014f-1646-d88f-a1cf-5f46b7bd0000&nrid=12069c7e-e346-405c-ad2c-71cb1a62e514&nlid=630318"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an interview with Politico}}}\uc2 , \uc2 Chris Van Hollen\uc2  demanded the Biden administration suspend weapons transfers if Israel does not better protect civilians, while Elizabeth Warren{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/04/israel-gaza-war-biden-netanyahu-latest-updates?page=with:block-660edb258f089fcebeb9cc99#block-660edb258f089fcebeb9cc99"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called for the planned sale}}}\uc2  of F-15 fighter jets to the country to be canceled.\par \par \uc2 Citing reports of famine in Gaza, independent senator Bernie Sanders, said yesterday \u8220\'20\'1CIsrael should not be getting another nickel in military aid until these policies are fundamentally changed.\u8221\'20\'1D The mounting opposition could further complicate Congress\u8217\'20\'19s approval of military aid package for Israel, Ukraine and other US allies, which has been deadlocked for months.\par \par \uc2 The two issues will intersect this afternoon, when Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/01/temporary-ship-route-baltimore-bridge-collapse"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 visits the site}}}\uc2  of the collapse Francis Scott Key bridge in Baltimore. \uc2 Van Hollen\uc2 , who represents Maryland and will attend the event, says he plans to bring up his concerns over his policies towards Israel when he sees the president.\par \par \uc2 You can follow everything as it happens here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/05/biden-israel-weapons-baltimore-visit-updates"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden urged to suspend weapons transfers to Israel; president to visit Baltimore after bridge collapse \u8211\'20\'13 live}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 One of the hostages seized by \uc2 Hamas\uc2  gunmen during their attack on Israeli communities around {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/israel-hamas/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gaza}}}\uc2  on 7 October was probably killed by an Israeli helicopter gunship that was responding to the attack, the military said on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Reuters reports:\par \par \uc2 For several weeks, the military has been investigating reports that some of the 1,200 Israelis and foreign victims of the attack were killed by friendly fire during the chaos, in which more than 250 people were abducted as hostages.\par \par \uc2 It said an inquiry into the events around the kidnapping of Efrat Katz, a resident of Kibbutz Nir Oz, one of the communities targeted by the attack, examined a variety of video evidence and testimony of witnesses.\par \par \uc2 It said the evidence showed that one of the helicopter gunships fired at a vehicle in which gunmen were travelling and which the evidence also suggested had hostages in it.\par \par \uc2 It said in a statement:\par \par \uc2 As a result of the fire, most of the terrorists manning the vehicle were killed, and most likely, Efrat Katz... was killed as well.\par \par \uc2 The commander of the air force did not find fault in the operation by the helicopter crew, who operated in compliance with the orders in a complex reality of war\par \par \uc2 It said the investigation showed that the hostages could not be distinguished by existing surveillance systems.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 Israeli military dismisses two officers over Gaza drone strikes\par \par \uc2 The Israeli military said Friday that it dismissed two officers and reprimanded three others for their roles in drone strikes in Gaza that killed seven aid workers on a food-delivery mission, saying they had mishandled critical information and violated the army\u8217\'20\'19s rules of engagement.\par \par \uc2 AP reports:\par \par \uc2 The findings of a retired general\u8217\'20\'19s investigation into the Monday killings marked an embarrassing admission by Israel, which faces growing accusations from key allies, including the US, of not doing enough to protect Gaza\u8217\'20\'19s civilians from its war with \uc2 Hamas\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The findings are likely to bolster widespread scepticism over the Israeli military\u8217\'20\'19s decision-making. Palestinians, aid groups and human rights organisations have repeatedly accused Israeli forces of firing recklessly at civilians throughout the conflict \u8212\'20\'14 a charge Israel denies.\par \par \uc2 With pressure mounting on Israel to hold itself accountable, Hagari and other officials late Thursday shared with reporters the results of the investigation.\par \par \uc2 The speed of the probe and the swift punishment of five senior officers were extremely unusual. Such investigations are often slow and in most cases end without charges being filed. Human rights activists have long complained that Israeli forces operate in a climate of impunity, an allegation the military rejects.\par \par \uc2 The military\u8217\'20\'19s spokesman, Rear Adm. Daniel Hagari, told reporters:\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s a tragedy.\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s a serious event that we are responsible for and it shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t have happened and we will make sure that it won\u8217\'20\'19t happen again.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.46pm BST\par \par \uc2 An Israeli military commission of inquiry has blamed a series of \u8220\'20\'1Cgrave errors\u8221\'20\'1D by military personnel, including lack of coordination and misidentification, for its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/apr/02/charities-halt-gaza-operations-after-israeli-drones-kill-aid-workers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 killing of seven World Central Kitchen aid workers}}}\uc2  in Gaza drone strikes, the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s foreign correspondent Peter Beaumont writes.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/israel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Israel}}}\uc2  Defense Forces said they had dismissed a brigade chief of staff with the rank of colonel and a brigade fire support officer with the rank of major and issued formal reprimands to senior officers, including the general at the head of the southern command.\par \par \uc2 The findings are likely to renew scepticism over the military\u8217\'20\'19s decision-making. Palestinians, aid groups and human rights organisations have repeatedly accused Israeli forces of firing recklessly at civilians throughout the conflict \u8211\'20\'13 a charge Israel denies.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 WCK\uc2  founder, Jos\u233\'00\'E9 Andr\u233\'00\'E9s, said:\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 IDF\uc2  cannot credibly investigate its own failure in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/gaza"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gaza}}}\uc2 . It\u8217\'20\'19s not enough to simply try to avoid further humanitarian deaths, which have now approached close to 200. All civilians need to be protected, and all innocent people in Gaza need to be fed and safe. And all hostages must be released.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/apr/05/israeli-inquiry-blames-wck-aid-killings-on-grave-errors-by-military-personnel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Israeli inquiry blames WCK aid killings on \u8216\'20\'18grave errors\u8217\'20\'19 by military personnel}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 1.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 UN Human Rights Council\uc2  demands halt to arms sales to Israel\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UN Human Rights Council\uc2  has demanded a halt in all arms sales to Israel, highlighting warnings of \u8220\'20\'1Cgenocide\u8221\'20\'1D in its war in Gaza, which has killed more than 33,000 people.\par \par \uc2 AFP reports:\par \par \uc2 The resolution - which passed with 28 of the council\u8217\'20\'19s 47 member states voting in favour, six opposed and 13 abstaining - marked the first time the \uc2 United Nations\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 top rights body has taken a position on the bloodiest-ever war in the besieged Palestinian territory.\par \par \uc2 Meirav Eilon Shahar, Israel\u8217\'20\'19s ambassador to the \uc2 UN\uc2  in Geneva, denounced the resolution as \u8220\'20\'1Ca stain for the \uc2 Human Rights Council\uc2  and for the \uc2 UN\uc2  as a whole\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The strongly worded text called on countries to \u8220\'20\'1Ccease the sale, transfer and diversion of arms, munitions and other military equipment to Israel... to prevent further violations of international humanitarian law and violations and abuses of human rights\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 It noted that the \uc2 International Court of Justice\uc2  ruled in January \u8220\'20\'1Cthat there is a plausible risk of genocide\u8221\'20\'1D in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 Friday\u8217\'20\'19s resolution, which was brought forward by Pakistan on behalf of all \uc2 Organisation of Islamic Cooperation\uc2  (\uc2 OIC\uc2 ) member states except Albania, also called for \u8220\'20\'1Can immediate ceasefire\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cfor immediate emergency humanitarian access and assistance\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The United States, Israel\u8217\'20\'19s key ally, heeded its call to vote no, as did Germany, Argentina, Bulgaria, Malawi and Paraguay.\par \par \uc2 US ambassador Michele Taylor nonetheless voiced unusually strong criticism of Israel, saying it \u8220\'20\'1Chas not done enough to mitigate civilian harm\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 But she said Washington could not support the text because of its \u8220\'20\'1Cmany problematic elements\u8221\'20\'1D, including failing to specifically condemn \uc2 Hamas\uc2  and its 7 October attacks.\par \par \uc2 While the rights council resolution did not name \uc2 Hamas\uc2 , it did condemn the firing of rockets at Israeli civilian areas and demanded \u8220\'20\'1Cthe immediate release of all remaining hostages\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 But the main focus was on Israel, with the text demanding that it end its occupation of all Palestinian territories, lift its blockade of Gaza, and end \u8220\'20\'1Call other forms of collective punishment\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The text also expressed \u8220\'20\'1Cgrave concern at statements by Israeli officials amounting to incitement to genocide\u8221\'20\'1D and urged countries to \u8220\'20\'1Cprevent the continued forcible transfer of Palestinians within and from Gaza\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 It warned in particular \u8220\'20\'1Cagainst any large-scale military operations in the city of Rafah\u8221\'20\'1D in the south of the densely populated Gaza Strip, where well over one million civilians are sheltering.\par \par \uc2 The resolution also condemned \u8220\'20\'1Cthe use of starvation of civilians as a method of warfare in Gaza\u8221\'20\'1D, where the \uc2 UN\uc2  has warned that famine is looming.\par \par \uc2 Two other resolutions targeting Israel also overwhelmingly passed at the rights council Friday.\par \par \uc2 One demanded a halt to Israeli settlements, calling on countries to do more to counter settler violence against Palestinians, including through sanctions, and on businesses to terminate activities in or with the settlements.\par \par \uc2 The other deplored Israel\u8217\'20\'19s occupation of the Syrian Golan Heights and its \u8220\'20\'1Csettlement policies and practices\u8221\'20\'1D there, in violation of the rights of Syrian inhabitants.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Anas Sarwar\uc2 , the Scottish {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/labour"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Labour}}}\uc2  leader, has become the latest senior party figure to urge an immediate ban on UK arms sales to Israel, as ministers face pressure to disclose the government\u8217\'20\'19s official legal advice on the trade.\par \par \uc2 Sarwar {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/BBCDavidWL/status/1776186376188277134"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told BBC Scotland}}}\uc2  that Israel had \u8220\'20\'1Cclearly\u8221\'20\'1D breached international law in Gaza and that UK arms sales should be halted immediately.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday \uc2 Sadiq Khan\uc2 , the London mayor and the party\u8217\'20\'19s other senior Muslim figure, made {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2024/apr/04/sadiq-khan-arms-sales-israel-got-to-stop"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the same call}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2024/apr/05/labour-anas-sarwar-calls-for-ban-on-uk-arms-sales-to-israel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Labour\u8217\'20\'19s Anas Sarwar joins calls for ban on UK arms sales to Israel}}}\par \par \uc2 Labour\u8217\'20\'19s official policy is to await information on the legal advice provided to ministers and to only push for an end to arms sales if this says continued weapons sales could risk the UK breaching international law.\par \par \uc2 In March, \uc2 David Cameron\uc2 , the foreign secretary, said information about the advice would be published within days, but ministers have since backtracked and are refusing to say if and when this might happen.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 These are the latest images coming across the wires from Gaza:\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.41pm BST\par \par \uc2 The US looking at report that Israel used AI to identify bombing targets in Gaza\par \par \uc2 The United States was looking into a media report that the Israeli military has been using artificial intelligence to help identify bombing targets in Gaza, White House national security spokesperson John Kirby told CNN in an interview on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, the \uc2 Guardian\uc2  reported on the Israeli military\u8217\'20\'19s use of the AI system Lavender which at one stage identified 37,000 potential targets based on their apparent links to \uc2 Hamas\uc2 , according to intelligence sources involved in the war.\par \par \uc2 Intelligence sources told the Guardian that Israeli military officials permitted large numbers of Palestinian civilians to be killed, particularly during the early weeks and months of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/israel-hamas-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 conflict}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The report in +972 Magazine and Local Call was also published on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 IDF\uc2 , in statements to the media on Thursday, denied that AI was used to identify suspected extremists and targets.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/apr/03/israel-gaza-ai-database-hamas-airstrikes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Read more here:}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/apr/03/israel-gaza-ai-database-hamas-airstrikes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18The machine did it coldly\u8217\'20\'19: Israel used AI to identify 37,000 Hamas targets }}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 The US Secretary of State \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  said Friday that the measures the Israeli government has announced to expand the flow of aid into Gaza are welcome but may not be enough to meet the Biden administration\u8217\'20\'19s demands for dramatic improvements in humanitarian conditions in the territory.\par \par \uc2 Blinken said that opening more border crossings, if fully implemented, has the potential to surge assistance to Palestinians caught in the fighting between Israel and \uc2 Hamas\uc2 . However, the US also wants to see tangible steps to bolster the protection of civilians and aid workers, he said.\par \par \uc2 In addition, he called for an \u8220\'20\'1Cindependent, thorough and fully publicized investigation\u8221\'20\'1D into the recent killings of aid workers. Seven employees of the charity \uc2 World Central Kitchen\uc2 , including six international volunteers, were killed in multiple Israeli airstrikes on their three-car convoy in Gaza late Monday.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe welcome that steps that have been announced by Israel,\u8221\'20\'1D Blinken said. \u8220\'20\'1CThese are positive developments but the real test is results and that\u8217\'20\'19s what we\u8217\'20\'19re looking to see in the coming days and the coming weeks.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 At the same time, he said the U.S. wanted to see a \u8220\'20\'1Cbetter system for de-confliction and coordination\u8221\'20\'1D so that aid can be safely delivered and distributed inside Gaza.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAll of these things are critical and that really needs to be measured by results,\u8221\'20\'1D Blinken told reporters in the town of Leuven, outside Brussels, where he was meeting with U.S. and European trade and commerce officials.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.35pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.23pm BST\par \par \uc2 World Central Kitchen\uc2  says without 'systemic change' there will be more military failures\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 World Central Kitchen\uc2  (\uc2 WCK\uc2 ) on Friday said the \uc2 IDF\uc2  deployed deadly force without regard to its own protocols, chain of command and rules of engagement, and has called for an independent commission to investigate the killing of 7 aid workers.\par \par \uc2 The Israeli military said that it has dismissed two officers and reprimanded three others for their roles in drone strikes in Gaza that killed seven aid workers on a food-delivery mission, saying they had mishandled critical information and violated the army\u8217\'20\'19s rules of engagement.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWithout systemic change, there will be more military failures, more apologies and more grieving families,\u8221\'20\'1D \uc2 WCK\uc2  said, calling the \uc2 IDF\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s disciplinary action against those involved and accepting responsibility \u8220\'20\'1Cimportant steps forward\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe demand the creation of an independent commission to investigate the killings of our \uc2 WCK\uc2  colleagues. The \uc2 IDF\uc2  cannot credibly investigate its own failure in Gaza.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 WCK\uc2  said the \uc2 IDF\uc2  acknowledged the organisations\u8217\'20\'19 teams followed proper communications procedures, and said the \uc2 IDF\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s video footage \u8220\'20\'1Cfails to show any cause to fire on our personnel convoy, which carried no weapons and posed no threat.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The investigation into Monday\u8217\'20\'19s killings found officers failed to read messages alerting troops that cars, not aid trucks, would carry workers from the charity away from the warehouse where aid was distributed. As a result, the cars that were targeted were misidentified as transporting militants.\par \par \uc2 The army also faulted a major who identified the strike target and a colonel who approved the strike for acting with insufficient information. The army said the order was given after one of the passengers inside a car was identified as a gunman.\par \par \uc2 The aid workers were three British citizens, a Polish citizen, an Australian and a Canadian American dual citizen. Their Palestinian driver also was killed.\par \par \uc2 WCK\uc2  founder Jos\u233\'00\'E9 Andr\u233\'00\'E9s said:\par \par \uc2 It\u8217\'20\'19s not enough to simply try to avoid further humanitarian deaths, which have now approached close to 200. All civilians need to be protected, and all innocent people in Gaza need to be fed and safe. And all hostages must be released.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 12.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 12.02pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jos\u233\'00\'E9 Andr\u233\'00\'E9s: the chef behind Gaza food aid charity who \u8216\'20\'18moves towards disaster\u8217\'20\'19 to help the hungry\par \par \uc2 When Jos\u233\'00\'E9 Andr\u233\'00\'E9s accepted the challenge of delivering food aid to a famine-threatened {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/gaza"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gaza}}}\uc2  last month, he declared \u8211\'20\'13 without a trace of overstatement \u8211\'20\'13 that he was \u8220\'20\'1Cworking with the urgency of now\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/apr/02/chef-jose-andres-israeli-strike-kills-aid-workers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Jos\u233\'00\'E9 Andr\u233\'00\'E9s: the chef behind Gaza food aid charity who \u8216\'20\'18moves towards disaster\u8217\'20\'19 to help the hungry}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s worth trying. We have to try. If we succeed, everybody is helped,\u8221\'20\'1D the celebrity chef turned aid supremo said of his plan to use his non-profit \uc2 World Central Kitchen\uc2  (\uc2 WCK\uc2 ) to help avert the looming humanitarian disaster.\par \par \uc2 On display was the same irrepressible can-do spirit that had enabled the Spanish-born Andr\u233\'00\'E9s, now a US citizen, to bring food relief to citizens stricken by natural disaster or war in numerous far-flung locations, from Haiti to Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.46am BST\par \par \uc2 The killing of the aid workers, all of whom worked for \uc2 World Central Kitchen\uc2 , were condemned by Israel\u8217\'20\'19s closest allies and renewed criticism of Israel\u8217\'20\'19s conduct in the nearly 6-month-old war with \uc2 Hamas\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The aid workers were three British citizens, a Polish citizen, an Australian and a Canadian American dual citizen. Their Palestinian driver also was killed.\par \par \uc2 The investigation into Monday\u8217\'20\'19s killings found two major areas of wrongdoing.\par \par \uc2 It faulted officers for failing to read messages alerting troops that cars, not aid trucks, would carry workers from the charity away from the warehouse where aid was distributed. As a result, the cars that were targeted were misidentified as transporting militants.\par \par \uc2 The army also faulted a major who identified the strike target and a colonel who approved the strike for acting with insufficient information.\par \par \uc2 The army said the order was given after one of the passengers inside a car was identified as a gunman. It said troops became suspicious because a gunman had been seen on the roof of one of the delivery trucks on the way to the warehouse. The army showed reporters footage of the gunman firing his weapon while riding atop one of the trucks.\par \par \uc2 After the aid was dropped off at a warehouse, an officer believed he had spotted a gunman in one of the cars. The passenger, it turned out, was not carrying a weapon \u8211\'20\'13 the military said its possible he was just carrying a bag.\par \par \uc2 The army said it initially hit one car. As people scrambled away into a second car, it hit that vehicle as well. It did the same thing when survivors scrambled into a third car. Army officials claimed that drone operators could not see that the cars were marked with the words \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 World Central Kitchen\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D because it was nighttime.\par \par \uc2 The army could not say exactly where the communication about the convoy\u8217\'20\'19s plans had broken down.\par \par \uc2 The army declined to answer questions about whether similar violations of rules of engagement have taken place during the war \u8211\'20\'13 in which Palestinians, aid workers and international rights groups have repeatedly accused the army of recklessly striking civilians.\par \par \uc2 The investigation was headed by Yoav Har-Even, a retired general.\par \par \uc2 The seven who were killed were distributing food that had been brought into Gaza through a newly established maritime corridor. \uc2 World Central Kitchen\uc2  said it had coordinated its movements with the military, and that the vehicles were marked with the organization\u8217\'20\'19s logo.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt was a direct attack on clearly marked vehicles whose movements were known by\u8221\'20\'1D the Israeli military, Andr\u233\'00\'E9s said on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 More than 220 humanitarian workers have been killed in the conflict, according to the \uc2 U.N.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CLet\u8217\'20\'19s be very clear. This is tragic, but it is not an anomaly,\u8221\'20\'1D Scott Paul, of the humanitarian group \uc2 Oxfam\uc2 , said Thursday in a briefing with other relief organizations before the results of Israel\u8217\'20\'19s investigation were released. \u8220\'20\'1CThe killing of aid workers in Gaza has been systemic.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.47am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.40am BST\par \par \uc2 Israel military sacks two senior officers over killing of aid workers and says strikes were a tragedy\par \par \uc2 The Israeli military said on Friday that it has dismissed two officers and reprimanded three others for their roles in drone strikes in Gaza that killed seven aid workers on a food-delivery mission, saying they had mishandled critical information and violated the army\u8217\'20\'19s rules of engagement.\par \par \uc2 The findings of a retired general\u8217\'20\'19s investigation into the Monday killings marked an embarrassing admission by Israel, which faces growing accusations from key allies, including the US, of not doing enough to protect Gaza\u8217\'20\'19s civilians from its war with \uc2 Hamas\uc2 , AP reports.\par \par \uc2 The findings are likely to renew scepticism over the Israeli military\u8217\'20\'19s decision-making. Palestinians, aid groups and human rights organisations have repeatedly accused Israeli forces of firing recklessly at civilians throughout the conflict \u8212\'20\'14 a charge Israel denies.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a tragedy,\u8221\'20\'1D the military\u8217\'20\'19s spokesman, Rear Adm. Daniel Hagari, told reporters. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a serious event that we are responsible for and it shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t have happened and we will make sure that it won\u8217\'20\'19t happen again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 With pressure mounting on Israel to hold itself accountable, Hagari and other officials late Thursday shared with reporters the results of the military\u8217\'20\'19s uncommonly speedy and detailed investigation.\par \par \uc2 It was unclear whether the punishments and the apology would calm an international outcry over the deaths of the \uc2 World Central Kitchen\uc2  workers or reassure international aid groups that it was safe to resume operations in Gaza, where nearly a third of the population is on the brink of starvation.\par \par \uc2 According to what spokespeople said were the Israeli army\u8217\'20\'19s rules, targets must be visually identified as threats for multiple reasons before they can be hit. But the investigation determined that a colonel had authorized the series of deadly drone strikes on the convoy based on one major\u8217\'20\'19s observation \u8212\'20\'14 from grainy drone-camera footage \u8212\'20\'14 that someone in the convoy was armed. That observation turned out to be untrue, military officials said.\par \par \uc2 The army said the colonel and the major were dismissed, while three other officers were reprimanded. It said the results of its investigation were turned over to the military\u8217\'20\'19s advocate general, who will decide whether the officers or anyone else involved in the killings should receive further punishment or be prosecuted.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.42am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.33am BST\par \par \uc2 Turkish authorities, who have denounced Israel for its war against \uc2 Hamas\uc2  militants in the Gaza Strip, have arrested two people suspected of spying for Israeli intelligence, interior minister Ali Yerlikaya said on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Since January, Turkish authorities have detained or arrested and charged dozens of people suspected of having ties to Israel\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 Mossad intelligence agency\uc2 , Reuters reports. Six people were charged last month.\par \par \uc2 Turkish and Israeli leaders have traded public barbs since Israel\u8217\'20\'19s war with the Palestinian militant group \uc2 Hamas\uc2  began in October. Turkey has warned Israel of \u8220\'20\'1Cserious consequences\u8221\'20\'1D if it tries to hunt down \uc2 Hamas\uc2  members living outside the Palestinian territories, including in Turkey.\par \par \uc2 In a post on social media platform X, Yerlikaya said police had detained eight people believed to be collecting and selling information to \uc2 Mossad\uc2  about targeted individuals and companies in Turkey. Of those, two had been arrested and six released on parole, he said.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe will never allow espionage activities that are carried out within our country\u8217\'20\'19s borders against our people\u8217\'20\'19s national unity and solidarity. We are in pursuit,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 A Turkish security official said the raids, carried out in Istanbul, targeted a Turkish private detective and his wife, who were believed to have been involved with \uc2 Mossad\uc2  from 2011-2020.\par \par \uc2 The official said the detective had previously met \uc2 Mossad\uc2  members in Austria, Switzerland and Germany and used private communication channels to keep in touch with them.\par \par \uc2 The detective \u8220\'20\'1Cearned significant income\u8221\'20\'1D from this and formed a network of nine people, the official said. Members of the network had confessed and the detective and his wife had been arrested, the person added.\par \par \uc2 There was no immediate comment from Israel.\par \par \uc2 A Turkish court in January ordered the arrest of 15 people and the deportation of eight suspected of having links to \uc2 Mossad\uc2  and targeting Palestinians living in Turkey.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.26am BST\par \par \uc2 Poland\u8217\'20\'19s deputy foreign minister said on Friday that the Israeli ambassador to Poland apologised after an Israeli air strike killed a Polish aid worker in Gaza this week.\par \par \uc2 Israeli ambassador Yacov Livne would not be expelled from Poland, the deputy Polish Deputy Foreign Minister Andrzej Szejna said.\par \par \uc2 On Friday a \uc2 German foreign ministry\uc2  spokesperson said attacks that killed seven food aid workers of the \uc2 World Central Kitchen\uc2  (\uc2 WCK\uc2 ) charity group in Gaza \u8220\'20\'1Ccast a bad light on the conduct of the Israeli army\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.14am BST\par \par \uc2 Summary\par \par \uc2 Welcome to our latest live coverage of the Israel-Gaza war and wider Middle East crisis. Here\u8217\'20\'19s a snapshot of all the key developments so far.\par \par \uc2 Israel has approved the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/apr/05/israel-reopen-erez-crossing-gaza-biden-warning-war-netanyahu-palestine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reopening of the Erez crossing}}}\uc2  into northern Gaza and the temporary use of Israel\u8217\'20\'19s Ashdod port to increase humanitarian aid supplies into Gaza, a statement from the prime minister\u8217\'20\'19s office said early on Friday.\par \par \uc2 It also approved expanded entry of aid from Jordan through the Kerem Shalom crossing.\par \par \uc2 The US secretary of state \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  has welcomed the steps announced by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/israel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Israel}}}\uc2  on humanitarian aid to Gaza, but said \u8220\'20\'1Cthe real test is results\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In other developments:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Since 7 October, 33,091 Palestinians have been killed and 75,750 injured in Israel\u8217\'20\'19s military offensive on Gaza, according to the Gaza health ministry on Friday. It was not possible to independently verify the figures.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 United Nations Human Rights Council\uc2  on Friday adopted a resolution calling for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/israel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Israel}}}\uc2  to be held accountable for possible war crimes and crimes against humanity committed in the Gaza Strip. Twenty-eight countries voted in favour, 13 abstained and six voted against the resolution.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Iran held a funeral on Friday for seven officers killed in a suspected Israeli airstrike on the Iranian embassy compound in Syria this week, an unprecedented attack for which Tehran has vowed to take revenge.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The findings of an investigation into the aid worker killings may come in \u8220\'20\'1Cthe next few days\u8221\'20\'1D, an Israeli spokesperson suggested to the BBC, after officials signalled earlier that it could take weeks. \uc2 WCK\uc2  has called for an \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/apr/04/world-central-kitchen-gaza-israel-strikes-biden-netanyahu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 independent, third-party investigation}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D into the Israeli strikes and asked Australia, Canada, Poland, the US and the UK \u8211\'20\'13 whose citizens were killed \u8211\'20\'13 to join them in demanding the inquiry.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/apr/04/another-former-supreme-court-judge-signs-letter-genocide-law-breach-sunak-gaza-catastrophe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fourth former supreme court justice}}}\uc2  has put his name to a letter warning the British prime minister, \uc2 Rishi Sunak\uc2 , that the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/apr/03/former-supreme-court-judges-say-uk-arming-israel-breaches-international-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 UK is breaching international law}}}\uc2  by continuing to arm Israel, as the number of legal experts signing the letter rose to more than 750. Lord Carnwath joins Lady Hale, who was president of the UK\u8217\'20\'19s highest court, and lords Sumption and Wilson in urging ministers to act to prevent the \u8220\'20\'1Cplausible risk\u8221\'20\'1D of genocide in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Israel Defense Forces\uc2  (\uc2 IDF\uc2 ) also said it again attacked what it described as \u8220\'20\'1Cterrorist infrastructure\u8221\'20\'1D in Lebanon. It identified launches \u8220\'20\'1Ccrossing from Lebanon toward the areas of Betzet and Shlomi in northern Israel\u8221\'20\'1D and struck the sources of the fire, it said. As well, \u8220\'20\'1CIDF fighter jets struck terrorist infrastructure in the areas of Yaroun, Aynata, and Maroun El Ras\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 US forces destroyed an anti-ship missile in a Houthi-controlled area of Yemen on Thursday, US central command said on Friday, adding there were no injuries or damage reported by US, coalition or commercial ships.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Israeli media reported a step up in GPS jamming inside the country, believed to be a preparation for a potential attack from Iran, which has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/apr/04/israel-on-high-alert-after-iran-missile-retaliation-threat"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 vowed revenge}}}\uc2  after an airstrike on its consulate in Damascus killed several senior military commanders.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Former US president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  urged Israel in its war with \uc2 Hamas\uc2  to \u8220\'20\'1Cget it over with fast\u8221\'20\'1D. In an interview with conservative radio host \uc2 Hugh Hewitt\uc2 , Trump said Israel was \u8220\'20\'1Cabsolutely losing the PR war\u8221\'20\'1D and called for a swift resolution to the bloodshed. \u8220\'20\'1CLet\u8217\'20\'19s get back to peace and stop killing people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A political row has developed in Israel over plans to allow members of Israel\u8217\'20\'19s ultra-Orthodox community, the Haredim, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/apr/04/israel-ultra-orthodox-jews-haredim-benjamin-netanyahu-court-military-conscription-gaza-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to be conscripted}}}\uc2 , ending a longstanding religious exemption from military service. Supporters of both sides of the argument are threatening to walk out of Netanyahu\u8217\'20\'19s wartime national coalition if they do not get their way.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 11.01am BST\par \par \uc2 Here are the latest images coming across the wires from Gaza:\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.44am BST\par \par \uc2 It is devastating that it took six months and the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/apr/02/israeli-airstrike-gaza-british-citizens-aid-workers-killed"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 killing of six western aid workers}}}\uc2  for a tipping point to be reached for Israel to change course over the supply of international humanitarian aid, the chair of the UK foreign affairs committee has said.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2024/apr/05/israel-gaza-aid-tipping-point-senior-tory-alicia-kearns"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Delay in reaching Gaza aid tipping point devastating, says senior Tory}}}\par \par \uc2 Speaking to BBC Radio 4\u8217\'20\'19s Today programme, \uc2 Alicia Kearns\uc2  said the government must suspend arms sales to Israel and claimed ministers were no longer saying that Israel was complying with international humanitarian law, merely that it had the capacity to do so.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI believe we have no choice but to suspend arms sales and it is important that the public understands this is not a political decision as some people want to present it as,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 10.13am BST\par \par \uc2 Lebanon\u8217\'20\'19s caretaker prime minister, \uc2 Najib Mikati\uc2 , has said Israeli air strikes have turned southern Lebanon into a \u8220\'20\'1Cdevastated agricultural area\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Israel and the Iranian-backed Lebanese armed group \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2  have been trading fire across Israel\u8217\'20\'19s northern border since war erupted in Gaza, with \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2  firing rockets and Israel launching air strikes and artillery shells.\par \par \uc2 The Israeli strikes have burned tens of thousands of olive trees and torched farmland across southern Lebanon, hurting herders and farmers already suffering from a deep economic crisis that has made it even more important for Lebanon to produce its own food.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CEight hundred hectares have been completely damaged, 340,000 heads of livestock have died, and about 75% of farmers have lost their final source of income,\u8221\'20\'1D Lebanon\u8217\'20\'19s National News Agency quoted Mikati as saying.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis problem will extend to the coming years.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Agriculture Minister Abbas Hajj Hassan sounded the alarm last month, saying the Israeli strikes were preventing farmers in villages and towns near the border reaching their fields, affecting up to 30% of Lebanon\u8217\'20\'19s agricultural output.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.49am BST\par \par \uc2 UN\uc2  rights body adopts resolution for Israel to be held accountable for possible war crimes in Gaza\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 United Nations Human Rights Council\uc2  on Friday adopted a resolution calling for Israel to be held accountable for possible war crimes and crimes against humanity committed in the Gaza Strip.\par \par \uc2 Twenty-eight countries voted in favour, 13 abstained and six voted against the resolution.\par \par \uc2 enltr {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/HRC55?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #HRC55}}}\uc2  | Draft resolution A/HRC/55/L.30 on the Human rights situation in the Occupied Palestinian Territory, including East Jerusalem, and the obligation to ensure accountability and justice was ADOPTED. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/URttz9IFjv"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/URttz9IFjv}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 United Nations Human Rights Council\uc2  | #HRC55 (@UN_HRC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/UN_HRC/status/1776167214678159575?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 5, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 The resolution stressed \u8220\'20\'1Cthe need to ensure accountability for all violations of international humanitarian law and international human rights law in order to end impunity\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 It also expressed \u8220\'20\'1Cgrave concern at reports of serious human rights violations and grave breaches of international humanitarian law, including of possible war crimes and crimes against humanity in the Occupied Palestinian Territory\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Meirav Eilon Shahar, Israel\u8217\'20\'19s permanent representative to the \uc2 United Nations\uc2  in Geneva, accused the Council of having \u8220\'20\'1Clong abandoned the Israeli people and long defended \uc2 Hamas\uc2 \u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAccording to the resolution before you today, Israel has no right to protect its people, while \uc2 Hamas\uc2  has every right to murder and torture innocent Israelis,\u8221\'20\'1D she said ahead of the vote. \u8220\'20\'1CA vote \u8216\'20\'18Yes\u8217\'20\'19 is a vote for \uc2 Hamas\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The United States had pledged to vote against the resolution because it did not contain a specific condemnation of \uc2 Hamas\uc2  for the Oct. 7 attacks, nor \u8220\'20\'1Cany reference to the terrorist nature of those actions\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 It did, however, said that its ally Israel had not done enough to mitigate harm to civilians.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe United States has repeatedly urged Israel to de-conflict military operations against \uc2 Hamas\uc2  with humanitarian operations, in order to avoid civilian casualties and to ensure humanitarian actors can carry out their essential mission in safety,\u8221\'20\'1D said Mich\u232\'00\'E8le Taylor, U.S. permanent representative to the Council.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThat has not happened and, in just six months, more humanitarians have been killed in this conflict than in any war of the modern era.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 U.N. Human Rights Council\uc2 , which meets several times a year, is the only intergovernmental body designed to protect human rights worldwide. It can increase scrutiny of countries\u8217\'20\'19 human rights records and authorise investigations.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 10.27am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.28am BST\par \par \uc2 Real test to Isreal's plans to increase humanitarian flow to Gaza 'is results', \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  says\par \par \uc2 The US secretary of state \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  has welcomed the steps announced by Israel on humanitarian aid to Gaza, but said \u8220\'20\'1Cthe real test is results\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The statements come after \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s office has said his security cabinet has approved a series of steps to increase the flow of humanitarian aid into {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/gaza"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gaza}}}\uc2 , including the temporary reopening of a key crossing that was destroyed in the 7 October \uc2 Hamas\uc2  attack.\par \par \uc2 The announcement was made hours after a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/apr/04/israel-us-gaza-joe-biden-benjamin-netanyahu-phone-call"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 warning from US president Joe Biden}}}\uc2  that future US support for Israel would depend on it taking concrete action to protect civilians and aid workers.\par \par \uc2 Blinken also said the US will look at the number of trucks entering and getting around Gaza, and will also look at indictators of potential famine to see if they reverse, according to Reuters.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThese are positive developments but the real test is results,\u8221\'20\'1D Blinken said.\par \par \uc2 Since 7 October, 33,091 Palestinians have been killed and 75,750 injured in Israel\u8217\'20\'19s military offensive on Gaza, according to the Gaza health ministry on Friday.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 11.09am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.14am BST\par \par \uc2 UN Human Rights Council\uc2  debating ban on arms sales to Israel\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UN Human Rights Council\uc2  was on Friday debating whether to demand a halt in arms sales to Israel, whose war in Gaza has killed more than 33,000 people, mostly civilians.\par \par \uc2 The draft text calls on countries to \u8220\'20\'1Ccease the sale, transfer and diversion of arms, munitions and other military equipment to Israel\u8221\'20\'1D. This, it said, is needed among other things \u8220\'20\'1Cto prevent further violations of international humanitarian law and violations and abuses of human rights\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 It stresses that the \uc2 International Court of Justice\uc2  ruled in January \u8220\'20\'1Cthat there is a plausible risk of genocide\u8221\'20\'1D in Gaza, AFP reports.\par \par \uc2 If the text is adopted, it would mark the first time that the \uc2 United Nations\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 top rights body has taken a position on the bloodiest-ever war to beset the besieged Palestinian territory.\par \par \uc2 Friday\u8217\'20\'19s draft resolution, which was brought forward by Pakistan on behalf of all \uc2 Organisation of Islamic Cooperation\uc2  (\uc2 OIC\uc2 ) member states except Albania, calls for \u8220\'20\'1Can immediate ceasefire\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Cfor immediate emergency humanitarian access and assistance\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 It comes after the \uc2 UN Security Council\uc2  in New York last week also finally passed a resolution calling for a ceasefire - thanks to an abstention from Washington, Israel\u8217\'20\'19s closest ally and largest arms supplier.\par \par \uc2 The rights council draft resolution does not name \uc2 Hamas\uc2  but it does condemn the firing of rockets at Israeli civilian areas and demands \u8220\'20\'1Cthe immediate release of all remaining hostages\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 It demands that Israel end its occupation of all Palestinian territories and \u8220\'20\'1Cimmediately lift its blockade on the Gaza Strip and all other forms of collective punishment\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The text, which was revised late on Thursday removing several references to genocide, continues to express \u8220\'20\'1Cgrave concern at statements by Israeli officials amounting to incitement to genocide\u8221\'20\'1D. And it urges countries to \u8220\'20\'1Cprevent the continued forcible transfer of Palestinians within and from Gaza\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 It warns in particular \u8220\'20\'1Cagainst any large-scale military operations in the city of Rafah\u8221\'20\'1D in the south of the densely populated Gaza Strip, where well over one million civilians are sheltering, warning of \u8220\'20\'1Cdevastating humanitarian consequences\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The draft resolution also condemns \u8220\'20\'1Cthe use of starvation of civilians as a method of warfare in Gaza\u8221\'20\'1D, where the \uc2 UN\uc2  has warned that famine is looming.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.51am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.55am BST\par \par \uc2 Iran held a funeral on Friday for seven officers killed in a suspected Israeli airstrike on the Iranian embassy compound in Syria this week, an unprecedented attack for which Tehran has vowed to take revenge.\par \par \uc2 The funeral coincided with the annual Quds (Jerusalem) Day, during which Iran stages large state-sponsored pro-Palestinian and anti-Israel rallies nationwide. State television showed demonstrators carrying pictures of those killed and banners with slogans such as \u8220\'20\'1CDeath to Israel\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1CDeath to America\u8221\'20\'1D, Reuters reports.\par \par \uc2 The leader of Palestinian militant group Islamic Jihad, Ziad al-Nakhala, took part in the rally in Tehran, Iranian media reported.\par \par \uc2 Among those killed in Monday\u8217\'20\'19s airstrike on the Iranian embassy compound in the Syrian capital Damascus was one of Iran\u8217\'20\'19s top soldiers, Brigadier General Mohammad Reza Zahedi, a senior commander in the Revolutionary Guard (IRGC).\par \par \uc2 It was the boldest, and deadliest, in a series of attacks that have killed Iranian officials in Syria since December.\par \par \uc2 Iran vowed harsh retaliation, raising the spectre of a wider war and prompting the Israeli armed forces to suspend leave for all combat units on Thursday, a day after they said they were mobilising more troops for air defence units.\par \par \uc2 Israeli Prime Minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  said on Thursday his country would harm \u8220\'20\'1Cwhoever harms us or plans to harm us\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The coffins of two of the killed officers were displayed in the capital, Tehran, to religious mourning chants. Some of those present waved the Palestinian flag. All seven officers were expected to be buried later on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Iran\u8217\'20\'19s Jerusalem Day rallies are held annually on the last Friday of the Muslim fasting month of Ramadan in support of Palestinians, who want East Jerusalem as the capital of a future state in territories captured by Israel in a 1967 war.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.33am BST\par \par \uc2 Should the UK stop arming Israel?\par \par \uc2 The killing of six international aid workers and their Palestinian driver this week has brought new scrutiny of Israel\u8217\'20\'19s conduct in its war in Gaza. Peter Beaumont and Patrick Wintour examine the growing backlash on Today in Focus.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/news/audio/2024/apr/05/should-the-uk-stop-arming-israel-podcast"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Should the UK stop arming Israel? \u8211\'20\'13 podcast}}}\par \par \uc2 They had told the Israelis they were there. Travelling along a coastal road in Gaza, six aid workers \u8211\'20\'13 from the UK, Poland, Australia and Canada \u8211\'20\'13 and their Palestinian driver. They had just unloaded more than 100 tonnes of humanitarian food aid brought to Gaza for the millions of people at risk of famine when suddenly a drone appeared above them and struck not once but three times. There were no survivors.\par \par \uc2 ?\par \par \uc2 As Peter Beaumont tells Michael Safi, the strikes on the team from the aid organisation \uc2 World Central Kitchen\uc2  have done what 33,000 Palestinians deaths apparently could not and outraged leaders in the UK and around the world. Israel says these strikes were an error, a tragedy, to be independently investigated.\par \par \uc2 People inspect the site where \uc2 World Central Kitchen\uc2  workers were killed in Deir al-Balah, Gaza Strip. Photograph: Abdel Kareem Hana/AP\par \par \uc2 As the Guardian\u8217\'20\'19s diplomatic editor, Patrick Wintour, explains, the mood at the highest level in the UK has noticeably shifted. Now there is an open debate among senior figures in the legal profession and at the top of politics about whether Britain should continue to arm Israel. Polling of the public suggests more than half of people believe it should stop.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.35am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.07am BST\par \par \uc2 Israel announces it will allow 'temporary' aid deliveries into northern Gaza\par \par \uc2 Israel announced on Friday that it would allow \u8220\'20\'1Ctemporary\u8221\'20\'1D aid deliveries into famine-threatened northern Gaza, hours after the United States warned of a sharp shift in its policy over Israel\u8217\'20\'19s war against \uc2 Hamas\uc2  militants.\par \par \uc2 In a tense, 30-minute phone call on Thursday, US President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  told prime minister \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  that US policy on Israel was dependent on the protection of civilians and aid workers in Gaza, the first hint of possible conditions to Washington\u8217\'20\'19s military support.\par \par \uc2 Just hours later, in the middle of the night in Jerusalem, Israel announced it would open more aid routes into the coastal Palestinian territory which Israel placed under siege at the start of the war nearly six months ago.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIsrael will allow the temporary delivery of humanitarian aid\u8221\'20\'1D through the Ashdod Port and the Erez land crossing, as well as increased deliveries from neighbouring Jordan at the Kerem Shalom crossing, Netanyahu\u8217\'20\'19s office said.\par \par \uc2 The White House quickly welcomed the moves - saying they came \u8220\'20\'1Cat the president\u8217\'20\'19s request\u8221\'20\'1D - and said they \u8220\'20\'1Cmust now be fully and rapidly implemented\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 9.52am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.00am BST\par \par \uc2 Here are the latest images coming across the wires from Gaza and elsewhere:\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 8.01am BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.44am BST\par \par \uc2 How Spain and Ireland became the \uc2 EU\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s sharpest critics of Israel\par \par \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s claim that the Israeli military\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/apr/02/gaza-aid-convoy-strike-what-happened-and-who-were-the-victims"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  killing of seven World Central Kitchen aid workers in Gaza on Monday night}}}\uc2  was \u8220\'20\'1Ca tragic incident\u8221\'20\'1D did precious little to allay the fears of Spain\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister, \uc2 Pedro S\u225\'00\'E1nchez\uc2 . Nor did his assertion that \u8220\'20\'1Cthis happens in wartime\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 S\u225\'00\'E1nchez, who has been one of the most outspoken and persistent European critics of the way in which Israel has prosecuted its war in Gaza after the terrorist atrocities of 7 October, described the Israeli prime minister\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Csupposed explanations\u8221\'20\'1D as \u8220\'20\'1Ctotally unacceptable and insufficient\u8221\'20\'1D. He added that Spain was waiting for a full and detailed account of the killings before deciding \u8220\'20\'1Cwhat action we\u8217\'20\'19ll take with regard to the government of Prime Minister Netanyahu\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 S\u225\'00\'E1nchez\u8217\'20\'19s latest remarks \u8211\'20\'13 along with his announcement on Monday that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/spain"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Spain}}}\uc2  intends to recognise a Palestinian state by July \u8211\'20\'13 are a further example of how some of the more habitually taciturn members of the \uc2 EU\uc2  have found themselves compelled to speak up amid concerns that the bloc is failing to live up to its moral, political and humanitarian duties.\par \par \uc2 Read more by my colleagues {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/samjones"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Sam Jones}}}\uc2  in Madrid, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/rorycarroll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Rory Carroll}}}\uc2  in Dublin and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/profile/lisaocarroll"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lisa O\u8217\'20\'19Carroll}}}\uc2  in Brussels here:\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/apr/05/spain-ireland-eu-critics-israel-warfare-gaza"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 How Spain and Ireland became the EU\u8217\'20\'19s sharpest critics of Israel}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.28am BST\par \par \uc2 The Australian foreign minister, \uc2 Penny Wong\uc2 , has rebuked \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  for trying to \u8220\'20\'1Cbrush aside\u8221\'20\'1D the deaths of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2024/apr/02/australian-aid-worker-zomi-frankcom-killed-idf-strike-gaza-world-central-kitchen"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Australian aid worker Zomi Frankcom}}}\uc2  and six of her colleagues in an Israeli missile attack in Gaza, labelling his remark that these things happen in war as \u8220\'20\'1Cdeeply insensitive\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Wong\u8217\'20\'19s direct personal condemnation of Netanyahu comes as the Israeli military reveals it has completed its investigation into the incident and briefed ambassadors from the countries whose citizens died in the attack.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/apr/05/zomi-frankcom-death-australian-gaza-penny-wong-benjamin-netanyahu-insensitive"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Penny Wong says Netanyahu trying to \u8216\'20\'18brush aside\u8217\'20\'19 death of Zomi Frankcom \u8216\'20\'18deeply insensitive\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI find that statement \u8230\'20\'26 frankly, for the family in particular, a pretty insensitive \u8211\'20\'13 deeply insensitive \u8211\'20\'13 thing to say,\u8221\'20\'1D Wong said of the Israeli prime minister\u8217\'20\'19s initial response.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.18am BST\par \par \uc2 Opening summary\par \par \uc2 Welcome to our latest live coverage of the Israel-Gaza war and wider Middle East crisis. Here\u8217\'20\'19s a snapshot of all the key developments.\par \par \uc2 Israel has approved the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/apr/05/israel-reopen-erez-crossing-gaza-biden-warning-war-netanyahu-palestine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reopening of the Erez crossing}}}\uc2  into northern Gaza and the temporary use of Israel\u8217\'20\'19s Ashdod port to increase humanitarian aid supplies into Gaza, a statement from the prime minister\u8217\'20\'19s office said early on Friday.\par \par \uc2 It also approved expanded entry of aid from Jordan through the Kerem Shalom crossing.\par \par \uc2 The Israeli move was announced shortly after a warning to \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  from the US president, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , and as international pressure mounts on Israel after it took responsibility for a strike that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/apr/02/charities-halt-gaza-operations-after-israeli-drones-kill-aid-workers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 killed seven workers}}}\uc2  with the \uc2 World Central Kitchen\uc2  (WCK) food charity.\par \par \uc2 In a tense call with Netanyahu on Thursday, Biden called for an \u8220\'20\'1Cimmediate ceasefire\u8221\'20\'1D and made clear that US policy would be determined by Israel taking \u8220\'20\'1Cconcrete and measurable steps\u8221\'20\'1D to address civilian harm and humanitarian suffering, according to the White House.\par \par \uc2 Right after Israel\u8217\'20\'19s announcement, the White House welcomed the moves to \u8220\'20\'1Cincrease aid flow to Gaza\u8221\'20\'1D and called for them to be \u8220\'20\'1Cfully and rapidly implemented\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In other developments:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 At least 33,037 Palestinians have been killed and 75,668 injured in the Israeli offensive on Gaza since 7 October, the territory\u8217\'20\'19s health ministry said. The \uc2 Hamas\uc2 -led ministry said on Thursday about 62 Palestinians were killed and 91 injured over the past 24 hours. It was not possible to independently verify the figures.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The findings of an investigation into the aid worker killings may come in \u8220\'20\'1Cthe next few days\u8221\'20\'1D, an Israeli spokesperson suggested to the BBC, after officials signalled earlier that it could take weeks. \uc2 WCK\uc2  has called for an \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/apr/04/world-central-kitchen-gaza-israel-strikes-biden-netanyahu"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 independent, third-party investigation}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D into the Israeli strikes and asked Australia, Canada, Poland, the US and the UK \u8211\'20\'13 whose citizens were killed \u8211\'20\'13 to join them in demanding the inquiry.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/apr/04/another-former-supreme-court-judge-signs-letter-genocide-law-breach-sunak-gaza-catastrophe"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 fourth former supreme court justice}}}\uc2  has put his name to a letter warning the British prime minister, \uc2 Rishi Sunak\uc2 , that the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/apr/03/former-supreme-court-judges-say-uk-arming-israel-breaches-international-law"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 UK is breaching international law}}}\uc2  by continuing to arm Israel, as the number of legal experts signing the letter rose to more than 750. Lord Carnwath joins Lady Hale, who was president of the UK\u8217\'20\'19s highest court, and lords Sumption and Wilson in urging ministers to act to prevent the \u8220\'20\'1Cplausible risk\u8221\'20\'1D of genocide in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Israel Defense Forces\uc2  (\uc2 IDF\uc2 ) also said it again attacked what it described as \u8220\'20\'1Cterrorist infrastructure\u8221\'20\'1D in Lebanon. It identified launches \u8220\'20\'1Ccrossing from Lebanon toward the areas of Betzet and Shlomi in northern Israel\u8221\'20\'1D and struck the sources of the fire, it said. As well, \u8220\'20\'1CIDF fighter jets struck terrorist infrastructure in the areas of Yaroun, Aynata, and Maroun El Ras\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 US forces destroyed an anti-ship missile in a Houthi-controlled area of Yemen on Thursday, US central command said on Friday, adding there were no injuries or damage reported by US, coalition or commercial ships.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Israeli media reported a step up in GPS jamming inside the country, believed to be a preparation for a potential attack from Iran, which has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/apr/04/israel-on-high-alert-after-iran-missile-retaliation-threat"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 vowed revenge}}}\uc2  after an airstrike on its consulate in Damascus killed several senior military commanders.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Former US president \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  urged Israel in its war with \uc2 Hamas\uc2  to \u8220\'20\'1Cget it over with fast\u8221\'20\'1D. In an interview with conservative radio host \uc2 Hugh Hewitt\uc2 , Trump said Israel was \u8220\'20\'1Cabsolutely losing the PR war\u8221\'20\'1D and called for a swift resolution to the bloodshed. \u8220\'20\'1CLet\u8217\'20\'19s get back to peace and stop killing people.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A political row has developed in Israel over plans to allow members of Israel\u8217\'20\'19s ultra-Orthodox community, the Haredim, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/apr/04/israel-ultra-orthodox-jews-haredim-benjamin-netanyahu-court-military-conscription-gaza-war"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to be conscripted}}}\uc2 , ending a longstanding religious exemption from military service. Supporters of both sides of the argument are threatening to walk out of Netanyahu\u8217\'20\'19s wartime national coalition if they do not get their way.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240405ek45000rx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
