\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 Biden hails \u8216\'20\'18America\u8217\'20\'19s comeback\u8217\'20\'19 as 303,000 new jobs in March beat forecast\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 558 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 April 2024\par 16:47 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Unemployment rate at 3.8% while job gains well above the 192,000 economists expected for the month\par \par \uc2 The US workforce added 303,000 jobs last month, far more than expected and the 39th straight month of job gains in the US. The unemployment rate dipped to 3.8%.\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden hailed the report as \u8220\'20\'1Ca milestone in America\u8217\'20\'19s comeback\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThree years ago, I inherited an economy on the brink. With today\u8217\'20\'19s report of 303,000 new jobs in March, we have passed the milestone of 15m jobs created since I took office. That\u8217\'20\'19s 15 million more people who have the dignity and respect that comes with a paycheck,\u8221\'20\'1D he said.\par \par \uc2 Economists had expected the US to add 192,000 jobs for the month. Hiring has remained surprisingly strong despite the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s attempts to cool inflation by raising interest rates.\par \par \uc2 Over the last 16 months, the Fed has raised its benchmark {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/interest-rates-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 interest rates}}}\uc2  from near zero to over 5%. Hikes have been paused recently and the Fed chair, \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.morningstar.com/markets/march-jobs-report-forecasts-show-still-strong-slowing-hiring-gains"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  in March that the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/mar/06/jerome-powell-interest-rate-cuts"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 central bank would cut rates}}}\uc2  in response to a perceived weakness in the jobs market. The next rate decision is in May.\par \par \uc2 Inflation has cooled as rates have risen. The annual rate of price rises {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/mar/12/us-inflation-rate-february"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was 3.2%}}}\uc2  in February, down from a high of over 9% in June 2022. And to the surprise of many economists hiring has remained robust. Unemployment has now been below 4% for two years, the longest such streak in decades and down from 6.7% when Biden took office.\par \par \uc2 Healthcare, government and construction led the gains and the labor department reported that employment in leisure and hospitality returned to pre-pandemic levels in February.\par \par \uc2 Wages rose by 0.3% from the previous month and were up 4.1% over the year, the smallest gain since June 2021.\par \par \uc2 While the report was far stronger than expected, it once again highlighted the racial disparities in the US jobs market. The Black unemployment rate rose 0.8% to 6.4%, its highest level since August 2022. Rates for Asians (2.5%) and Hispanics (4.5%) decreased while White unemployment was unchanged at 3.4%.\par \par \uc2 The report is likely to bolster the Fed\u8217\'20\'19s reluctance to begin cutting rates soon.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CReducing rates too soon or too much could result in a reversal in the progress we\u8217\'20\'19ve seen on inflation and ultimately require even tighter policy to get inflation back to 2%,\u8221\'20\'1D Powell said this week at a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://abcnews.go.com/Business/fed-chair-jerome-powell-pumps-brakes-rate-cuts/story?id=108792470#:~:text=%E2%80%9CReducing%20rates%20too%20soon%20or,weaken%20economic%20activity%20and%20employment.%E2%80%9D"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 business conference}}}\uc2  at Stanford. \u8220\'20\'1CBut easing policy too late or too little could unduly weaken economic activity and employment.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Paul Ashworth\uc2 , chief North America economist at \uc2 Capital Economics\uc2 , said the \u8220\'20\'1Cblockbuster\u8221\'20\'1D report \u8220\'20\'1Csupports the Fed\u8217\'20\'19s position that the resilience of the economy means it can take its time with rate cuts, which might now not begin until the second half of this year\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In February 2024, non-farm employment in the US {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bls.gov/news.release/pdf/empsit.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 increased}}}\uc2  by a revised 270,000 jobs, with the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/mar/08/us-jobs-february-growth-layoffs"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 unemployment rate rising to 3.9%}}}\uc2  from 3.7% the month prior.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday ADP, the country\u8217\'20\'19s largest private payroll company, said US businesses added 184,000 new positions in March, the largest rise since July last year.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240405ek45001p7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
