\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Biden tells Netanyahu Gaza aid strikes \u8216\'20\'18unacceptable\u8217\'20\'19 and Israel must end civilian suffering to keep US support \u8211\'20\'13 as it happened\b0\par\par\uc2 L\u233\'00\'E9onie Chao-Fong (now) and Gloria Oladipo (earlier) \par \uc2 5,889 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 April 2024\par 20:13 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This live blog is now closed. For more on the Biden-Netanyahu phone call, you can read our full report:Protect civilians and aid workers or risk losing US support, Biden tells Israel\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 9.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Closing summary\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has told \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  that future US support for the war in Gaza {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/04/israel-gaza-war-biden-netanyahu-latest-updates?page=with:block-660ee5f88f08d7255e640f8d#block-660ee5f88f08d7255e640f8d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will depend on }}}\uc2  Israel taking concrete action to protect civilians and aid workers, as the two leaders held their first phone call since Israeli airstrikes {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://theguardian.com/world/2024/apr/03/very-best-of-humanity-the-seven-aid-workers-killed-in-israeli-airstrike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 killed seven employees }}}\uc2  of the international food charity \uc2 World Central Kitchen\uc2  (\uc2 WCK\uc2 ). Biden\u8217\'20\'19s comments were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/04/israel-gaza-war-biden-netanyahu-latest-updates?page=with:block-660efc7b8f085621a6804c71#block-660efc7b8f085621a6804c71"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 echoed }}}\uc2  by his secretary of state, \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2 , who said US support would be curtailed if Israel failed to adjust its conduct.\par \par \uc2 Also:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 The centrist group No Labels{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/apr/04/no-labels-drops-out-candidate-presidential-election"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  it will not field a third-party candidate for US president this year.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A federal judge {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/04/israel-gaza-war-biden-netanyahu-latest-updates?page=with:block-660ef7568f089fcebeb9cdf5#block-660ef7568f089fcebeb9cdf5"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 refused to throw out }}}\uc2  the classified documents prosecution against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , rejecting a defense argument that the case should be tossed because he was entitled as a former president to retain the records after he left office.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 A Georgia judge {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/04/israel-gaza-war-biden-netanyahu-latest-updates?page=with:block-660edf578f08d7255e640f52#block-660edf578f08d7255e640f52"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rejected}}}\uc2 Trump \u8217\'20\'19s bid to dismiss criminal charges in the state\u8217\'20\'19s election interference against him on first amendment grounds.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 Biden will travel to Baltimore tomorrow to receive an operational update on response efforts after the collapse of the Francis Scott Key Bridge, the White House said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.38pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s more from secretary of state \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s briefing following a Nato meeting of foreign ministers in Brussels.\par \par \uc2 Blinken, speaking to reporters, reaffirmed the US\u8217\'20\'19s commitment for Ukraine to eventually join \uc2 Nato\uc2  but held back commitments ahead of the alliance\u8217\'20\'19s annual summit, which will take place in July. He said:\par \par \uc2 Ukraine will become a member of Nato. Our purpose at the summit is to help build a bridge to that membership.\par \par \uc2 He added that more aid is urgently needed for Ukraine, and that the message from \uc2 Nato\uc2  allies was clear that the Congress vote on aid for Ukraine cannot happen soon enough.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.28pm BST\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration issued a new rule on Thursday making it harder to fire thousands of federal employees, hoping to head off the risk that if \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  wins back the White House in November he won\u8217\'20\'19t be able to bully and decimate the workforce as he imposes the radical ideologies he\u8217\'20\'19s been pushing on the campaign trail, escalating what he did while in office.\par \par \uc2 New regulations coming out of the government\u8217\'20\'19s chief human resources agency, the Office of Personnel Management, will bar career civil servants from being reclassified as political appointees or as other at-will workers \u8211\'20\'13 who are more easily dismissed from their jobs.\par \par \uc2 The move comes in response to so-called \u8220\'20\'1CSchedule F\u8221\'20\'1D, an executive order Trump issued in 2020 that sought to allow for reclassifying tens of thousands of the 2.2m federal employees and thus reduce their job security protections.\par \par \uc2 Biden nullified Schedule F upon taking office. But if Trump were to win the election for the Republicans and revive it during a second administration, he could dramatically increase number of federal employees \u8211\'20\'13 about 4,000 \u8211\'20\'13 who are considered political appointees and typically change with each new president.\par \par \uc2 In a statement issued Thursday, Biden called the rule a \u8220\'20\'1Cstep toward combatting corruption and partisan interference to ensure civil servants are able to focus on the most important task at hand: delivering for the American people\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s a clip from the secretary of state, \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2 , who spoke about \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s warning to Israel\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister, \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 , that future US support for the war in Gaza depends on the swift implementation of new steps to protect civilians and aid workers.\par \par \uc2 The president \u8220\'20\'1Cmade clear the need for Israel to announce and implement a series of specific, concrete, and measurable steps to address civilian harm, humanitarian suffering, and the safety of aid workers,\u8221\'20\'1D the White House said in a statement after a call between Biden and Netanyahu.\par \par \uc2 Speaking to reporters in Brussels, Blinken said:\par \par \uc2 If we don\u8217\'20\'19t see the changes that we need to see, there\u8217\'20\'19ll be changes in our own policy.\par \par \uc2 enltr\u8220\'20\'1CWith regard to our policy in Gaza... if we don't see the changes that we need to see, there'll be changes in our own policy.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Sec. of State \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2 , when asked what changes there will be if Israel doesn't create specific steps to protect civilians and aid workers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/hUSIbarGKj"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/hUSIbarGKj}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 The Recount (@therecount) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/therecount/status/1775961270535196985?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 4, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 No Labels drops bid for third-party election ticket after spending millions\par \par \uc2 The centrist political group No Labels will not run a third-party campaign for the presidency in the 2024 election, after the group spent millions trying to recruit a candidate.\par \par \uc2 It emerged on Thursday afternoon that the group plans to announce it won\u8217\'20\'19t field a so-called \u8220\'20\'1Cunity ticket\u8221\'20\'1D that even if it was a long shot for the White House threaten to undermine \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  or \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s campaigns. The story was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/no-labels-will-abandon-2024-presidential-campaign-effort-4b4e5121?mod=hp_lead_pos2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first reported}}}\uc2  by the Wall Street Journal and then reported by the Associated Press.\par \par \uc2 Democrats were particularly concerned that it would drain enough support from the president that he could lose his re-election bid, handing the White House back to former president Trump, who is signaling an even more extremist hard-right agenda if he wins a second term.\par \par \uc2 Conservative Democratic Senator Joe Manchin of West Virginia and \uc2 Nikki Haley\uc2 , a Republican candidate for the nomination who lost out to Trump in the primaries, including losing her home state of South Carolina, where she had been a governor, were just two names floated for a No Labels ticket who reportedly turned the opportunity down.\par \par \uc2 No Labels was founded in 2009 by Nancy Jacobson, a prominent Washington political fundraiser.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 8.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Lawyers for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  had argued the criminal case charging him with retaining classified documents should be dismissed on grounds of presidential immunity, claiming they were his to keep because he designated them personal records while he was president.\par \par \uc2 The decision to designate the documents as personal records under the Presidential Records Act meant it was an official act of his presidency for which he could not face prosecution, his lawyers said.\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors working with the special counsel \uc2 Jack Smith\uc2  disputed the former president\u8217\'20\'19s depiction of the records as personal. Trump was not authorized to hold on to secret information related to national security after leaving the White House even if he viewed the records as personal, they argued.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.58pm BST\par \par \uc2 Trump loses bid to dismiss classified documents case on personal records claim\par \par \uc2 A federal judge has rejected \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s motion to dismiss the criminal case over his retention of classified information because he viewed the material as his personal records.\par \par \uc2 Trump faces 40 charges arising from his retention of classified information after leaving the White House and alleged obstruction of attempts to recover such records. He has pleaded not guilty.\par \par \uc2 enltrBREAKING: Judge Cannon denies Trump's motion to dismiss the Mar-a-Lago classified docs case on Presidential Records Act grounds {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/llOQyugV4D"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/llOQyugV4D}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Hugo Lowell (@hugolowell) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hugolowell/status/1775959981973537109?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 4, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden feeling 'growing frustration' with Netanyahu, says White House\par \par \uc2 John Kirby, the national security spokesperson, said the call between \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  lasted about 30 minutes.\par \par \uc2 Asked if there had been growing frustration on the part of Biden that his previous messages to the Israeli leader hadn\u8217\'20\'19t gotten through, Kirby said:\par \par \uc2 Yes, there\u8217\'20\'19s been growing frustration.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.29pm BST\par \par \uc2 White House spokesman refuses to say what Israel policies US could change\par \par \uc2 At a White House briefing, national security council spokesperson John Kirby was repeatedly asked what the US policy changes are on the table that would be determined by Washington\u8217\'20\'19s assessment of Israel\u8217\'20\'19s steps to address civilian harm in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 Kirby said he was not going to preview any potential policy decisions.\par \par \uc2 What we want to see are some real changes on the Israeli side. We don\u8217\'20\'19t see changes from their side.\par \par \uc2 The US is looking for \u8220\'20\'1Cconcrete, tangible\u8221\'20\'1D steps \u8220\'20\'1Cin the coming hours and days\u8221\'20\'1D that would include a dramatic increase in the humanitarian assistance getting into Gaza, additional crossings opening up, and a reduction in the violence against civilians and aid workers, he said.\par \par \uc2 We want to see that the Israelis are willing and able to take practical, immediate steps to protect a workers on the ground and to demonstrate that they have that civilian harm mitigation in place.\par \par \uc2 He said the US will \u8220\'20\'1Cwatch closely\u8221\'20\'1D for what steps Israel will take, and that Washington is not looking for just an announcement \u8220\'20\'1Cbut it\u8217\'20\'19s the execution of those announcements and those decisions and implementing them.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.18pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will travel to Baltimore tomorrow to receive an operational update on response efforts after the collapse of the Francis Scott Key Bridge, the White House said.\par \par \uc2 The president will meet with the loved ones of the six individuals who went missing and are presumed dead as a result of the incident, the White House\u8217\'20\'19s press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.21pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.07pm BST\par \par \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  said he was \u8220\'20\'1Coutraged\u8221\'20\'1D by the Israeli strike that killed seven aid workers in Gaza on Monday, and that he \u8220\'20\'1Cstrongly\u8221\'20\'1D condemns it.\par \par \uc2 He said the US\u8217\'20\'19s conviction remains to see an immediate ceasefire to enable the release of hostages, and to enable a dramatic surge in humanitarian assistance, as well as better protecting civilians.\par \par \uc2 It is our expectation that Israel will and certainly should announce concrete, specific, measurable steps that it will take, and take as soon as possible to make sure that there can be an effective surge and assistance, that it can be sustained, and that humanitarian workers and civilians are better protected.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.04pm BST\par \par \uc2 Blinken suggests 'changes in policy' if Israel takes no action\par \par \uc2 Asked what aspects of US policy with respect to Gaza could change if Israel does not taken immediate concrete steps, \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  did not expand. He said:\par \par \uc2 If we don\u8217\'20\'19t see the changes that we need to see, there\u8217\'20\'19ll be changes in policy.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 7.00pm BST\par \par \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  said the current reality in Gaza is that \u8220\'20\'1Cdespite important steps that Israel has taken to allow assistance into Gaza\u8221\'20\'1D, the results on the ground are \u8220\'20\'1Cwoefully insufficient and unacceptable\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Humanitarian workers bringing aid into Gaza are doing so \u8220\'20\'1Cheroically \u8230\'20\'26 in great peril to their own lives\u8221\'20\'1D, he said.\par \par \uc2 This week\u8217\'20\'19s horrific attack on \uc2 World Central Kitchen\uc2  was not the first such incident. It must be the last.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 7.09pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.53pm BST\par \par \uc2 Blinken: Biden told Netanyahu strikes on aid workers in Gaza 'unacceptable'\par \par \uc2 The US secretary of state, \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2 , is currently holding a news conference in Brussels, where he is speaking about the recent call between \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and Israel\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister, \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Biden \u8220\'20\'1Cemphasized that the strikes on humanitarian workers and the overall humanitarian situation are unacceptable\u8221\'20\'1D, Blinken said, echoing the White House\u8217\'20\'19s readout of the phone call.\par \par \uc2 The US president \u8220\'20\'1Cmade clear the need for Israel to announce a series of specific, concrete and measurable steps to address civilian harm, humanitarian suffering and the safety of aid workers,\u8221\'20\'1D Blinken said.\par \par \uc2 He made clear that US policy with respect to Gaza will be determined by our assessment of Israel\u8217\'20\'19s immediate action on these steps He underscored as well that an immediate ceasefire is essential to stabilize and improve the humanitarian situation and protect innocent civilians.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  also \u8220\'20\'1Cdiscussed public Iranian threats against Israel and the Israeli people\u8221\'20\'1D, the White House said.\par \par \uc2 Biden \u8220\'20\'1Cmade clear that the US strongly supports Israel in the face of those threats\u8221\'20\'1D, it said.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.45pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden told Netanyahu that US support depends on Israel's immediate new steps in Gaza - White House\par \par \uc2 The White House has released a readout of the phone call between \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and the Israeli prime minister, \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The US president emphasized that the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/apr/02/gaza-aid-convoy-strike-what-happened-and-who-were-the-victims"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 strikes on humanitarian workers}}}\uc2  and the overall humanitarian situation are \u8220\'20\'1Cunacceptable\u8221\'20\'1D, the White House said.\par \par \uc2 Biden \u8220\'20\'1Cmade clear the need for Israel to announce and implement a series of specific, concrete, and measurable steps to address civilian harm, humanitarian suffering, and the safety of aid workers\u8221\'20\'1D, it said.\par \par \uc2 He made clear that U.S. policy with respect to Gaza will be determined by our assessment of Israel\u8217\'20\'19s immediate action on these steps. He underscored that an immediate ceasefire is essential to stabilize and improve the humanitarian situation and protect innocent civilians, and he urged the prime minister to empower his negotiators to conclude a deal without delay to bring the hostages home.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 The White House has confirmed that a phone call between \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  has ended.\par \par \uc2 A readout of the call will be issued soon, it said.\par \par \uc2 The call between the two leaders lasted less than 30 minutes, Reuters reported, citing a White House official.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 Georgia judge rejects Trump free speech challenge to election interference case\par \par \uc2 A Georgia judge has rejected \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s bid to dismiss criminal charges in the state\u8217\'20\'19s election interference against him on first amendment grounds.\par \par \uc2 In a 14-page ruling, Fulton County superior court judge Scott McAfee found that the indictment alleges statements by Trump and his co-defendants were made \u8220\'20\'1Cin furtherance of criminal activity\u8221\'20\'1D and are not protected under free speech rights.\par \par \uc2 The court \u8220\'20\'1Cfinds these vital constitutional protections do not reach the actions and statements alleged\u8221\'20\'1D by the state, he wrote. Their motions to dismiss are \u8220\'20\'1Ctherefore denied\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 My colleague Hugo Lowell has a statement by Trump\u8217\'20\'19s lawyer responding to the judge\u8217\'20\'19s ruling:\par \par \uc2 enltrTrump lawyer Steve Sadow statement: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/6WlxCUwL1V"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/6WlxCUwL1V}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Hugo Lowell (@hugolowell) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hugolowell/status/1775933441332376019?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 April 4, 2024}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 6.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 A phone call between \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  has ended after about 45 minutes, the Times of Israel is reporting.\par \par \uc2 We\u8217\'20\'19ll bring you more information as soon as we hear it.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.55pm BST\par \par \uc2 Elizabeth Warren said that she would block the sale of F-15s to Israel after an Israeli strike killed seven aid workers, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/homenews/senate/4574559-warren-block-sale-f-15s-israel/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  the Hill reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Massachusetts senator said that Congress had a \u8220\'20\'1Cresponsibility to act\u8221\'20\'1D and accused Israel of violating laws that require an access to humanitarian relief, during an interview with CNN News Central.\par \par \uc2 I think it is clear that Congress has a responsibility to act. We have legal tools here. And as I said, we cannot approve the sale of arms to a country that is in violation of our own laws on this. And that includes access to humanitarian relief\u8230\'20\'26This is a moral question, it is also a legal question. Congress has responsibility here and I\u8217\'20\'19m willing to take that responsibility\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 Warren did not confirm if she is putting legislation on the floor to block any potential sale.\par \par \uc2 When asked, Warren said:\par \par \uc2 Actually, let\u8217\'20\'19s put this in a slightly different context. We already have an established U.S. policy here.\par \par \uc2 Warren\u8217\'20\'19s comments come as the US is preparing to sell Israel up to 50 F-15 fighter jets, 30 medium-range Air-to-Air Missiles, and other weapons, the Hill reported.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.10pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.31pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden and Netanyahu speaking now in first call since aid workers were killed\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  are now speaking for the first time since the Israeli attack on seven aid workers from \uc2 World Central Kitchen\uc2 , CNN reports.\par \par \uc2 The phone call comes after the US president has increasingly criticized the Israeli prime minister for failing to protect relief workers amid ongoing airstrikes in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 The White House previously said that Biden is outraged at the killing of relief workers. But Biden has not made changes to the US\u8217\'20\'19s support of Israel or add conditions on any weapons sold.\par \par \uc2 Prior to Thursday\u8217\'20\'19s conversation, a US official said that Biden is expected to bring up the need for better protections of aid workers and press for increased food deliveries in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 Hundreds of thousands of people in Gaza face starvation as Israel\u8217\'20\'19s war in the territory continues.\par \par \uc2 More than 25 children in Gaza have died from complications associated with malnourishment, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.emro.who.int/images/stories/Sitrep_-_issue_26c.pdf?itid=lk_inline_enhanced-template"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the World Health Organization reported}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.11pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 5.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 It is unclear if Biden\u8217\'20\'19s outrage at the killing of aid workers by Israeli strikes will cause him to put conditions on weapons sent to Israel.\par \par \uc2 The White House has not confirmed if Biden\u8217\'20\'19s fury at the situation will lead to consequences for Israel, the \uc2 New York Times\uc2  reported.\par \par \uc2 But Biden has harshly criticized Israel ahead of a call between Biden and Netanyahu scheduled for Thursday. Following the air strike against the \uc2 World Central Kitchen\uc2  (\uc2 WCK\uc2 ) convoy, Biden said that Israel \u8220\'20\'1Chas not done enough to protect aid workers,\u8221\'20\'1D the Times reported.\par \par \uc2 Other Democrats have more clearly called for Biden to \u8220\'20\'1C[change] course\u8221\'20\'1D after the killing of \uc2 WCK\uc2  relief workers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI hope this will be the moment where the president changes course,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Chris Van Hollen\uc2 , a Democratic Senator from Maryland, to the Times.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNetanyahu ignored the president\u8217\'20\'19s requests, and yet we send 2,000-pound bombs with no restrictions on their use,\u8221\'20\'1D he added.\par \par \uc2 But Democratic leaders have declined to call for restrictions on arms to Israel.\par \par \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2 , the Senate majority leader, declined to support a limit on the use of weapons, later refusing to discuss the topic with the Times.\par \par \uc2 Read the full analysis from the Times here ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/04/03/us/politics/biden-israel-gaza.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 paywall}}}\uc2  ).\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.56pm BST\par \par \uc2 The international food charity \uc2 World Central Kitchen\uc2  (\uc2 WCK\uc2 ) has called for an independent investigation into the Israeli strikes that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/apr/03/very-best-of-humanity-the-seven-aid-workers-killed-in-israeli-airstrike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 killed seven of its aid workers in Gaza}}}\uc2  on Monday, as \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  were expected to discuss the attack on the phone.\par \par \uc2 WCK\uc2  asked Australia, Canada, Poland, the US and the UK, whose citizens were killed, to join it in demanding \u8220\'20\'1Can independent, third-party\u8217\'20\'19\u8217\'20\'19 inquiry into the strikes.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis was a military attack that involved multiple strikes and targeted three \uc2 WCK\uc2  vehicles,\u8221\'20\'1D the charity said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 All three vehicles were carrying civilians; they were marked as \uc2 WCK\uc2  vehicles; and their movements were in full compliance with Israeli authorities, who were aware of their itinerary, route and humanitarian mission. An independent investigation is the only way to determine the truth of what happened, ensure transparency and accountability for those responsible, and prevent future attacks on humanitarian aid workers.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.12pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 World Central Kitchen\uc2  (\uc2 WCK\uc2 ) was one of few aid organizations permitted by Israeli authorities to deliver food to northern Gaza and has brought hundreds of tonnes of food aid into the Palestinian territory.\par \par \uc2 On Monday night, a convoy of three armored cars belonging to \uc2 WCK\uc2  was attacked while leaving a warehouse in Deir al-Balah.\par \par \uc2 According to a report in the Israeli daily Haaretz, an Israeli drone fired three missiles at the convoy of three armored cars \u8211\'20\'13 all of which were clearly marked on the roof and sides with the \uc2 WCK\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s logo \u8211\'20\'13 as they travelled back along a route pre-approved and coordinated with the \uc2 Israel Defense Forces\uc2  (IDF).\par \par \uc2 An Hermes 450 drone struck one car, causing some of the passengers to abandon it and switch to the other two vehicles. According to Haaretz, the team notified the \uc2 IDF\uc2  they had been attacked, but another missile then hit the second car.\par \par \uc2 Passengers in the third car tried to help the wounded, the newspaper said. According to the \uc2 Guardian\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s geolocation of the strikes, the last car was hit by a third missile about a mile farther south.\par \par \uc2 Video obtained by Reuters showed a large hole in the roof of a four-wheel-drive WCK vehicle and its burnt and torn interior, as well as paramedics moving bodies into a hospital and displaying the passports of three of those killed.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://interactive.guim.co.uk/uploader/embed/2024/04/gaza_vehicles/giv-13425IchCLZXyh1YK/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Interactive}}}\par \par \uc2 The seven victims were named by \uc2 WCK\uc2  as Britons John Chapman, 57, James Henderson, 33, and James Kirby, 47, who were working for the charity\u8217\'20\'19s security team. The team\u8217\'20\'19s leader, Lalzawmi (Zomi) Frankcom, 43, an Australian national, also died, along with American-Canadian dual citizen Jacob Flickinger, 33, Polish national Damian Sobol, 35, and Palestinian Saif Issam Abu Taha, 25.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.13pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 Ahead of an expected call between \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2  today, Israel has said it will \u8220\'20\'1Cadjust our practices\u8221\'20\'1D after seven aid workers working for \uc2 World Central Kitchen\uc2  (\uc2 WCK\uc2 ) were killed in an Israeli strike in Gaza on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Asked to respond to comments by \uc2 WCK\uc2  founder Jos\u233\'00\'E9 Andr\u233\'00\'E9s, who has said he believes his workers were {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/04/israel-gaza-war-biden-netanyahu-latest-updates?page=with:block-660eb4888f08d7255e640c2c#block-660eb4888f08d7255e640c2c"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Csystematically\u8221\'20\'1D targeted}}}\uc2  by \uc2 Israel Defense Forces\uc2 , Israeli government spokesperson Raquela Karamson said:\par \par \uc2 This was unintended \u8230\'20\'26 In the coming weeks, as the findings become clear, we will be transparent and share the results with the public.\par \par \uc2 Speaking during a media briefing on Thursday, she added:\par \par \uc2 Clearly something went wrong here, and as we learn more and the investigation reveals exactly what happened, and the cause of what happened, we will certainly adjust our practices in the future to make sure this does not happen again.\par \par \uc2 The Israeli government had previously confirmed its military had carried out \u8220\'20\'1Can unintended strike\u8221\'20\'1D, with Israeli defense sources saying that the aid workers\u8217\'20\'19 vehicles had been hit three times by missiles because of erroneous suspicions that a terrorist was traveling with the convoy.\par \par \uc2 Andr\u233\'00\'E9s has insisted that his team was in clear communication with the Israeli military, which he said knew his aid workers\u8217\'20\'19 movements, and that the convoy \u8220\'20\'1Chad signs in the top, in the roof, a very colorful logo \u8230\'20\'26 [it is] very clear who we are and what we do.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 4.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jill Biden privately urged \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  to end conflict in Gaza - report\par \par \uc2 Jill Biden pleaded with her husband, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , to \u8220\'20\'1Cstop it, stop it now\u8221\'20\'1D, referring to the war in Gaza, the president told guests at the White House, according to a report.\par \par \uc2 At a meeting with Muslim community members on Tuesday, a guest told Biden that his wife had disapproved of him attending the event because of the president\u8217\'20\'19s support for Israel in its war in Gaza, the \uc2 New York Times{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/04/03/us/politics/jill-biden-israel-hamas.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  reported }}}\uc2  yesterday. The report states:\par \par \uc2 Mr Biden replied that he understood. The first lady, he said, had been urging him to \u8216\'20\'18Stop it, stop it now,\u8217\'20\'19 according to an attendee who heard his remarks.\par \par \uc2 Asked about the president\u8217\'20\'19s remarks, the White House said Jill Biden was not calling for Israel to end its war in Gaza, the paper said. In a statement, the first lady\u8217\'20\'19s communications director Elizabeth Alexander said:\par \par \uc2 Just like the president, the first lady is heartbroken over the attacks on aid workers and the ongoing loss of innocent lives in Gaza. They both want Israel to do more to protect civilians.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.49pm BST\par \par \uc2 At home, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  \u8217\'20\'19s material support of Israel has alienated Arab Americans, other minorities, young and progressive Democrats, and as a result has jeopardised his prospects for winning the key swing state of Michigan at the very least, and with it possibly the whole general election.\par \par \uc2 A policy U-turn now would not be guaranteed to win those votes back, while it would risk alienating the instinctively pro-Israel parts of the Democratic coalition.\par \par \uc2 The last president to threaten to block weapons supplies to Israel was Republican \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2 , while the last Democratic president to seriously alienate Jewish Americans in his own party was \uc2 Jimmy Carter\uc2 , who authorised secret contacts in 1979 with the Palestinian Liberation Organisation, and paid an electoral price the following year, losing the 1980 election.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.47pm BST\par \par \uc2 Administration officials have faced questions almost daily as to why \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has not restricted or conditioned military aid on a change of Israeli behavior in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 The stock response has been that the Biden administration, while urging Israel to do more to protect the civilians of Gaza, should do nothing to limit Israel\u8217\'20\'19s ability to defend itself, a touchstone of US foreign policy for more than half a century.\par \par \uc2 Democrats of all hues, whether they support the current policy or not, say that a change of course by the Biden administration on arms supplies is highly unlikely, for both policy and political reasons.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CHe is not going to do it. He fundamentally believes Israel has a right to defend itself, and he believes that in his heart,\u8221\'20\'1D said a former senior Biden administration official of the president, adding: \u8220\'20\'1CThere is zero probability in my view.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s personal sense of commitment to Israel, cemented over decades of close contact with Israeli leaders, is a large part of the reason his administration is so resistant to change.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.37pm BST\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/29/us-approves-weapons-bombs-israel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported approval}}}\uc2  last week of billions of dollars worth of US bombs and planes for Israel, as well as the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/04/israel-gaza-war-biden-netanyahu-latest-updates?page=with:block-660eb0518f089fcebeb9c92b#block-660eb0518f089fcebeb9c92b"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported transfer}}}\uc2  of thousands of bombs to Israel on the same day Israeli airstrikes killed seven aid workers, comes amid growing questions as to why continued US military aid is not being made conditional on a change of Israeli behavior to limit the civilian death toll and significantly expand aid delivery.\par \par \uc2 Among the weapons that were reportedly approved last week to Israel were 1,800 MK-84 2,000lb bombs, which can flatten an apartment block and leave an 11-metre deep crater. It is a devastating weapon that has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnn.com/gaza-israel-big-bombs/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly been used frequently}}}\uc2  by the Israeli air force, playing a significant role in the estimated 33,000 death toll in Gaza since October.\par \par \uc2 The news that the nearly $4bn a year arms pipeline from the US to Israel remained in full uninterrupted flow drew a furious reaction from critics, who pointed to the irony of the Biden administration urging a ceasefire and the delivery of food aid into Gaza while supplying the weapons that fuel both the war and the humanitarian crisis.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://interactive.guim.co.uk/uploader/embed/2024/04/us-foreignassistancechart/giv-13425lmdytnxtfcrn/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Interactive}}}\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.16pm BST\par \par \uc2 Jos\u233\'00\'E9 Andr\u233\'00\'E9s, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/apr/02/chef-jose-andres-israeli-strike-kills-aid-workers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 celebrity chef and founder of the non-profit World Central Kitchen (WCK),}}}\uc2  has condemned Israeli airstrikes that killed seven of his aid workers in Gaza and called for an investigation of the incident by the \uc2 US government\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Andr\u233\'00\'E9s, who is Spanish born and now a US citizen, in an interview yesterday said the Israeli attack had targeted his workers taking food shipments from a warehouse in Deir al-Balah \u8220\'20\'1Csystematically, car by car\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 He said the \uc2 WCK\uc2  had clear communication with the Israeli military, which he said knew his aid workers\u8217\'20\'19 movements.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis was not just a bad luck situation where \u8216\'20\'18oops\u8217\'20\'19 we dropped the bomb in the wrong place,\u8221\'20\'1D he said, rejecting Israeli and US assertions that the strike was not deliberate. He said:\par \par \uc2 They were targeting us in a deconflicting zone, in an area controlled by \uc2 IDF\uc2  [\uc2 Israel Defense Forces\uc2 ]. They knowing that it was our teams moving on that road... with three cars.\par \par \uc2 block-time updated-timeUpdated at 6.14pm BST\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 3.06pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden administration approved more bombs to Israel on day of Gaza aid convoy strike - report\par \par \uc2 The US authorized the transfer of thousands of bombs to Israel on the same day {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/apr/02/gaza-aid-convoy-strike-what-happened-and-who-were-the-victims"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Israeli airstrikes killed seven aid workers}}}\uc2  working for the \uc2 World Central Kitchen\uc2  (\uc2 WCK\uc2 ) in Gaza, the \uc2 Washington Post{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/national-security/2024/04/04/world-central-kitchen-us-weapons-israel/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reported, }}}\uc2  citing multiple officials.\par \par \uc2 The state department approved the transfer of more than 1,000 MK82 500lb bombs, more than 1,000 small-diameter bombs, and fuses for MK80 bombs to Israel, it said. The transfer authorization was also reported by CNN.\par \par \uc2 According to the Post, a state department confirmed the approval and said it occurred sometime \u8220\'20\'1Cprior\u8221\'20\'1D to when the Israeli aircraft struck the aid convoy. A day after the attack, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  released a statement that he was {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2024/apr/04/israel-gaza-war-biden-netanyahu-latest-updates?page=with:block-660ea7458f085621a68046e4#block-660ea7458f085621a68046e4"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1Coutraged and heartbroken\u8221\'20\'1D }}}\uc2  by the deaths of the aid workers, which included a US-Canada dual citizen.\par \par \uc2 Last week, the US {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/29/us-approves-weapons-bombs-israel"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly authorized }}}\uc2  the transfer of similar weaponry worth billions of dollars to Israel, including more than 1,800 MK-84 2,000lb bombs and 500 MK-82 500lb bombs.\par \par \uc2 Washington gives $3.8bn in annual military assistance to Israel, its longtime ally. The latest transfers came from authorizations granted by Congress several years before the Israel-Gaza war began in October, but the \uc2 US government\uc2  has the authority to suspend an arms package any time before delivery.\par \par \uc2 Asked why the Biden administration did not pause the process after the Israeli drone attack on the \uc2 WCK\uc2  humanitarian aid convoy, the state department spokesperson did not comment, the Post wrote.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.48pm BST\par \par \uc2 During the 90-minute meeting last Tuesday, defense secretary \uc2 Lloyd Austin\uc2  pressed his Israeli counterpart, Yoav Gallant, to ensure that any Israeli military operation in Gaza\u8217\'20\'19s southern city of Rafah would prioritize the protection of civilians and secure the delivery of aid, according to a Pentagon official.\par \par \uc2 Speaking after his meeting with Gallant, which also included the chair of the Joint Chiefs of Staff, Gen CQ Brown, Austin said it was a moral and strategic imperative to protect Palestinian civilians, but there was nothing to suggest that he sought to condition future US military aid to Israel on an improvement of the humanitarian situation in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 The meeting at the Pentagon came a day after Israel\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister, \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 , abruptly canceled a high-level visit to Washington over {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/mar/25/un-gaza-ceasefire-vote"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the US abstention}}}\uc2  in a \uc2 UN\uc2  security council vote to call for an immediate ceasefire in the Palestinian territory.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.33pm BST\par \par \uc2 Austin expressed 'outrage' over Gaza aid convoy strike in call with Israel\par \par \uc2 Defense secretary \uc2 Lloyd Austin\uc2  spoke with his Israeli counterpart, Yoav Gallant, in a phone call yesterday in which he expressed his \u8220\'20\'1Coutrage\u8221\'20\'1D over the \uc2 Israel Defense Forces\uc2  (IDF) strike on Monday that killed seven aid workers trying to deliver much-needed food to Gaza.\par \par \uc2 A {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.defense.gov/News/Releases/Release/Article/3730091/secretary-of-defense-lloyd-j-austin-iiis-call-with-israeli-minister-of-defense/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 readout }}}\uc2  of the call, published last night by the Pentagon\u8217\'20\'19s press secretary, Maj Gen Patrick Ryder, states:\par \par \uc2 Secretary Austin expressed his outrage at the Israeli strike on a \uc2 World Central Kitchen\uc2  humanitarian aid convoy that killed seven aid workers, including an American citizen. Secretary Austin stressed the need to immediately take concrete steps to protect aid workers and Palestinian civilians in Gaza after repeated coordination failures with foreign aid groups.\par \par \uc2 Austin also urged Gallant to conduct a \u8220\'20\'1Cswift and transparent investigation, to share their conclusions publicly, and to hold those responsible to account\u8221\'20\'1D, it said.\par \par \uc2 Austin\u8217\'20\'19s comments on Wednesday marked a significant change in tone from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.defense.gov/News/Releases/Release/Article/3719161/readout-of-secretary-of-defense-lloyd-j-austin-iiis-meeting-with-israeli-minist/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 previous calls}}}\uc2  between the US and Israeli defense ministers, and comes after the pair {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/mar/23/israel-defence-chief-to-head-to-us-for-gaza-talks"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 held talks}}}\uc2  last week in Washington in what the Pentagon later described as a frank and direct discussion.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.19pm BST\par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , in a statement after the \uc2 Israel Defense Forces\uc2  (IDF) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/apr/02/gaza-aid-convoy-strike-what-happened-and-who-were-the-victims"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 drone attack }}}\uc2  on Monday that killed seven people working for the \uc2 World Central Kitchen\uc2  (\uc2 WCK\uc2 ) charity, said Israel was not doing enough to protect aid workers and called for a swift investigation into the strike.\par \par \uc2 In comments that were highly critical of Israel\u8217\'20\'19s actions in Gaza, Biden said:\par \par \uc2 This conflict has been one of the worst in recent memory in terms of how many aid workers have been killed.\par \par \uc2 He said he was \u8220\'20\'1Coutraged and heartbroken\u8221\'20\'1D by the aid workers\u8217\'20\'19 deaths and highlighted that this was not a standalone incident.\par \par \uc2 This is a major reason why distributing humanitarian aid in Gaza has been so difficult \u8211\'20\'13 because Israel has not done enough to protect aid workers trying to deliver desperately needed help to civilians \u8230\'20\'26 Israel has also not done enough to protect civilians.\par \par \uc2 Among those killed in the attack was Jacob Flickinger, a US-Canada dual citizen working for \uc2 WCK\uc2 , as well as three British nationals, an Australian, a Polish national and a Palestinian.\par \par \uc2 block-time published-time 2.08pm BST\par \par \uc2 Biden and Netanyahu to speak for first time since Gaza aid convoy attack\par \par \uc2 Good morning {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/us-politics/all"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US politics }}}\uc2  readers. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and Israel\u8217\'20\'19s prime minister, \uc2 Benjamin Netanyahu\uc2 , are expected to hold their first call since {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/apr/02/gaza-aid-convoy-strike-what-happened-and-who-were-the-victims"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Israeli airstrikes that killed seven aid workers}}}\uc2  in Gaza on Monday.\par \par \uc2 Biden, in a statement the following day, said he was \u8220\'20\'1Coutraged and heartbroken\u8221\'20\'1D by the deaths of the \uc2 World Central Kitchen\uc2  (WCK) humanitarian workers, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2024/apr/03/very-best-of-humanity-the-seven-aid-workers-killed-in-israeli-airstrike"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 who included}}}\uc2  an American-Canadian dual citizen, and is fully prepared to make his feelings clear to Netanyahu in their conversation today, CNN reported, citing a senior administration official. The president \u8220\'20\'1Cis pissed. The temperature regarding Bibi is very high,\u8221\'20\'1D an official told Axios.\par \par \uc2 Biden\u8217\'20\'19s criticism of Israel\u8217\'20\'19s actions in Gaza, where authorities say more than 33,000 Palestinians have been killed since 7 October, has grown over recent weeks and his {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/08/biden-netanyahu-israel-hot-mic"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 frustration with}}}\uc2  Netanyahu has become increasingly visible. The president has faced increasing pressure over his handling of the war, including from the first lady, Jill Biden, who {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nytimes.com/2024/04/03/us/politics/jill-biden-israel-hamas.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly pleaded }}}\uc2  with her husband to \u8220\'20\'1Cstop it, stop it now\u8221\'20\'1D. Meanwhile, defense secretary \uc2 Lloyd Austin{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.defense.gov/News/Releases/Release/Article/3730091/secretary-of-defense-lloyd-j-austin-iiis-call-with-israeli-minister-of-defense/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2  \u8220\'20\'1Cexpressed his outrage\u8221\'20\'1D }}}\uc2  at the aid convoy strike in a call on Wednesday with his counterpart, Israeli defense minister Yoav Gallant, according to the Pentagon.\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration, however, has continued to affirm its support of Israel in the wake of the Israeli drone strike, and Biden has shown no signs of trying to restrict or withhold US military aid to Israel. Just this week it was reported that the administration is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2024/apr/01/israel-hamas-war-airstrike-iran-consulate-gaza-syria-live-updates?page=with:block-660b16558f0831dce221b8d0#block-660b16558f0831dce221b8d0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 close to approving}}}\uc2  a major new weapons sale to Israel worth more than $18bn that will include up to 50 US-made F-15 fighter jets.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what else we\u8217\'20\'19re watching:\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 1.30pm ET. White House press secretary \uc2 Karine Jean-Pierre\uc2  will brief.\par \par \uc2 *\par \par \uc2 5pm. \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  will host a reception celebrating Greek Independence Day at the White House.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240404ek44001pm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
