\par\par \uc2 Technology\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18They are breaking the law\u8217\'20\'19: inside \uc2 Amazon\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s bid to stall a union drive\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 1,419 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 April 2024\par 10:01 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Retailer doing \u8216\'20\'18whatever it takes\u8217\'20\'19 to halt organizing at warehouse in Moreno Valley, California, workers say, as \uc2 Amazon\uc2  faces unfair labor practice charges\par \par \uc2 Facing an insurgent campaign which threatened to unleash a wave of unionization across its vast workforce, \uc2 Amazon\uc2  stands accused of reaching for dirty tricks.\par \par \uc2 Workers who tried to organize inside its warehouses claim the technology giant orchestrated an illegal counteroffensive, using scare tactics and spreading misconceptions.\par \par \uc2 Nearly two years have passed since workers in Staten Island, New York, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2022/apr/09/amazon-union-organization-staten-island"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voted to form its first US warehouse union}}}\uc2 . As the Amazon Labor Union took its battle nationwide, the company scrambled to ensure it did not suffer the same crushing blows.\par \par \uc2 The world\u8217\'20\'19s largest retailer is \u8220\'20\'1Cgoing to do whatever it takes\u8221\'20\'1D, Nannette Plascencia, who has worked for nine years at its ONT8 fulfillment center in Moreno Valley, California, said in an interview, \u8220\'20\'1Ceven knowing they are breaking the law\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Photographs shared with the Guardian reveal how \uc2 Amazon\uc2  pushed back against an organizing drive inside ONT8 with anti-union messaging. \u8220\'20\'1CUnions run their business with your money,\u8221\'20\'1D and deduct dues \u8220\'20\'1Cregularly\u8221\'20\'1D from paychecks, employees were warned on TV screens installed in the warehouse.\par \par \uc2 These tactics are at the heart of an operation by \uc2 Amazon\uc2  which is the subject of unfair labor practice charges, leaving battles to unionize across \uc2 Amazon\uc2  in limbo while both sides wait for months on actions and rulings by the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  (\uc2 NLRB\uc2 ), a federal agency.\par \par \uc2 Amazon\uc2  workers in Moreno Valley filed for a union vote in October 2022, only to pull the election petition after significant opposition from the company. Those who led the campaign allege managers violated labor laws to halt it in its tracks.\par \par \uc2 They cried foul to the \uc2 NLRB\uc2 , which last March consolidated their cases into a formal complaint seen by the Guardian. Managers at ONT8 \u8220\'20\'1Cdirected employees not to discuss the union on the work floor during work time\u8221\'20\'1D, but permitted discussion of other, non-work subjects, according to the complaint, which also alleges the company held \u8220\'20\'1C\u8216\'20\'18captive audience\u8217\'20\'19 meetings with workers.\par \par \uc2 The charges will be heard before an administrative law judge in August. \uc2 Amazon\uc2  denies all allegations of labor law violations at ONT8.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CA majority of the charges brought forth by the ALU have already been withdrawn or dismissed by the \uc2 NLRB\uc2 ,\u8221\'20\'1D Eileen Hards, an \uc2 Amazon\uc2  spokeswoman, said. \u8220\'20\'1CWe disagree with these allegations and look forward to showing that as the legal process continues.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 When workers at ONT8 first filed for a union election, \uc2 Amazon\uc2  quickly got to work, according to Plascencia, who described how operational managers from across the company descended on the warehouse for over a year.\par \par \uc2 Flyers were posted in the breakroom and employees summoned to meetings \u8211\'20\'13 referred to as \u8220\'20\'1Cprotect your privacy\u8221\'20\'1D meetings by \uc2 Amazon\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 where external anti-union consultants are frequently said to have assisted.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey scanned all our badges, took us in groups of 30, and there would be a TV monitor on, with slides \u8230\'20\'26 and a man in front we never saw before,\u8221\'20\'1D said Plascencia. \u8220\'20\'1CWe were told they were there to talk to us about union authorization cards and what we should know about them.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey would say, \u8216\'20\'18Be careful, because this is a government form you are signing,\u8217\'20\'19 and basically they would go on about how it\u8217\'20\'19s not good to unionize. They would tell us we would lose all our benefits and start all over again.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Plascencia said the operational managers regularly interrogated workers at ONT8, including herself, about unions and their union support.\par \par \uc2 It was possible, employees were warned, that collective bargaining by a union could leave them with \u8220\'20\'1Cless than you have now\u8221\'20\'1D. \u8220\'20\'1CWhatever the result, unions will charge you for representation,\u8221\'20\'1D according to one slide titled \u8220\'20\'1CGet the facts\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe truth is that with a union, there are no guarantees,\u8221\'20\'1D claimed one post on \uc2 Amazon\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s internal online board for employees.\par \par \uc2 The messaging instilled fear, anxiety and disrupted their union organizing efforts, Plascencia claimed \u8211\'20\'13 to the point where workers would berate her, and other organizers, over claims they would cause them to lose their pay and benefits.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CManagers would come up to us and say we\u8217\'20\'19re not allowed to talk about unions. I personally experienced this,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CA manager actually came up to me and some of my co-workers and said we\u8217\'20\'19re not allowed to talk about unions on the shop floor.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI pushed back and they said something as delicate as \u8216\'20\'18unions \u8230\'20\'26 could upset somebody, you can\u8217\'20\'19t talk about things like that\u8217\'20\'19.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Amazon\uc2  was particularly vehement in its warnings against authorization cards, which authorize unions to negotiate employment terms on a worker\u8217\'20\'19s behalf. \u8220\'20\'1CA third party may use it to call or text you or visit you at home,\u8221\'20\'1D it claimed on one flyer.\par \par \uc2 Such messaging made employees \u8220\'20\'1Cvery hesitant about signing\u8221\'20\'1D, Plascencia said. \u8220\'20\'1CThey believed that this was coming from the company they worked for, and that the company they worked for would not lie, so it has to be true.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe had to try to break it down to people that yes, the corporation will lie to you, because they don\u8217\'20\'19t care. It\u8217\'20\'19s all about them controlling and retaining their power, so they\u8217\'20\'19re going to say what they need to say to scare us.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Amazon\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s efforts upended union organizing efforts at ONT8, as concern over its claims became embedded among rank-and-file workers. \u8220\'20\'1CThat was really hard,\u8221\'20\'1D said Plascencia. \u8220\'20\'1CIt put a big dent in our movement.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The company does not want its workers to have the \u8220\'20\'1Cpower they deserve\u8221\'20\'1D in its warehouses, she claimed. \u8220\'20\'1CThey don\u8217\'20\'19t want us seated at the table with them, when deciding important things for us and our families.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey want to decide on their own without worker involvement, so they\u8217\'20\'19re going to do whatever it takes to make sure they accomplish that, even knowing they are breaking the law.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The events in Moreno Valley are not unique. Complaints over \uc2 Amazon\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s conduct during union elections that fell short at warehouses in Albany, New York, and Bessemer, Alabama, are still awaiting review at the \uc2 NLRB\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 At \uc2 Amazon\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s air hub in Kentucky, workers who have been {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2023/nov/29/amazon-union-busting-kentucky-air-hub"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 organizing }}}\uc2  for over a year have also filed unfair labor practice charges. \u8220\'20\'1CThe allegations in this complaint are without merit,\u8221\'20\'1D said Hards, the \uc2 Amazon\uc2  spokeswoman. \u8220\'20\'1COur solicitation policy is lawful, and we will continue to defend our position as the legal process continues.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Across the US, the wider fight to organize within \uc2 Amazon\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 the country\u8217\'20\'19s second-largest private employer \u8211\'20\'13 has lost momentum. Even at JFK8, in Staten Island \u8211\'20\'13 which remains its only US warehouse to unionize \u8211\'20\'13 the company has yet to have started bargaining with the union on a first contract.\par \par \uc2 Amazon\uc2  continues to deny the election results, despite the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  certifying the results after its objections were dismissed. \u8220\'20\'1CWe strongly disagree with the outcome of the election,\u8221\'20\'1D said Hards. The company is pushing for a review of a regional director\u8217\'20\'19s decision which dismissed its objections to the election.\par \par \uc2 The process is slow. In Moreno Valley, workers at ONT8 filed again for a union election last September, only to again pull the petition while waiting on the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  to review and respond to the unfair labor practice charges they have filed against \uc2 Amazon\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 As its conduct comes under scrutiny at the \uc2 NLRB\uc2  amid labor law violation proceedings, earlier this year \uc2 Amazon\uc2  argued the agency is unconstitutional, joining the likes of \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 SpaceX\uc2  and Trader Joe\u8217\'20\'19s to question the legality of its structure.\par \par \uc2 Amazon\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s leaders \u8220\'20\'1Cdon\u8217\'20\'19t care\u8221\'20\'1D about breaking the rules, Plascencia claimed. \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s not a big deal to them because it\u8217\'20\'19s not going to come around until years later.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The first campaign at ONT8 was in 2022, she noted, and the challenge over \uc2 Amazon\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s response is \u8220\'20\'1Cbarely coming around now\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Seth Goldstein, a labor attorney representing the Amazon Labor Union, said: \u8220\'20\'1CThe National Labor Relations Act\u8217\'20\'19s toothless enforcement and remedies allow employers to exploit endless due process rights, delaying bargaining for years, as seen at JFK8, where workers are left disillusioned or forced out, and union organizers are targeted and fired.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s outrageous that unions must spend hundreds of thousands of dollars in legal fees to force employers to bargain a contract. Fundamental labor reform is urgently needed to empower workers and hold employers accountable for their bargaining obligations.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240403ek43001e3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
