\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Rank-and-file union members back campaign to ditch Biden over Gaza\b0\par\par\uc2 Alice Herman in Madison, Wisconsin \par \uc2 1,097 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 April 2024\par 13:07 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Wisconsin coalition of low-wage workers and immigrants push back in anger against president\u8217\'20\'19s handling of Gaza war\par \par \uc2 In Wisconsin, a campaign by anti-war voters to abandon Joe Biden during the Democratic primary has found an ally in the labor movement \u8211\'20\'13 but not from its traditional leaders.\par \par \uc2 Instead, the Listen to Wisconsin campaign, an effort inspired by the Michigan campaign to reject Biden during the primary over his military support for Israel, has earned the support of rank-and-file trade unionists and a statewide coalition of low-wage workers and immigrants angry about the president\u8217\'20\'19s handling of the war.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIndividuals in labor have been very active,\u8221\'20\'1D said Janan Najeeb, a Wisconsin organizer spearheading the Listen to Wisconsin campaign.\par \par \uc2 Israel\u8217\'20\'19s war on Gaza has laid bare a divide within the labor movement \u8211\'20\'13 which has played out largely between union leaders in the \uc2 AFL-CIO\uc2 , the largest US labor federation, and the movement\u8217\'20\'19s rank and file, many of whom have vocally opposed the war and turned to their unions as an avenue for political action.\par \par \uc2 In the wake of \uc2 Hamas\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s bloody incursion into Israel and Israel\u8217\'20\'19s military response, which has so far killed more than 31,000 Palestinians, union members have drafted resolutions calling for a ceasefire and action by the Biden administration to pressure Israel to end the war and lift its siege on Gaza.\par \par \uc2 In Wisconsin, they\u8217\'20\'19re using the 2 April primary as a tool to increase the pressure on Biden. Workers affiliated with the grassroots group Wisconsin Labor for Palestine have allied with the Uninstructed campaign, helping organize a 30 March rally at the capitol and phone-banking to get out the vote. At a small Biden campaign event on 26 March at Madison Labor Temple \u8211\'20\'13 a meeting space for local unions \u8211\'20\'13 union members handed out leaflets encouraging workers to vote \u8220\'20\'1Cuninstructed\u8221\'20\'1D in the primary.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19ve gotten changes in wording \u8211\'20\'13 now they\u8217\'20\'19re willing to say \u8216\'20\'18ceasefire,\u8217\'20\'19\u8221\'20\'1D said Barret Elward, a member of the union representing faculty and staff at the \uc2 University of Wisconsin\uc2 , of the Biden administration. \u8220\'20\'1CBut I mean, it\u8217\'20\'19s just pablum, it\u8217\'20\'19s just messaging, it\u8217\'20\'19s just a PR thing. Nothing has changed on the ground.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Uninstructed campaign has also picked up the support of a powerful network of immigrant and low-wage workers in Wisconsin.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe should not be giving all of this money to this genocidal war,\u8221\'20\'1D said Christine Neumann-Ortiz, the executive director of Voces de la Frontera, whose advocacy arm has come out in support of the Listen to Wisconsin campaign.\par \par \uc2 For members of the Latino voter network, Neumann-Ortiz said, voting \u8220\'20\'1Cuninstructed\u8221\'20\'1D is also a way to voice their disapproval of Biden\u8217\'20\'19s rightward shift on immigration. This year, Biden has touted legislation to crack down on the southern border and limit the number of asylum seekers accepted on a daily basis there, and even used the pejorative \u8220\'20\'1Cillegal\u8221\'20\'1D in his State of the Union address.\par \par \uc2 Instead of adopting an increasingly rightwing rhetoric and policy toward immigration, Neumann-Ortiz said, Biden should use his executive authority to expand protections for undocumented immigrants and campaign on protections for immigrants that his administration has implemented \u8211\'20\'13 like a 2023 measure the \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2  quietly passed to protect non-citizen workers whose workplace rights have been violated from deportation.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CYou\u8217\'20\'19re not going to win those Trump supporters, but you are definitely eroding and alienating your own base,\u8221\'20\'1D said Neumann-Ortiz.\par \par \uc2 During the 2022 midterms, Voces de la Frontera Action poured its resources into mobilizing support for Democrats at the ballot box, with volunteer members directly contacting nearly 30,000 voters in their network and reaching 30,000 more through phone-banking and door-knocking, according to the organization. In 2020, Voces supported Biden\u8217\'20\'19s presidential run.\par \par \uc2 Now, the group has turned its efforts toward promoting the Uninstructed campaign with mailers, door-knocking and social media promotion.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s so important that in the months ahead, that he respond to the demands that are being made on Gaza, and for Latinos and immigrants, who he needs to reaffirm his commitment to,\u8221\'20\'1D said Neumann-Ortiz.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, nearly every major US union has refrained from endorsing the protest vote, and Wisconsin\u8217\'20\'19s affiliated unions have largely followed suit \u8211\'20\'13 underscoring the split within the labor movement over Israel-Palestine.\par \par \uc2 On 11 October, the \uc2 AFL-CIO\uc2  released a statement condemning the massacre of civilians on 7 October and voicing concerns about \u8220\'20\'1Cthe emerging humanitarian crisis that is affecting Palestinians in Gaza\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 The union called for a \u8220\'20\'1Cswift resolution\u8221\'20\'1D to the conflict, but refrained from calling for a \u8220\'20\'1Cceasefire\u8221\'20\'1D and made clear that labor councils within the federation were not to issue their own resolutions on the subject. When a council in Washington state passed a resolution on 18 October calling for a ceasefire and opposing \u8220\'20\'1Cunion involvement in the production or transportation of weapons destined for Israel\u8221\'20\'1D, the federation {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://inthesetimes.com/article/afl-cio-israel-palestine-ceasefire-resolution-gaza"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stepped in}}}\uc2  to overrule the resolution.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 United Auto Workers union\uc2  in December {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/01/uaw-ceasefire-gaza#:~:text=The%20United%20Auto%20Workers%2C%20one,have%20called%20for%20a%20ceasefire."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 called for a ceasefire}}}\uc2  and announced it would explore divesting from military manufacturing jobs, prompting other US unions to adopt stronger demands.\par \par \uc2 In Wisconsin, members of the South Central Federation of Labor \u8211\'20\'13 a federation of unions within the \uc2 AFL-CIO\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 introduced a ceasefire resolution in October that passed in late January, calling on the \uc2 AFL-CIO\uc2  to \u8220\'20\'1Cuse its influence to get the US to suspend further military aid to Israel that prolongs this conflict\u8221\'20\'1D. On 8 February, the \uc2 AFL-CIO\uc2  issued its own {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://aflcio.org/press/releases/afl-cio-statement-situation-israel-and-gaza"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 statement}}}\uc2  urging a ceasefire, stopping short of calling for reduced military assistance to Israel.\par \par \uc2 With few exceptions (the union representing graduate student workers at the \uc2 University of Wisconsin\uc2 , Madison, has endorsed the Uninstructed campaign), traditional unions in Wisconsin, which have formed a bastion of support for Democrats, have largely stayed out of the fray.\par \par \uc2 Jacob Flom, the president of the union representing workers at the Milwaukee Public Museum, who sits on the board of the Milwaukee Area Labor Council and is a vocal opponent of Israel\u8217\'20\'19s war in Gaza, said the Wisconsin Labor for Palestine coalition aims to push Wisconsin\u8217\'20\'19s unions to take a stronger stand in defense of Palestinian workers.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs trade unionists, we feel like it is our obligation to stand in solidarity with them and to pressure our electeds and our unions to do more and to do better to stop the US support for the genocide in Gaza,\u8221\'20\'1D said Flom.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240401ek41000xh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
