\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Huge breakthrough\u8217\'20\'19 in \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  union talks \u8211\'20\'13 which other US firms will follow?\b0\par\par\uc2 Steven Greenhouse \par \uc2 1,264 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 March 2024\par 11:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Coffee chain appears willing to come to the table, which could mean good news for Trader Joe\u8217\'20\'19s, Amazon and REI workers\par \par \uc2 For more than two years \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  has fought fiercely against unionization. Now the company appears willing to come to the bargaining table.\par \par \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  and its union made a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2024/feb/27/starbucks-workers-union-bargaining"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 surprise joint announcement}}}\uc2  in late February: they had agreed to seek \u8220\'20\'1Ca constructive path forward\u8221\'20\'1D on \u8220\'20\'1Cthe future of organizing and collective bargaining\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, the \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  union said it would resume in-person bargaining with the company in late April, with the aim of achieving a \u8220\'20\'1Cfoundational framework agreement\u8221\'20\'1D. It said there would be \u8220\'20\'1Cbargaining delegates representing more than 400\u8221\'20\'1D unionized \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  stores.\par \par \uc2 The news \u8211\'20\'13 while cautiously received \u8211\'20\'13 is not just much-needed cheer for workers at the coffee chain, but for others at Amazon, Trader Joe\u8217\'20\'19s and the outdoor sports retailer REI, whose own efforts to reach a first contract {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://newrepublic.com/article/177557/trader-joes-union-busting-bargaining-table-first-contract"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have barely inched forward}}}\uc2  in the last 18 months.\par \par \uc2 If \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  \u8211\'20\'13 the company that labor experts say has been the most aggressive union-buster in decades \u8211\'20\'13 has signaled that it might finally be ready to reach a union, who would be next?\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s a huge breakthrough,\u8221\'20\'1D said Claire Chang, a sales associate at the REI store in Soho in Manhattan, which, in March 2022, became the first REI store in the US to unionize. \u8220\'20\'1CAfter two years of trying to win a contract, the \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  workers finally got this huge multibillion corporation to meet them at the bargaining table, after the company was so adamant, it gives us some hope.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Chang and many other REI workers have criticized their company for the glacial pace of contract talks. The \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  developments, Chang said, \u8220\'20\'1Creignited the flame for us that we just have to keep going\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 John Logan, a professor of labor studies at \uc2 San Francisco State University\uc2 , said he remained skeptical about the \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  announcement and whether the coffee chain will stop its union-busting activities and reach a first contract any time soon. The \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  (\uc2 NLRB\uc2 ) has filed 128 complaints against \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 , accusing it of more than 1,000 violations of the law, among them, firing dozens of baristas in retaliation for supporting the union. \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  denies any wrongdoing.\par \par \uc2 Logan said that if \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  reaches a good contract with its union, Starbucks Workers United, \u8220\'20\'1Cthat could turn out to be one of the greatest union success stories of the last several decades. It\u8217\'20\'19s almost akin to Amazon or Tesla deciding they\u8217\'20\'19re not going to union-bust any more.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIf \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  does reach an agreement,\u8221\'20\'1D Logan added, \u8220\'20\'1Cit would act as an inspiration for other workers.\par \par \uc2 Michelle Eisen, a barista and spokesperson for the \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  union, voiced optimism about the \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 -union announcement. \u8220\'20\'1CWe\u8217\'20\'19re excited to forge a new path forward with \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  based on mutual respect,\u8221\'20\'1D she said in an email. \u8220\'20\'1CWe hope our shared commitment to work collaboratively inspires other companies to recognize that respecting worker voice is good for business.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 If Starbuck workers are able to get a contract, that changes the whole narrative about what\u8217\'20\'19s possible\par \par \uc2 Sarah Beth Ryther\par \par \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  made its peace offering to its union after its union-busting and the many \uc2 NLRB\uc2  charges against it hurt its reputation, after its stock price took a beating, after the union disrupted dozens of stores with a wave of strikes, and after many people began calling for a nationwide boycott. \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  officials have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://stories.starbucks.com/press/2024/message-from-sara-starbucks-and-workers-united-agree-on-path-forward/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 indicated they are ready}}}\uc2  to turn the page with the union.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s incredibly significant that \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  has finally agreed to a framework for working with the union,\u8221\'20\'1D said Richard Bensinger, who was an adviser to the \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  union when it won its first unionization elections in late 2021 and early 2022 despite the company\u8217\'20\'19s aggressive anti-union efforts. \u8220\'20\'1CThis will send a message to other workers that organizing can succeed.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Seth Goldstein is a lawyer for the Amazon Labor Union, which made history by winning the first union election at an Amazon warehouse in the United States \u8211\'20\'13 the union won 2,654 votes to 2,131 in April 2022 at Amazon\u8217\'20\'19s JFK8 warehouse on Staten Island. Goldstein said \u8220\'20\'1Cit would be wonderful\u8221\'20\'1D if \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  stops fighting its union and agrees to a first contract.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt would have a positive effect for Amazon workers because they would see that unionization works,\u8221\'20\'1D he said. \u8220\'20\'1CBut I don\u8217\'20\'19t know if it will change Amazon\u8217\'20\'19s union-busting policies.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Goldstein said that to change Amazon\u8217\'20\'19s anti-union stance, \u8220\'20\'1Cthere will have to be extreme pressure on Amazon from all sectors, including the government\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 In light of \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 announcement, it looks as if two Seattle-area corporate giants, \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  and \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 , are making peace with labor, while two other prominent Seattle-area companies, Amazon and REI, remain opposed to unionization. \uc2 Elizabeth Ford\uc2 , who runs the workers\u8217\'20\'19 rights clinic at the Seattle University School of Law, said that in Seattle, the talk about the \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  announcement was being eclipsed by something else: \u8220\'20\'1CThe thing that is consuming people\u8217\'20\'19s attention a little more is that \uc2 SpaceX\uc2 , \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  and Amazon are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/mar/10/starbucks-trader-joes-spacex-challenge-labor-board"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 challenging the constitutionality}}}\uc2  of the \uc2 NLRB\uc2 .\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Ford agreed with Goldstein, saying: \u8220\'20\'1CI don\u8217\'20\'19t think it [the \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  announcement] is going to influence Amazon.\u8221\'20\'1D She said it could influence REI, however. \u8220\'20\'1CWill REI recognize that it can forestall damage to its brand and perhaps even enhance its brand by making the negotiations with its workers as frictionless as possible?\u8221\'20\'1D Ford said. She added that REI\u8217\'20\'19s opposition to its union undercuts its efforts to project a \u8220\'20\'1Cprogressive corporate identity\u8221\'20\'1D.\par \par \uc2 Adam Obernauer, organizing director for the Retail, Wholesale and Department Store Union, which has unionized several REI stores, said the \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  developments raise a question. \u8220\'20\'1CFor progressive employers like REI and Trader Joe\u8217\'20\'19s that are fighting the law over and over and being repeatedly accused of breaking the law, is it sustainable for them to keep fighting day after day and spending all this money battling the union?\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Obernauer said a cooperative like REI \u8220\'20\'1Cneeds to understand that its membership base believes in workers\u8217\'20\'19 rights, believes in environmental rights, believes in a better future. You can\u8217\'20\'19t try to make money through the progressive positions you take and at the same time ignore things when it comes to the rights of your own workers.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Sarah Beth Ryther, who spearheaded the 55-to-5 unionization win at a Trader Joe\u8217\'20\'19s store in Minneapolis, faults her company for the snail-like pace of negotiations and says the \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  announcement gives her hope. \u8220\'20\'1CFrom our perspective, it\u8217\'20\'19s been really cool to see all the power that the \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  union has brought to bear through all their strikes and everything.,\u8221\'20\'1D she said. \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19ve been incredibly inspiring, and I really hope for labor\u8217\'20\'19s sake they are able to make headway.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIt\u8217\'20\'19s the kind of thing where I will believe it when it happens, and if it does happen, that would be absolutely amazing,\u8221\'20\'1D she continued. \u8220\'20\'1CIt would be a huge deal if any of the newly unionized workers get a contract. Right now, it feels like we\u8217\'20\'19re in uncharted territory, with these contract talks lasting forever.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Ryther acknowledged that Starbucks Workers United, with about 400 stores unionized, has more leverage than the Trader Joe\u8217\'20\'19s union, which has organized only four stores. \u8220\'20\'1CIf \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  workers are able to get a contract, that changes the whole narrative about what\u8217\'20\'19s possible,\u8221\'20\'1D she said.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240322ek3m0018m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
