\par\par \uc2 US news\par \b \uc2 Minneapolis drivers protested wages \u8211\'20\'13 and won. \uc2 Lyft\uc2  and \uc2 Uber\uc2  are choosing to leave the city rather than pay up\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 821 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 March 2024\par 11:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Groups of drivers backed a bill setting minimum pay, but the two tech companies say it\u8217\'20\'19d make riders\u8217\'20\'19 fees unsustainable\par \par \uc2 Uber\uc2  and \uc2 Lyft\uc2  claim they will cease operating in the Minneapolis area in protest of a minimum pay ordinance that the city council voted to approve last week.\par \par \uc2 The bill, to go into effect on 1 May, would establish a minimum pay of $1.40 per mile and $0.51 cents per minute for rideshare drivers, with a $5 per ride minimum. The city council voted to override the mayor\u8217\'20\'19s veto of the ordinance, prompting \uc2 Uber\uc2  and \uc2 Lyft\uc2  to threaten to leave the region in response.\par \par \uc2 Minneapolis would be the only city in the US without \uc2 Uber\uc2  and \uc2 Lyft\uc2  services if the rideshare companies uphold their threat to cease operations on 1 May.\par \par \uc2 The legislation was backed by groups of rideshare drivers over low pay and high costs amid reports their {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://viewfromthewing.com/ubers-downward-spiral-how-driver-pay-has-worsened-as-the-company-stopped-innovating/https://viewfromthewing.com/ubers-downward-spiral-how-driver-pay-has-worsened-as-the-company-stopped-innovating/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pay has been declining}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Eid Ali, a rideshare driver for nine years and president of the Minnesota \uc2 Uber\uc2  and Lyft Drivers Association dismissed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/lyft-uber-minneapolis-ridehailing-apps-0a51b37c37202f61bb4943089e5a288d"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 claims}}}\uc2  from \uc2 Uber\uc2  and \uc2 Lyft\uc2  that the minimum pay is too high and would make passengers\u8217\'20\'19 fees unsustainable.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CI refuse to believe a $7.3bn company [ {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fool.com/investing/2024/03/13/lyft-stock-is-soaring-should-you-buy-below-20/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lyft}}}\uc2  ] cannot pay their workers minimum wage in our city. That is so difficult for me to swallow,\u8221\'20\'1D said Ali. \u8220\'20\'1CEvery worker has the right to be paid a living wage.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Ali said if \uc2 Uber\uc2  and \uc2 Lyft\uc2  ultimately leave, they would only be taking software with them and claimed other startups, companies and taxi cab companies have already expressed interest in trying to replace them.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe drivers are here. Their cars are here. They\u8217\'20\'19re not leaving,\u8221\'20\'1D said Ali. \u8220\'20\'1CWhy I think they\u8217\'20\'19re doing this is if they let the drivers here get what they want in this small market, it will have a bigger effect on their bigger, more lucrative markets. So they have to stop this. That is what their fight is based on. It\u8217\'20\'19s not about the minimum wage, I believe it\u8217\'20\'19s about how it will impact their bigger markets.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Farhan Badel has worked as a driver for \uc2 Uber\uc2  and \uc2 Lyft\uc2  since 2018 said he enjoys working as a rideshare driver, but that he felt their role in society was severely undervalued.\par \par \uc2 He claimed that rideshare driver compensation in the area has declined in recent years, noting that the takeaway pay for driving a common route from the airport to the Mayo Clinic has dropped significantly. Badel argued he has been working longer hours and getting paid less than he did years ago and that the rideshare apps have been exploiting rideshare drivers who are predominantly from immigrant communities in the Minneapolis area.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1C\uc2 Uber\uc2  and \uc2 Lyft\uc2 , it seems they want to turn this into riders versus drivers, but the reality is a lot of the riders understand that they are overpaying, they\u8217\'20\'19re getting overcharged, while we\u8217\'20\'19re getting underpaid. That\u8217\'20\'19s what our struggle is,\u8221\'20\'1D said Badel. \u8220\'20\'1CAll we\u8217\'20\'19re asking for is fair compensation. They decide what to charge the riders, we don\u8217\'20\'19t have control over what they charge the riders. All we\u8217\'20\'19re asking for is a fair wage. If they\u8217\'20\'19re charging the rider $90 and only giving us $20, that is what they\u8217\'20\'19re fighting against.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Republicans in the Minnesota legislature have already {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.kare11.com/article/news/local/lawmakers-to-introduce-bill-in-an-attempt-to-keep-uber-lyft-in-minneapolis/89-6975176c-adf0-4607-8ba2-320bd3807c3f"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 introduced }}}\uc2  a bill to pre-empt the regulations in Minneapolis, aimed at keeping \uc2 Uber\uc2  and \uc2 Lyft\uc2  in the region.\par \par \uc2 Josh Gold, senior director of public affairs at \uc2 Uber\uc2 , said: \u8220\'20\'1CWe are disappointed the council chose to ignore the data and kick \uc2 Uber\uc2  out of the Twin Cities, putting 10,000 people out of work and leaving many stranded. But we know that by working together with all stakeholders \u8211\'20\'13 drivers, riders and state leaders \u8211\'20\'13 we can achieve comprehensive statewide legislation that guarantees drivers a fair minimum wage, protects their independence and keeps rideshare affordable.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 A spokesperson for \uc2 Lyft\uc2  added they are also supporting a state-level pre-emption.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThis deeply-flawed bill has been jammed through despite major concerns being raised by the community,\u8221\'20\'1D said the spokesperson in an email. \u8220\'20\'1CWe support a minimum earning standard for drivers, which is why we recently {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.lyft.com/blog/posts/early-2024-driver-release"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  a commitment where drivers will always make at least 70% of the weekly rider fares after external fees. However, this ordinance would make rides unaffordable for the majority of Minneapolis residents. The drastic drop in rides means the thousands of drivers who rely on \uc2 Lyft\uc2  for earnings would ultimately make less, creating an unsustainable situation for our customers.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Rideshare corporations have been at loggerheads with regulators across the US and abroad. There have been several instances where \uc2 Uber\uc2  and \uc2 Lyft\uc2  have threatened to leave jurisdictions over regulations often aimed at resolving scrutiny over low pay and working conditions of drivers.\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240320ek3k001gw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
