\par\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 US Volkswagen workers file for union election to join \uc2 United Auto Workers\b0\par\par\uc2 Michael Sainato \par \uc2 572 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 March 2024\par 17:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Guardian\par \uc2 GRDN\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024.  The Guardian.  All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Tennessee plant is currently the only \uc2 Volkswagen\uc2  plant globally without union representation, according to the \uc2 UAW\par \par \uc2 Volkswagen\uc2  workers in Chattanooga, Tennessee, filed a petition to join the \uc2 United Auto Workers (UAW)\uc2  on Monday after a supermajority of workers at the plant signed union authorization cards.\par \par \uc2 It is the first union election filing for the union since it launched a massive campaign aimed at organizing 150,000 workers at non-unionized auto plants in the US in the wake of securing historic gains in their contracts at the big three US automakers, Ford, \uc2 General Motors\uc2  and \uc2 Stellantis\uc2 , last year.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CToday, we are one step closer to making a good job at \uc2 Volkswagen\uc2  into a great career,\u8221\'20\'1D said Isaac Meadows, a production team member in assembly at the \uc2 Volkswagen\uc2  plant, in a press release on the union election filing. \u8220\'20\'1CRight now, we miss time with our families because so much of our paid-time-off is burned up during the summer and winter shutdowns. We shouldn\u8217\'20\'19t have to choose between our family and our job. By winning our union and a real voice at \uc2 Volkswagen\uc2 , we can negotiate for more time with our families.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The Chattanooga plant is currently the only \uc2 Volkswagen\uc2  plant globally without union representation, according to the \uc2 UAW\uc2  which released a video announcing the union election filing at the plant. The \uc2 UAW\uc2  has filed unfair labor practice charges against \uc2 Volkswagen\uc2  amid the union organizing campaign over claims of union busting, which the company has denied.\par \par \uc2 In early February 2024, the union {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cbtnews.com/uaw-says-it-has-secured-majority-support-in-non-union-volkswagen-factory/#:~:text=This%20is%20the%20first%20time,a%20non%2Dunion%20auto%20plant.&text=On%20February%206%2C%20a%20news,join%20the%20Detroit%2Dbased%20union."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  more than 50% of the 4,000 workers in the bargaining unit had signed union authorization cards.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UAW\uc2  has also announced organizing milestones at the \uc2 Mercedes-Benz\uc2  plant in Alabama, reaching a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://uaw.org/we-are-the-majority-workers-at-mercedes-benzs-largest-us-plant-announce-majority-support-for-movement-to-join-uaw/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 50% majority }}}\uc2  of union support last month, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://thehill.com/business/4440930-hyundai-workers-alabama-uaw/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 30% }}}\uc2  support at a Hyundai plant in Alabama, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://uaw.org/we-keep-toyota-running-workers-at-critical-toyota-plant-launch-campaign-to-join-the-uaw/#:~:text=TROY%2C%20Mo.,campaign%20to%20win%20their%20union."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 30%}}}\uc2  at a \uc2 Toyota\uc2  plant in Missouri. The union announced plans in February 2024 to devote {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://uaw-newsroom.prgloo.com/press-release/uaw-announces-usd-40-million-commitment-to-organizing-auto-and-battery-workers-over-next-two-years"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $40m }}}\uc2  toward organizing auto and battery workers over the next two years.\par \par \uc2 Under previous leadership at the \uc2 UAW\uc2 , the union came close to winning elections in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/dec/07/uaw-volkswagen-chattanooga-tennessee"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2014 and 2019}}}\uc2  at the plant but came up short after a surge of anti-union organizations and Republican elected officials aggressively opposed the efforts. Similar efforts have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonexaminer.com/opinion/523800/sen-bob-corker-warns-nlrb-ruling-on-uaw-vw-election-could-muzzle-lawmakers/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 already begun}}}\uc2  during the current campaign at the plant.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs it stands, we don\u8217\'20\'19t really have a whole lot of freedom at work, we don\u8217\'20\'19t have a whole lot of say on how things are done and how things go on,\u8221\'20\'1D Zach Costello, a worker at the \uc2 Volkswagen\uc2  plant in Chattanooga since 2017, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2024/jan/11/volkswagen-automakers-union-uaw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told }}}\uc2  the Guardian in January. \u8220\'20\'1COur lives are at work and if our lives spend so much time at work and we have no say, then how free are you? If people truly want a democratic life, regardless of how good their job is, worker organization is very important.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 In response to the union election petition, a spokesperson for \uc2 Volkswagen\uc2  said in an email, \u8220\'20\'1CWe respect our workers\u8217\'20\'19 right to a democratic process and to determine who should represent their interests. We will fully support an \uc2 NLRB\uc2  vote so every team member has a chance to vote in privacy in this important decision. The election timeline will be determined by the \uc2 NLRB\uc2 . \uc2 Volkswagen\uc2  is proud of our working environment in Chattanooga that provides some of the best paying jobs in the area.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Document GRDN000020240318ek3i0020j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw127\pich40\picscaley313\picscalex313\picwgoal610\pichgoal192
